hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Narration of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 1. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, by reading upon him while you listened; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Abu Bakr stood among us delivering a sermon and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year and said: Nothing better than well-being after certainty has been distributed among people. Verily, truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise, and verily, lying and wickedness are in the Fire."
"2","2. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, with my reading upon him, on the western side of Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us; Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada narrating from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman that Umar said: Abu Bakr addressed us as a preacher and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year and said: Verily, nothing better than well-being after certainty has been distributed among people. Verily, truthfulness and righteousness are in Paradise; verily, lying and wickedness are in the Fire. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Bahz ibn Asad, from Salim ibn Hayyan. The Imam Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni the Hafiz said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari al-Basri narrated it, and there was disagreement from him: Qatada narrated it from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umar, from Abu Bakr. Salim ibn Hayyan narrated it likewise from Qatada. And there was disagreement from Salim: it was said from him, from Qatada, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, from Abu Bakr. And Abu al-Tayyah narrated it from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Bakr, without mentioning Umar or Ibn Abbas. The statement of Salim ibn Hayyan in it is most correct, because he is trustworthy, and he added Umar in it, and his addition is accepted. I say: I do not know whether Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari heard from Umar ibn al-Khattab or not, and al-Daraqutni did not mention anything about that."
"3","3. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us; Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar came upon Abu Bakr while he was stretching his tongue, and said: What are you doing, O successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: This has brought me to ruinous places. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing of the body except that it complains of the sharpness of the tongue. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, and he mentioned the narration of Abd al-Samad from al-Darawardi. He said: There was an error in it against al-Darawardi. He said: Hisham ibn Sad and Muhammad ibn Ajlan and others narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father: that Umar entered upon Abu Bakr, with wording like that of al-Darawardi, but they did not mention the raised chain to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), neither as mursal nor as musnad."
"4","4. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me; al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, from Abu Labid, who said: A man of al-Asd from Tahiya came out, called Bayrah ibn Asad, emigrating to Madina, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had died before that. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab saw Bayrah wandering in the streets of Madina and found him unfamiliar, and said: From whom are you? He said: I am a man from the people of Oman. So he took his hand and went with him to Abu Bakr, and said: O Abu Bakr, this is from the land whose people, from the people of Oman, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention. Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a land whose side is washed by the sea, in it is a tribe of Arabs: if my messenger came to them, they would not shoot him with an arrow nor a stone."
"5","5. The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us; Abd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Abu Labid, who said: A man from Tahiya came out emigrating, called Yabrah ibn Asad, and arrived in Madina days after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar ibn al-Khattab saw him and knew he was a stranger, and said to him: From where are you? He said: From the people of Oman? He said: Yes. So he took his hand and brought him to Abu Bakr, and said: This is from the land about which I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a land called Oman, whose side is washed by the sea, in it is a tribe of Arabs: if my messenger came to them, they would not shoot him with an arrow nor a stone. The name of Abu Labid is Limaza ibn Zabbar. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun in the Musnad of Umar. Ahmad said: It is only 'you heard,' meaning Abu Bakr, while Yazid said 'I heard' in the nominative, meaning Umar."
"6","Narration of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 6. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwa informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: And Amr informed me, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, that Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by Uthman while he was sitting in the mosque and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting. So he entered upon Abu Bakr and complained of that to him, saying: I passed by Uthman and greeted him, but he did not return it to me. He said: Where is he? He said: He is sitting in the mosque. He said: So we went to him, and Abu Bakr said to him: What prevented you from returning the greeting of your brother when he greeted you? He said: By Allah, I did not feel that he greeted; he passed by me while I was talking to myself, so I did not feel that he greeted. Abu Bakr said to him: What were you saying to yourself? He said: Satan had isolated me and began casting things into my mind that I would not love to have spoken, even if I had all that is on earth. I said to myself when Satan cast that into my mind: I wish I had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what saves us from this talk that Satan casts into our minds. Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I had complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I asked him who saves us from this talk that Satan casts into our minds. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What saves you from that is that you say what I commanded my uncle with at death, but he did not do it. Imam Ahmad narrated it in abridged form from Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad and Said ibn Salama, the freedman of Abu al-Husam, both from Amr ibn Abi Amr. The name of Abu al-Huwayrith is Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiya. Al-Daraqutni said: The hearing of Muhammad ibn Jubayr from Uthman is not established, so this hadith of his is mursal. Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa narrated it with a connected chain from Uthman: he narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman, from Abu Bakr. Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa is alone in it from Ibn Aqil, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa except Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Zayd. It is a connected, good chain, except that Ibn Aqil is not strong. Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala narrated it from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Uthman, from Abu Bakr. Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Dibaji narrated it to us in Basra; Sayyar ibn al-Hasan al-Tustari narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala narrated to us with that. Up to here from al-Daraqutni. I say: Ibn Wahb narrated from Haywa ibn Shurayh, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, who informed him that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab while standing on the pulpit: Learn your lineages and join your ties of kinship. If his hearing from Umar is sound, then his hearing from Uthman is not far-fetched, and Allah knows best."
"7","Narration of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him. 7. The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi al-Isbahani informed us, with my reading upon him, in it, I said to him: Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Baqqal informed us; Abu Ahmad Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, by reading upon him, he said: Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Mani ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr al-Asadi narrated to us; Misar narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, from Ali ibn Rabia, from Asma ibn al-Hakam, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed of it; but when someone else narrated to me from him, I made him swear an oath, and when he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no servant who commits a sin, then stands and performs ablution well, then prays and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that Allah forgives him."
"8","8. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi also informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in al-Harbiyya, it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki narrated to us; Misar and Sufyan informed us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, from Ali ibn Rabia al-Walibi, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed of it; and when someone else narrated to me from him, I made him swear an oath, and when he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no man who commits a sin and performs ablution and performs it well, Misar said: and prays, and Sufyan said: then prays two rakats and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him."
"9","9. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; al-Qawariri informed us; Ghundar narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, he said: I heard Uthman ibn al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Ali ibn Rabia, from a man of Banu Fazara called Asma, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: Whenever I heard something from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me with. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no Muslim servant, Shuba said: I think he said, who commits a sin, then performs ablution, then prays two rakats, then seeks Allah's forgiveness for that sin, except that He forgives him. Shuba said: And he recited one of these two verses: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it, and: Those who, when they commit immorality or wrong themselves."
"10","10. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath Abu Bahr informed us; Abu Awana informed us, he said: Ali said: I was a man who, when I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me; and when one of his Companions narrated to me, I made him swear an oath, and when he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution and performs it well, then stands and prays, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him. Then he recited: Those who, when they commit immorality or wrong themselves."
"11","11. Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, with my reading upon him, in it, I said to him: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Fudayli informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Ismail, he is Ibn Mudar ibn Ismail al-Dabbi, informed us; Abu Said al-Khalil ibn Ahmad ibn al-Shajari informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us; Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us; Abu Awana narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, from Ali ibn Rabia, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, who said: I heard Ali say: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed to benefit me; but when a man among his Companions narrated to me, I made him swear an oath, and when he swore to me, I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no believing man who commits a sin, then stands and purifies himself and performs purification well, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that Allah forgives him. Then he recited this verse: Those who, when they commit immorality or wrong themselves, to the end of the verse. Sharik, Qays ibn al-Rabi, Israil, and al-Hasan ibn Umara also narrated it, and they agreed in its chain as Misar, Sufyan, Shuba, and Abu Awana narrated it, except that Shuba says: from Asma or Abu Asma. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement in this hadith and said: The best and soundest in chain is what al-Thawri and Misar and those who followed them narrated from Uthman ibn al-Mughira. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Abu Awana. Al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasai narrated it from Qutayba, from Abu Awana, and al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan hadith, we know it only from this route from Uthman. Al-Nasai narrated it from Bundar, from Yahya, from Sufyan; and from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Jafar ibn Awn, from Misar. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Nasr ibn Ali, from Waki, from Misar and Sufyan, from Uthman. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Khalifa al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Musaddad, from Abu Awana."
"12","Narration of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 12. Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Isbahani informed us, by reading while we listened, in Isfahan, it was said to him: Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed you, by reading upon her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us; Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us; Ulwan ibn Dawud al-Bajali narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, who said: I entered upon Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, visiting him in the illness in which he died. I greeted him and asked him: How have you woken? He sat upright. I said: By Allah's praise you have woken recovered. He said: I am, as you see, in pain, and you have given me occupation along with my pain. I made for you a covenant after me, and I chose for you the best of you in my view, yet each of you has swelled his nose for it, hoping the matter would be his. I saw the world approaching, though it has not yet approached, and it is coming. You will furnish your houses with curtains of silk and cushions of brocade, and you will find painful the beds of soft Adhri wool, as if one of you were upon the thorns of sadan. By Allah, for one of you to be brought forward and his neck struck without legal punishment is better for him than to swim in the flood of the world. Then he said: I grieve over nothing except three things I did, which I wish I had not done; three things I did not do, which I wish I had done; and three things I wish I had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about. As for the three I wish I had not done: I wish I had not uncovered the house of Fatima, or left it, and had closed war upon myself; I wish that on the day of the Saqifa of Banu Saida I had cast the matter upon the neck of one of the two men, Abu Ubayda or Umar, so he would be the Commander of the Faithful and I a minister; and I wish that when I directed Khalid ibn al-Walid to the people of apostasy, I had stayed at Dhu al-Qassa: if the Muslims triumphed, they triumphed, otherwise I would have been a support and reinforcement. As for those I wish I had done: I wish that on the day al-Ashath was brought to me as a captive I had struck his neck, for it seems to me no evil occurs except he flies to it; I wish that on the day al-Fujaa al-Sulami was brought to me I had not burned him, but killed him swiftly or released him safely; and I wish that when I directed Khalid ibn al-Walid to Syria, I had directed Umar to Iraq, so I would have extended my hands, my right and my left, in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic. As for the three I wish I had asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about: I wish I had asked him in whom this authority lies, so its people would not be disputed; I wish I had asked him whether the Ansar have any share in this matter; and I wish I had asked him about the paternal aunt and the brother's daughter, for in my mind concerning them is a need. The Imam Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni mentioned this narration and said: Al-Layth ibn Sad opposed him, narrating it from Ulwan, from Salih ibn Kaysan with this chain, except that he did not mention Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman between Ulwan and Salih. It resembles that Said ibn Ufayr preserved it from Ulwan, for he added a man in it, and Said ibn Ufayr was among the preserving trustworthy. I say: This is a hasan hadith from Abu Bakr, except that there is nothing in it of the speech of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bukhari narrated in his book more than one saying of the Companions, among them what Tariq narrated."
"13","Narration of Abd Allah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 13. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi, with my reading upon him also, informed us. I said to each of them: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abd Allah, who said: I was in the mosque praying when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, with him Abu Bakr and Umar. I had begun Surat al-Nisa and recited it. When I finished, I sat and began with praise of Allah, mighty and majestic, and blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I supplicated for myself. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask, you will be given; ask, you will be given. Then he said: Whoever loves to recite the Quran fresh, let him recite it as Ibn Umm Abd recites. He said: I returned to my house, and Abu Bakr came to me and said: Do you remember anything of what you were supplicating? I said: Yes. O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that does not end, and companionship of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest Garden of Eternity. Umar came to Abd Allah to give him glad tidings, but found Abu Bakr coming out, having preceded him. He said: If you did, you are indeed foremost in good. Imam Ahmad narrated in his Musnad from Yahya ibn Adam the musnad from him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan. Ibn Maja narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, both from Yahya ibn Adam. The narration of al-Khallal is abridged, and al-Tirmidhi said: A sahih hadith."
"14","14. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani also informed us, with my reading upon him, in Isfahan, I said to him: Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed you, by reading upon her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us; al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, who said: A man came to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I have come to you from a man who dictates the codices from memory. Umar was alarmed and said: Woe to you, look at what you say, and he grew angry. He said: I have come to you only with truth. He said: Who is he? He said: Abd Allah ibn Masud. He said: I know no one more entitled to that than him. I shall tell you about Abd Allah: We spent an evening in the house of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning some need of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then we went out, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) between me and Abu Bakr. When we reached the mosque, there was a man reciting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood listening to him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have delayed the night prayer. He nudged me with his hand: Be silent. He said: He recited, bowed, prostrated, and sat supplicating and seeking forgiveness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask, you will be given. Then he said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran moist as it was revealed, let him recite the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd. I and my companion knew it was Abd Allah. In the morning I went early to him to give him glad tidings, but he said: Abu Bakr preceded you with it. I never raced him to any good except he preceded me to it. Zaida narrated it from al-Amash, from Ibrahim. Khaythama ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated it from Qays ibn Marwan, who said: A man came to Umar, with wording like the hadith of Alqama."
"15","Abd Allah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 15. Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Isfahan, it was said to him: Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed you, by reading upon her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ruwasi narrated to us; Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Umayr, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Ali and al-Abbas disputed to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them, concerning the inheritance of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I would not move it from the place in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it."
"16","16. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us; Abu Awana narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Umayr, the freedman of al-Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken and Abu Bakr was made successor, al-Abbas disputed with Ali concerning things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, to Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said: A thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left and did not move, I shall not move. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Yahya ibn Hammad. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the hadith of Aisha: that Fatima bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr after the death of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to apportion for her. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad only eats from this wealth. By Allah, I shall not change anything of the charity of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the state it was upon in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I shall act in it as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted. It resembles that this is the meaning of the hadith of Ibn Abbas, and Allah knows best."
"17","17. Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Sufi informed us in Herat that Abu al-Qasim Tamim ibn Abi Said ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them, by reading upon him: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu Said Muhammad ibn Thawr al-Abbas al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us; Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris ibn Iyas al-Sami al-Sarakhsi informed us; Suwayd, he is Ibn Said, narrated to us; Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us from his father, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clientage belongs to the one who frees. I do not know that I wrote it except from the hadith of Suwayd ibn Said; some scholars spoke about him, yet Muslim produced many hadiths from him in his Sahih. Something has been narrated from al-Daraqutni strengthening his standing, and Allah knows best. That is what the Shaykh Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, with my reading upon him in Dar al-Qazz in Baghdad, I said to him: The minister Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Tirad ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Masada al-Ismaili informed us, by reading upon him more than once, he said: Abu al-Qasim Hamza ibn Yusuf al-Sahmi informed us, by reading upon him: I asked al-Daraqutni about Suwayd ibn Said; Yahya ibn Main spoke about him. He said: He narrated from Abu Muawiya, from al-Amash, from Atiyya, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise. Yahya ibn Main said: This is false from Abu Muawiya; none narrated it except Suwayd, and Suwayd was disparaged for narrating this hadith. Abu al-Hasan said: We continued to think it was as Yahya said, and that Suwayd had committed a grave matter in narrating this hadith, until I entered Egypt in the year fifty-seven and found this hadith in the Musnad of Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Yunus, known as al-Manjaniqi, and he was trustworthy. He narrated from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Muawiya, exactly as Suwayd said. Suwayd was cleared and the hadith was established from Abu Muawiya. Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated from this Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, and Abu Abd al-Rahman died before him."
"18","Abu Said al-Khudri, Sad ibn Malik, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 18. The Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghanayim al-Ansari the preacher informed us, with my reading upon him in the land of Egypt, I said to him: Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl ibn Abi Mansur al-Harawi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Muqatil ibn Subayh ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra al-Azdi informed us, he said: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jarrah al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Fudayl the merchant al-Mahbubi informed us, he said: Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawra al-Tirmidhi informed us; Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us; Uqba ibn Khalid narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Said, who said: Abu Bakr said: Am I not the most entitled of people to it? Am I not the first to accept Islam? Am I not the companion of such-and-such? Am I not the companion of such-and-such? Al-Tirmidhi narrated it so and said: A gharib hadith. He said: Some narrated it from Shuba, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, he said: Abu Bakr said; and this is more correct. Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us with that; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Shuba, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, he said: Abu Bakr said, and he mentioned the like in meaning, without mentioning Abu Said in it, and this is more correct. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from al-Hasan ibn Ishaq al-Isbahani, from Abd Allah ibn Said al-Ashajj with its chain."
"19","19. Abu al-Thana Hammad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Hammad al-Harrani and others also informed us in his book, and from him Abu al-Tahir Ismail ibn Tughra ibn Ahmad al-Nabulsi informed me: Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed us, by reading upon him: Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Saydalani informed us, with my reading upon him, I said to him: Abu Muhammad Yazdad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Yazdad the scribe informed you, by reading upon him: Abu Said Abd Allah ibn Said al-Ashajj narrated to us; Uqba narrated to me; Shuba narrated to us; Said al-Jurayri narrated to me, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Said, Abu Bakr said: Am I not the most entitled of people to it? Am I not the first to accept Islam? Am I not the companion of such-and-such?"
"20","Abu Barza Nadla ibn Ubayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 20. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, with my reading upon him, on the western side of Baghdad, I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Affan narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us; Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, that he narrated to them from Abu Barza al-Aslami that he said: We were with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq in his work, and he grew angry at a man among the Muslims, his anger intensified greatly against him. When I saw that, I said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, shall I strike his neck? When I mentioned killing, he turned from that talk altogether to other discourse. When we dispersed, Abu Bakr sent for me after that and said: O Abu Barza, what did you say? He said: I had forgotten what I said. I said: Remind me of it. He said: Do you not remember what you said? He said: I said: No, by Allah. He said: Did you see when I grew angry at the man, and you said: Shall I strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of Allah? Do you not remember that? Would you have done it? He said: I said: Yes, by Allah, and now if you command me, I shall do it. He said: Woe to you, by Allah, it belongs to no one after Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"21","21. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us; Yazid narrated to us, from Yunus, from Humayd, from Abd Allah ibn Mutarrif. 22. Abu Yala said: Umayya, he is Ibn Bistam, also narrated it to us; Yazid, he is Ibn Zuray, narrated to us; Yunus narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abd Allah ibn Mutarrif, from Abu Barza, who said: While Abu Bakr... In the hadith of Suwayd: We were with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq in his work, and he grew angry at a man among the Muslims; his anger intensified greatly against him. When I saw that, I said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, shall I not strike his neck? When I mentioned killing, he turned from that talk altogether to other discourse. When we dispersed, Abu Bakr sent for me after that and said: O Abu Barza, what did you say? He said: I had forgotten what I said. He said: I said: What did I say? Remind me of it. He said: Do you not remember what you said? He said: I said: No, by Allah. He said: Did you see when I grew angry at the man, and you said: Shall I strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of Allah? Do you not remember that? Would you have done that? He said: Yes, by Allah, and now if you command me, I shall do it. He said: Woe to you, by Allah, it belongs to no one after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Daraqutni said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated it and perfected its chain, saying: from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Barza. That is what Yazid ibn Zuray narrated from Yunus, and al-Hasan ibn Dinar followed him from Humayd ibn Hilal. Shuba narrated this hadith from Tawba al-Anbari, from Abu al-Sawwar the judge, whose name is Abd Allah ibn Qudama ibn Anaza, from Abu Barza."
"22","23. Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi and al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwa informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by reading upon him while they listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us; Tawba al-Anbari informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar Abd Allah narrating from Abu Barza that a man insulted Abu Bakr. He said: I said: Shall I not strike his neck, O successor of the Messenger of Allah? He said: It belongs to no one after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"23","24. With it Abu Yala informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us; Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, from Tawba al-Anbari, from Abd Allah ibn Qudama, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, who said: A man was harsh toward Abu Bakr. He said: I almost killed him, but Abu Bakr rebuked me and said: It belongs to no one except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"24","25. Zahir ibn Ahmad also informed us in Isfahan that Muhammad ibn Abi Dharr al-Salihani informed them, by reading upon him: Abu Tahir ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Musa and Bundar informed us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us; Shuba narrated to us, from Tawba al-Anbari, he said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar the judge narrating from Abu Barza al-Aslami, who said: A man was harsh toward Abu Bakr, so I said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, shall I not strike his neck? He rebuked me and said: It belongs to no one after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"25","26. My maternal uncle, the Imam the scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudama al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, also informed us that Wajih ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Mubarak al-Saqati informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Rafii informed us; Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Makhlad informed us; Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Daqqaq informed us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram ibn Hibban al-Bazzar narrated to us; Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, from Tawba al-Anbari, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Abu Barza, that a man angered Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, so I said: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, shall I not strike his neck? He said: Woe to you, this belongs to no one after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shuba. Abu Dawud narrated it from Harun ibn Abd Allah and Nusayr ibn al-Faraj, from Abu Usama, from Yazid ibn Zuray, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abd Allah ibn Mutarrif, from Abu Barza. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abu Dawud, from Affan, from Yazid ibn Zuray. He narrated it through routes and said: This is the best and finest of these hadiths. He narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Muadh ibn Muadh, from Shuba, from Tawba al-Anbari."
"26","Narration of Abu Hurayra from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both. 27. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him: Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba al-Asqalani informed us; Harmala ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Haywa informed us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn al-Harith al-Qurashi say: Abu Hurayra said: I heard Abu Bakr upon this pulpit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) this day last year say, then Abu Bakr wept with tears, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will not be given anything after the word of sincerity like well-being, so ask Allah for well-being. Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri also narrated it from Haywa."
"27","28. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, on the western side of Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading upon him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us; Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn al-Harith say: Abu Hurayra said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq upon this pulpit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on this day last year, then Abu Bakr wept with tears, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You have not been given anything after the word of sincerity like well-being, so ask Allah for well-being. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba."
"28","29. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii Abu Jafar informed us; Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Abu Bakr stood upon the pulpit and said: You know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with last year, and he wept, then repeated it, then wept, then repeated it, then wept. He said: People have not been given in this world anything better than pardon and well-being, so ask Allah, mighty and majestic, for them. Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of the Deed of Day and Night from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Husayn ibn Ali, its chain; and from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq, from his father, from Abu Hamza al-Sukkari, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Abu Bakr stood, without naming Abu Hurayra. Al-Daraqutni said: Zaida is alone in it from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from Abu Bakr; none narrated it from Zaida except Husayn, and Husayn ibn Ali was not followed in mentioning Abu Hurayra in its chain."
"29","30. Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us; Abu Ahmad Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, he said: Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Mani ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Hushaym narrated to us; Yala ibn Ata narrated to us, from Amr ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, that Abu Bakr asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Command me with words I say when I wake and when I evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil of Satan and his association. He said: Say them when you wake, when you evening, and when you take your bed."
"30","31. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi and Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal al-Adib informed them, by reading upon him while they listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Umar, narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra: that Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me words I say when I wake and evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You are Lord of everything and its Sovereign; there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil of Satan and his association. Say it when you wake, when you evening, and when you retire to your bed."
"31","32. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi also informed us, by reading upon him while I listened, it was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us; my father narrated to me; Bahz narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us; Yala ibn Ata informed us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim say: I heard Abu Hurayra say: Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I say when I wake, when I evening, and when I take my bed. He said: Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, or he said: O Allah, Knower of the seen, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and the evil of Satan and his association. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Hushaym. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud, from Shuba, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Uthman, from Abd al-Rahman, from Hushaym; and from Ziyad ibn Ayyub, from Hushaym; and from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ghundar, from Shuba. This hadith is more likely from the Musnad of Abu Hurayra, except that we found Imam Ahmad, Ahmad ibn Mani, and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili narrated it in the Musnad of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it in his Musnad from al-Abbas ibn Muhammad, from Hajjaj ibn Nusayr, from Shuba, from Yala ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from Abu Bakr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me, and he mentioned the hadith."
"32","Narration of Amr ibn Hurayth from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 33. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him while they listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to me, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abu Bakr, that he fell ill, and when many visited him, he said: O people, I do not spare you advice. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan; peoples will follow him as if their faces were shields."
"33","34. With it Abu Yala informed us; Harun al-Hammal narrated to us; Abu Usama narrated to us; al-Fazari, meaning Abu Ishaq, narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, who said: I heard Abu Bakr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Dajjal will emerge from a village called Khurasan."
"34","35. With it Abu Yala informed us; Abu Musa al-Zamin and al-Dawraqi Abu Abd Allah narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like. In the hadith of Abu Musa: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, he said: The Dajjal will emerge from a land toward the east called Khurasan; peoples will follow him as if their faces were layered shields."
"35","36. The Imam the scholar Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us; Abu Ahmad Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: My grandfather Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, by reading upon him, he said: Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Mani ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us. 37. The Imam Muzaffar ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Qiba al-Harimi also informed us, with my reading upon him in al-Harim in Baghdad, I said to him: Sulayman ibn Masud al-Qassab informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Rabii informed us; Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Khuldi narrated to us by dictation; al-Harith ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usama al-Tamimi narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us: that the Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan; peoples will follow him as if their faces were layered shields. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it from Rawh ibn Ubada. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and said: A hasan gharib hadith. Ibn Maja narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali, Muhammad ibn Bashshar, and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, all from Rawh ibn Ubada. Al-Daraqutni said: Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab narrated it from Abu al-Tayyah. Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated it from Abu al-Tayyah; Rawh ibn Ubada is alone in it from Said. It is said: Said ibn Abi Aruba only heard it from Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, and concealed it from him, dropping his name in the chain. The soundest in chain is the hadith of Ibn Shawdhab from Abu al-Tayyah."
"36","Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them. 38. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi al-Harawi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: The Imam Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai al-Bukhari informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Miqal al-Shashi informed us; Abu Yahya Isa ibn Ahmad informed us; al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Abu Naama al-Adawi narrated to us; Abu Hunayda al-Bara ibn Nawfal narrated to us, from Walan al-Adawi, from Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq."
"37","39. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Abu Naama narrated to us; al-Bara ibn Nawfal informed us, from Walan al-Adawi, from Hudhayfa, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one day, prayed the dawn prayer, then sat, until when it was forenoon, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed. Then he sat in his place until he prayed the first, the afternoon, and the sunset prayers, each time not speaking, until he prayed the last night prayer. Then he rose to his family. People said to Abu Bakr: Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is his affair; today he did something he never did. He asked him, and he said: Yes. What will be of the affair of the world and the Hereafter was displayed to me. The first and the last will be gathered on one plain, and that will terrify people. They will go to Adam, with sweat almost bridling them, and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind, and Allah chose you; intercede for us to your Lord. He will say: I have met the like of what you met; go to your father after your father, to Noah: Verily Allah chose Adam and Noah and the family of Ibrahim and the family of Imran above the worlds. He said: They will go to Noah and say: Intercede for us to your Lord, for Allah chose you and answered you in your supplication, so He left none of the disbelievers on earth. He will say: That is not with me; go to Ibrahim, for Allah took him as a friend. They will come to Ibrahim, and he will say: That is not with me; go to Musa, for Allah spoke to him with speech. Musa will say: That is not with me, but go to Isa, for he heals the blind and the leper and gives life to the dead. Isa will say: That is not with me; go to the master of the children of Adam, for he is the first for whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection. Go to Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him intercede for you to your Lord. He said: He will go, and Jibril will come to his Lord. Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: Jibril will go with him, and he will fall prostrate for the extent of a Friday. Then Allah Most High will say: O Muhammad, raise your head; speak, you will be heard; intercede, you will be granted intercession. He said: He will raise his head, and when he looks at his Lord, mighty and majestic, he will fall prostrate for the extent of another Friday. Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: O Muhammad, raise your head; speak, you will be heard; intercede, you will be granted intercession. He said: He will go to fall prostrate. Jibril will take him by his upper arms, and Allah Most High will open for him supplication He never opened for any human. He said: He will say: My Lord, You made me the master of the children of Adam, without pride, and the first for whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection, without pride, until there comes to me at the Basin more than what is between Sanaa and Ayla. Then it will be said: Call the truthful, and they will intercede. Then it will be said: Call the prophets. He said: The prophet will come with a company, the prophet with five and six, and the prophet with no one. Then it will be said: Call the martyrs. He said: They will intercede for whomever they wish. When the martyrs do that, He said: Allah, blessed and exalted, will say: I am the Most Merciful of the merciful; admit to My Paradise whoever did not associate anything with Me, and they will enter Paradise. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, will say: Look in the Fire whether anyone ever did any good. He said: They will find in the Fire a man, and it will be said to him: Did you ever do any good? He will say: No, except that I was lenient with people in sale. It will be said: Be lenient to My servant as he was lenient to My servants. Then they will bring out of the Fire another man, and it will be said to him: Did you ever do any good? He will say: No, except that I commanded my children: when I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter me in the sea, for by Allah, if my Lord seizes me, He will punish me such as He punished none of the worlds. Allah will say: Why did you do that? He will say: Out of fear of You. He will say: Look at the greatest kingdom you see, for it is yours with its like. A man will say: Do you mock me while You are the King? Allah will laugh at that and say: I do not mock you, but I am able over whatever I will. That is when he laughed in forenoon. And Allah knows best concerning the rest of the hadith. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Musa Ishaq al-Harawi, and he mentioned the hadith in full. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb also narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Yahya Isa ibn Ahmad. Al-Daraqutni said: Walan al-Adawi is unknown, and Abu Hunayda is unknown; this hadith is not established."
"38","Muhammad ibn Hatib, and it is said: al-Harith ibn Hatib, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 40. Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us; Khalid informed us, from Khalid, from Yusuf Abu Yaqub, from Muhammad ibn Hatib or al-Harith, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr was mentioned, and he said: How long he coveted command. I said: What is that? He said: A thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered his killing. It was said: He stole. He said: Cut him. Then he was brought after that to Abu Bakr, having stolen, with his limbs cut. Abu Bakr said: I find for you nothing except what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed concerning you on the day he ordered your killing, for he knew you better. He ordered his killing: young lads among the sons of the Emigrants, I among them. Ibn al-Zubayr said: Make me commander over you, so we made him commander over us. We went with him to al-Baqi and killed him."
"39","41. Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us, by reading upon him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us; Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us; al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Ibn al-Munadi, he is Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Sad, from al-Harith ibn Hatib, that a man stole in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was brought. They said: He stole. He said twice: Kill him. They said: He only stole. He said: Cut his hand, and it was cut. Then he stole in the time of Abu Bakr and was cut, then stole and was cut, then stole and all his limbs were cut. Then he stole a fifth time. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew this about him when he ordered his killing. Take him and kill him. He handed him to youths of Quraysh, among them Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Make me commander over you, so they made him commander over them. When he threw, they threw until they killed him. Al-Qasim also narrated it from Ibn al-Munadi, from Yunus ibn Muhammad, from Hammad with its chain, the like, and in it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew better about him when he ordered his killing, without mentioning Muhammad ibn Hatib."
"40","Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathila from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 42. Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, with my reading upon him, on the western side of Baghdad, I said: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd Allah said: I heard it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Shayba; Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken, Fatima sent to Abu Bakr: Did you inherit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or his family? He said: He said: No, rather his family. She said: Where is the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Abu Bakr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah, mighty and majestic, feeds a prophet a sustenance then takes him, He makes it for the one who stands after him. I deemed to return it to the Muslims. She said: You know best what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud produced it from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"41","43. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi also informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi and al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by reading upon them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: Fatima sent to Abu Bakr after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: What is with you, O successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Did you inherit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or his family? He said: No, rather his family. She said: What of the share of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah feeds a prophet a sustenance then takes him to Him, He makes it for the one who stands after him. I deemed to return it to the Muslims. She said: You know best what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"42","Wahshi ibn Harb from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. 44. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in al-Harbiyya, it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi ibn Harb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Wahshi ibn Harb: that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, appointed Khalid ibn al-Walid over fighting the people of apostasy, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What an excellent servant of Allah and brother of the tribe is Khalid ibn al-Walid, a sword among the swords of Allah that Allah, mighty and majestic, unsheathed against the disbelievers and hypocrites."
"43","45. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai al-Bukhari informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Miqal al-Shashi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us; Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us; al-Walid narrated to us; Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi ibn Harb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that Abu Bakr directed Khalid ibn al-Walid to fight the people of apostasy. He was spoken to about that but refused to turn him back, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, mentioning Khalid ibn al-Walid: What an excellent servant of Allah and brother of the tribe, a sword among the swords of Allah that Allah unsheathed against the disbelievers and hypocrites. Then Abu Bakr said: O Wahshi, march with Khalid and strive in the path of Allah as you strove to turn away from the path of Allah. Wahshi said: He marched and I marched with him. We fought the people of apostasy until they returned to Islam. Then Abu Bakr wrote to him ordering him to march to Musaylima the liar and the disbelievers of Banu Hanifa. He marched to them and they fought fiercely. They routed the Muslims times, and in the fourth the Muslims charged them, Allah turned to them, Allah made their feet firm, and they felt the place of swords. Swords clashed between them and Banu Hanifa until I saw like fire coming from their midst, until I heard for it sounds like bells. Allah, majestic His majesty, sent His help, Allah routed Banu Hanifa, and Allah killed Musaylima. Wahshi said: I struck that day with my sword until its hilt stuck to my palm from their blood. They wrote of Allah's conquest and help to Abu Bakr, and he wrote to Khalid ordering him to march toward Iraq, and he did."
"44","46. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed you, by reading upon her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather: that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, directed Khalid ibn al-Walid in fighting the people of apostasy. He was spoken to about that but refused to turn him back, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, mentioning Khalid ibn al-Walid: What an excellent servant of Allah and brother of the tribe, a sword among the swords of Allah."
"45","Rafi ibn Amr al-Tai, the companion of Abu Bakr in the expedition of Dhu al-Salasil. 47. al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading upon him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Said ibn Dhi Uswan al-Ansi informed me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rafi al-Tai, the companion of Abu Bakr in the expedition of al-Salasil, who said: I asked him about what was said of their pledge. He said, narrating to him what the Ansar said, what he said to them, what Umar ibn al-Khattab said to the Ansar, and what he reminded them of my leading them in prayer by command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness. They pledged to me for that, I accepted it from them, and I feared there would be a trial after which would be apostasy."
"46","Narration of Aisha from her father, may Allah be pleased with them both. 48. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Haddad informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us; Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isa ibn Talha narrated to me, from Aisha, who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: I was the first to return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud, with him Talha. We found him overcome by bleeding, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was better than him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tend to your companion. We did not turn to him, but turned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), upon his head a helmet whose rings had stuck to his cheeks. Between me and the east was a man, though I was nearer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); it was Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah. I went to remove it from him, but Abu Ubayda said: I beseech you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, leave me to remove it. He pulled it and brought it out, and a front tooth of Abu Ubayda was pulled out. I went to remove the other ring, but Abu Ubayda said to me: I beseech you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, leave me to remove it. I left him, he pulled it out, and the other front tooth of Abu Ubayda was pulled out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your companion has earned. Shababa narrated it from Ishaq ibn Yahya."
"47","49. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us, by reading upon him in Balkh: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Munadi narrated to us; Shababa narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us; Isa ibn Talha narrated to us, from Aisha, who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: On the day of Uhud, all people turned away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was the first to return to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw before him a man fighting for him and shielding him. I said: Be Talha, may my father and mother be ransom for you; be Talha, may my father and mother be ransom for you. I had hardly waited when Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah caught up with me, hastening as if a bird, until he joined me. We reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was Talha fallen before him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tend to your brother, for he has earned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been struck in his forehead, his face struck until a ring of the helmet sank into his cheek. I went to remove it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but Abu Ubayda said: I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, leave me. He said: Abu Ubayda took the arrow with his mouth and began moving it, disliking to hurt the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he drew the arrow with his mouth, and a front tooth of Abu Ubayda fell. Abu Bakr said: Then I went to take the other, but Abu Ubayda said: I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, leave me. He said: He took it with his mouth and began moving it, then drew it, and the other front tooth of Abu Ubayda fell. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tend to your brother, for he has earned. He said: We turned to Talha treating him; he had received a dozen and more wounds, between strike, stab, and shot, among them a glint on his forehead, and among them what severed his sciatic vein until his finger withered. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ishaq. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, from Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith, from Shababa, the like. I say: I know this hadith only from the narration of Ishaq ibn Yahya; more than one of the Imams spoke about him, though more than one of the Imams narrated from him. But the story of Talha and his steadfastness with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Uhud is well known, and Allah knows best."
"48","Asma bint Umays, wife of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both. 50. Abu al-Hasan al-Muayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tusi informed us, with my reading upon him in Nishapur, I said: Abu Muhammad Hibat Allah ibn Sahl ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn, known as al-Sayyidi, informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Uthman Said ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhayri informed us; Abu Ali Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi informed us in Baghdad; Abu Musab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri al-Madani narrated to us; Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Command her to bathe, then to enter ihram."
"49","51. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us; and I said to our Shaykh... Fatima bint Abd Allah informed you, by reading upon her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us, they said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Asma bint Umays, that she gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at al-Bayda. Abu Bakr mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Command her to bathe. Yusuf ibn Abi al-Muhajir narrated it from al-Qasim, from Asma."
"50","52. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi and al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading upon them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is al-Qawariri, informed us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Asma bint Umays, that she entered postpartum at Dhu al-Hulayfa. Abu Bakr asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Command her to bathe and enter ihram. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Salama and al-Harith ibn Miskin, from Ibn al-Qasim, from Malik. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement in it, saying: Malik narrated it from Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Asma bint Umays. Among them who said: from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that Asma bint Umays. Ubayd Allah ibn Umar said: from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha. He said: The soundest in my view is the statement of Malik and those who followed him. I say: As for the narration of Aisha, Muslim narrated it in his Sahih. Al-Qasim may have heard it from Aisha and from Asma bint Umays, and Allah knows best. Perhaps one says: If it is established from Aisha, why did you narrate it? We say: No one mentioned it in the narration of Aisha from Abu Bakr; it is only from the narration of Aisha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the hadith of Asma is mentioned in the narration of Asma from Abu Bakr. Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated it from Asma."
"51","53. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Warraq narrated to us; Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Asma bint Umays: that she entered postpartum with Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr at Dhu al-Hulayfa. Abu Bakr asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded him to command her to bathe and enter ihram."
"52","Narration of Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 54. Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, with my reading upon him, on the western side of Baghdad, I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to me from his book; Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us; Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us, from Qays. 55. Imam Ahmad also said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muawiya, narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us; Qays narrated to us. 56. Imam Ahmad said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim. 57. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Khaythama informed us; Jarir narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim. 58. Abu Yala said; Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh, he is Ibn Muadh al-Anbari, narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O people, you recite this verse and place it other than where Allah, mighty and majestic, placed it: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided. When people see wrong and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them in punishment. The wording of Shuba from Ismail. Jarir said in his narration: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, recited this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided, then said: People place this verse other than its place. Verily I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hand, or see wrong and do not change it, Allah, majestic and mighty, envelops them in His punishment. Yazid ibn Harun said, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hand, Allah is about to envelop them in punishment. Zuhayr ibn Muawiya said in his narration: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, saying: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided, to the end of the verse, and you place it other than its place. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people see wrong and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them in His punishment. He said: I heard Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, say: O people, beware of lying, for lying is apart from faith. Al-Hakam narrated it from Qays ibn Abi Hazim as mawquf."
"53","59. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Muadh, narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr with the like, without mentioning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar ibn Ali narrated it from Ismail as marfu."
"54","60. Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us likewise that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us; Umar ibn Ali narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays, who said: I heard Abu Bakr say: O people, you recite this verse and place it other than its place: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided, and we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people see wrong and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them in His punishment. Ahmad ibn Mani and Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun in their Musnads."
"55","61. Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us; Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us; my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us; Ahmad ibn Mani informed us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hand, Allah is about to envelop them in punishment from Him. Al-Daraqutni was asked about this hadith, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated it from Qays. A group of trustworthy narrated it, differing upon him in it: among them who raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among them who stopped it upon Abu Bakr. Among those who raised it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abd Allah ibn Numayr, Abu Usama, Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi, Zuhayr ibn Muawiya, Hushaym ibn Bashir, Abd Allah ibn Amr, Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyya, Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari, Murajja ibn Raja, Yazid ibn Harun, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, al-Walid ibn al-Qasim, Ali ibn Asim, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid, Shuba ibn al-Hajjaj, Malik ibn Mighwal, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali, Hayyaj ibn Bistam, Mualla ibn Hilal, Abu Hamza al-Sukkari, and Waki ibn al-Jarrah; they agreed on raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan, Sufyan ibn Uyayna, Ismail ibn Mujalid, and Ubayd Allah ibn Musa opposed them, narrating it from Ismail as mawquf upon Abu Bakr. He said: All narrators of this hadith are trustworthy. It resembles that Qays ibn Abi Hazim was active in narration at times, raising it, and at times cautious about it, stopping it upon Abu Bakr. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Wahb ibn Baqiyya, from Khalid al-Tahhan, and from Amr ibn Awn, from Hushaym, all from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, the hadith of Amr being fuller. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and Ibn Bashshar, separating them, from Yazid ibn Harun. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama, from Ismail. Al-Nasai narrated it from Utba ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ismail. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq, from Jarir."
"56","62. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, by reading upon him while they listened: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu Amr ibn Hamdan informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Shayban ibn Abi Shayba; Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to me; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Association is more hidden in my nation than the crawling of ants upon smooth rock. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how is salvation and exit from that? He said: Shall I not inform you of something which, when you say it, you are cleared of its little, much, and small? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know."
"57","63. Abu al-Qasim Said ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Attaf al-Hamdani informed us, with my reading upon him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you by license that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tamimi permitted them narration: Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Shahin informed us, by reading upon him; Abd Allah narrated to us; Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us; Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us; Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among association is what is more hidden than the crawling of ants upon smooth rock. Abu Bakr says: O Messenger of Allah, how is safety and exit from that? He said: Shall I not inform you of something which, when you say it, you are cleared of its little and much? Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from associating with You while I know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know."
"58","64. My maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudama, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, by reading upon him, it was said to him: Abu Zura Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham informed us; Abu Talha al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salama al-Qattan informed us; Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Maja narrated to us; Amr ibn Uthman ibn Said ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama al-Majishun narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Habis al-Yamani, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn is in Allah's protection; do not betray Allah in His covenant. Whoever kills him, Allah will seek him until He throws him in the Fire upon his face. So Abu Abd Allah Ibn Maja narrated it in his Sunan."
"59","Abd al-Rahman ibn Yarbu from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both. 65. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by reading upon him while he listened: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Ibrahim, Duhaym al-Dimashqi, narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yarbu, from his father, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which Hajj is best? He said: Raising the voice and shedding blood. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi and Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yarbu, from Abu Bakr, saying: A gharib hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Ibn Abi Fudayk. Ibn al-Munkadir did not hear from Abd al-Rahman, though he narrated from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yarbu other than this hadith. Abu Nuaym Dirar ibn Surad al-Tahhan narrated it from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Said, from his father, from Abu Bakr. Ibn Hanbal said: Whoever says in this hadith: from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yarbu, from his father, has erred. Ibn Maja narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir and Yaqub ibn Humayd, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, mentioning it with its chain, the like. Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated it from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Dahhak, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Said, from his father. Al-Daraqutni said: The genealogists say: Abd al-Rahman ibn Said ibn Yarbu; whoever says: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman has erred, and Allah knows best."
"60","Awsat ibn Ismail ibn Awsat, and it is said: Ibn Amr, and it is said: Ibn Amir al-Bajali Abu Ismail, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 66. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Your father informed you; the preacher Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Hizar-mard al-Sarifini informed us, by reading upon him: Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababa informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Ali, he is Ibn al-Jad, narrated to us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, he said: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir narrating from Awsat al-Bajali ibn Ismail ibn Awsat that he heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, a year after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood last year in this place of mine. Then Abu Bakr wept, then said: Upon you is truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and they are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and they are in the Fire. Ask Allah, mighty and majestic, for well-being, for no one has been given anything after certainty better than well-being. Do not sever, do not turn backs, do not envy, do not hate, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"61","67. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, on the western side of Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai al-Bukhari informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Miqal al-Shashi narrated to us; Ibn al-Munadi, meaning Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us; Yazid ibn Khumayr informed me, he said: Sulaym ibn Amir, a man of Hims who had met the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: I heard Awsat al-Bajali say: I heard Abu Bakr, addressing us when he was made successor, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in this place of mine last year. Then he wept, then said: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being. Upon you is truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and they are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and they are in the Fire. Do not sever, do not turn backs, do not hate, do not envy, and be servants of Allah as brothers, as Allah commanded you."
"62","68. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa and Umm Habiba Aisha bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Muhammad Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim al-Dimashqi narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Amir says: I heard Awsat al-Bajali, upon the pulpit of Hims, say: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say, then tears choked him, then he returned and tears choked him, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say last year: Ask Allah for certainty and well-being, for a servant is only given after certainty better than well-being. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Ali ibn Muhammad, from Ubayd ibn Said, from Shuba. Al-Nasai narrated it in the Deed of Day and Night from Yahya ibn Uthman, from Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir; and from Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami, from Umayya ibn Khalid, from Shuba; and from Abu Dawud al-Harrani, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman, from Isa ibn Abi Razin al-Yamani al-Himsi, from Luqman ibn Amir, from Awsat; and from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Mahdi, from Muawiya ibn Salih, from Sulaym ibn Amir, the like. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. Abu Abd Allah al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Asamm, from al-Rabi ibn Sulayman, from Bishr ibn Bakr, from Jabir, from Sulaym."
"63","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both. 69. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal and Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon them while you listened, they said: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr narrated to me, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, how is well-being after this verse: Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it; for everything we do we are recompensed? He said: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr, do you not fall ill? Do you not toil? Does hardship not befall you? That is what you are recompensed with."
"64","70. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa and Umm Habiba Aisha bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Abu Muhammad Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us, he said: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us; Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, a maternal brother of Abu Abd Allah al-Jadali, that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, how is well-being after this verse: It is not by your wishes nor the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil will be recompensed for it. For every evil we do we are recompensed, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr, do you not toil? Do you not grieve? Does hardship not befall you? He said: Yes. He said: That is what you are recompensed with. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Ismail, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr: I was informed that Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah. He narrated it also from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr, I think he said Abu Bakr: O Messenger of Allah. Abu Zura al-Razi said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq is mursal. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, from Abu Khaythama."
"65","Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with them both. 71. Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamza ibn Ali ibn Talha al-Baghdadi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Cairo, and Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qasri, with my reading upon him in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Asadi narrated to me in Aleppo; Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Abu Khalid al-Mujawwiz narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Sad al-Tai, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood among us beside the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and wept. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in this place of mine last year, saying: O people, ask Allah for well-being, for no one has been given after certainty like well-being."
"66","72. Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Hasan ibn Zayd ibn al-Hasan ibn Said ibn Isma al-Kindi also informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Said ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: The Sharif Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: It was read upon Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Khalaf, while I listened: Ibn Said narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Faraj Abu Utba al-Himsi and Uthman ibn Mabad ibn Nuh al-Muqri narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Umar al-Muhri narrated to us. 73. Ibn Said said: Muhammad ibn Awf also narrated to us; Khattab ibn Uthman al-Fawzi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umar Abu Khalid al-Muhri al-Himsi, he said: I heard Thabit ibn Sad al-Tai narrating from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he stood among people upon the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Uthman ibn Mabad said in his hadith: beside the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then wept, saying: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in this place of mine of last year, saying: O people, ask Allah for well-being, for no one has been given like well-being after certainty. Uthman said: after certainty. Al-Nasai narrated it in the book Deed of Day and Night from Amr ibn Uthman, from his father, from Abu Khalid Muhammad ibn Amr al-Muhri al-Tai, the like."
"67","74. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia, from Hakim ibn Hakim, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf: that a man shot a man with an arrow and killed him, with no heir except a maternal uncle. Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah wrote about that to Umar, and Umar wrote: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of one with no guardian, and the maternal uncle is heir of one with no heir."
"68","75. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, with my reading upon him in Baghdad, I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us; my father narrated to me; Waki narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that a man shot a man with an arrow and killed him, with no heir except a maternal uncle. Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah wrote about that to Umar, who wrote: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of one with no guardian, and the maternal uncle is heir of one with no heir. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yahya ibn Adam, from Sufyan."
"69","76. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi also informed us, with my reading upon him, I said to him: Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is al-Qawariri, narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Umar wrote to Abu Ubayda: Teach your boys swimming and your fighters shooting. They would move between targets, when a stray arrow came and struck a boy, killing him. No origin was known for the boy except his maternal uncle. He said: Abu Ubayda wrote to Umar mentioning to him the affair of the boy, to whom to pay his blood-money. He wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of one with no guardian, and the maternal uncle is heir of one with no heir."
"70","77. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, by reading upon him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Duri narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabia, from Hakim ibn Hakim, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of one with no guardian, and the maternal uncle is heir of one with no heir. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Ali ibn Muhammad, both from Waki. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Waki, the like. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan hadith. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala."
"71","Abu Khalid Aslam, freedman of Umar, from him, may Allah be pleased with him. 78. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Umar, narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: What is trotting and baring shoulders, when Allah has illumined Islam and removed association? He said: Then he said: Yet we do not leave anything we used to do in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"72","79. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, in it, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading upon him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: What is trotting now and baring shoulders, when Allah has established Islam and removed disbelief and its people? Yet we do not leave anything we used to do in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Hanbal. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abu Bakr, from Jafar ibn Awn, from Hisham."
"73","Another. 80. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to give charity, and wealth coincided with me. I said: Today I shall outstrip Abu Bakr, if ever I outstrip him a day. He said: I brought half my wealth. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What have you left for your family? I said: The like. Abu Bakr came with all he had, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have you left for your family? He said: I left for them Allah and His Messenger. I said: I shall never race you to anything."
"74","81. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Hurdi al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us, by reading upon him, while we listened, on the western side of Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ziyadi al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai al-Bukhari informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Miqal al-Shashi the litterateur in Bukhara informed us; Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Abu Nuaym, he is al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to give charity, and wealth coincided with me. I said: Today I shall outstrip Abu Bakr, if ever I outstrip him a day. He said: I brought half my wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: What have you left for your family? I said: The like. Abu Bakr came with all he had, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, what have you left for your family? He said: I left for them Allah and His Messenger. I said: I shall never race you to anything. Marked part dropped from our hearing. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Nuaym. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Salih and Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, from al-Fadl ibn Dukayn. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from al-Fadl, saying: A sahih hadith."
"75","82. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Muhammad ibn Sahl narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat oil as condiment and anoint with it, for it comes from a blessed tree. Ibn Askar said: A youth of Marw called Ahmad ibn Said said to him: This hadith you used not to raise? He said: That is upon what we were narrated, and this is upon what we narrate."
"76","83. Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi also informed us, with my reading upon him in it, I said to him: Abu al-Mahasin Asad ibn Ziyad informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuya al-Sarakhsi informed us; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Zayd, from his father, from Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat oil as condiment and anoint with it, for it comes from a blessed tree. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yahya ibn Musa, from Abd al-Razzaq, saying: We know it only from the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq. Abd al-Razzaq was confused in its narration: sometimes he mentioned Umar in it, sometimes he narrated it in doubt, saying: I think it is from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and sometimes he said: from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without mentioning Umar. Ibn Maja narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Mahdi, from Abd al-Razzaq."
"77","84. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Isbahani informed us, with my reading upon him in it, I said to him: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Prophet Musa said: My Lord, show us our father who expelled us and himself from Paradise. Allah showed him Adam, blessings upon him."
"78","85. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Sad ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; al-Harith ibn Miskin al-Misri narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sad informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, he is Ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Musa, blessings upon him, said: My Lord, our father Adam expelled us and himself from Paradise. He showed him Adam, blessings upon him, and said: Are you Adam? He said: I am Adam, yes. He said: Are you the one into whom Allah breathed of His spirit, to whom He made His angels prostrate, and whom He taught all names? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to expel us and yourself from Paradise? Adam said to him: Who are you? He said: I am Musa. He said: Are you the prophet of Banu Israil to whom Allah spoke from behind a veil, making no messenger of His creation between you and Him? He said: Yes. He said: Do you blame me for a matter whose decree preceded from Allah, mighty and majestic, before? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa; Adam overcame Musa. The wording of al-Harith ibn Miskin. The narration of al-Hizami: He said: Are you the one who expelled us and yourself from Paradise? Adam said to him: Yes. He said: Are you the one into whom He breathed of His spirit, whom He taught all names, and commanded His angels who prostrated to you? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to expel us and yourself from Paradise? Adam said to him: Who are you? He said: I am Musa. He said: Are you the prophet of Banu Israil? Are you the one to whom your Lord spoke from behind a veil, making no messenger of His creation between you and Him? He said: Yes. He said: Did you not find that in Allah's Book, that it would be before I was created? He said: Yes. He said: For what do you blame me for something whose decree preceded from Allah before me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa. Abu Dawud narrated it in al-Sunna from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ibn Wahb, the like. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayra."
"79","Another. 86. Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that Abu al-Fath Muflih ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Dumi informed them, by reading upon him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi informed us; Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lului informed us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us; Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, struck a son of his who took the kunya Abu Isa, and that al-Mughira ibn Shuba took the kunya Abu Isa. Umar said to him: Does it not suffice you to take the kunya Abu Abd Allah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunya. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed, while in our midst. He continued to take the kunya Abu Abd Allah until he died. So Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan; it more resembles the Musnad of al-Mughira ibn Shuba, but some produced it in the Musnad of Umar ibn al-Khattab. Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam."
"80","87. The Hafiz Imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini al-Isbahani informed us in his book that Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Abi Nasr al-Burji informed them in the year seven: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abu Ali al-Sawwaf narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Khuttali narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that he mentioned that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent for his son Abd al-Rahman. When he came, he said: What is Abu Isa? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, al-Mughira ibn Shuba took it as kunya in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, saying: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrates it from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar as musnad. Hammad ibn Salama and others opposed him, narrating it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Umar. The more resembling is the statement of one who sent it as mursal. I say: The narration of Hisham ibn Sad from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar is other than the narration of Habib, except that he mentioned the musnad from the statement of al-Mughira, and Allah knows best."
"81","Another. 88. Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah al-Qasri informed us, with my reading upon him, on the western side of Baghdad, I said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; the Sharif Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Miqal al-Shashi informed us in Bukhara; Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawra al-Tirmidhi, may Allah's mercy upon him, informed us; Harun ibn Musa ibn Abi Alqama al-Madini narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him to give him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have nothing, but buy upon my account; when something comes to me, I shall pay it. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you have given him; Allah has not burdened you with what you cannot bear. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked Umar's statement. A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, spend, and do not fear from the Owner of the Throne lessening. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, and cheer was known on his face at the Ansari's statement, then said: With this I was commanded. So al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the book al-Shamail."
"82","Another. 89. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me wealth, but I returned it. When I came to him, he said: What carried you to return what I sent to you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not say: It is better for you not to take anything from people? He said: That is only asking people. What comes to you without asking is only provision Allah, mighty and majestic, provided you. It is narrated in the Sahih from the narration of Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, and from the narration of Abd Allah ibn al-Sadi, from Umar, but in this are wordings not in what was mentioned, and Allah knows best. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Ibn Abi Shayba, from Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Hisham."
"83","Another. 90. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Isfahan, it was said to him: Abu Nasr Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Imam Abi Abd Allah ibn Manda permitted you in the year five hundred fourteen: My grandfather Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab al-Abdi informed us, by reading upon him: My father, the Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Khurasan informed us; Ahmad ibn Abbad ibn Tamim informed us; Hamid ibn Adam narrated to us; Abu Ghanim Yunus ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the hireling his wage while his sweat remains. Yunus ibn Nafi: Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, Muadh ibn Asad, and Utba ibn Abd Allah al-Marwazi also narrated from him."
"84","Another. 91. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us...; Zakariyya al-Saji narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us; Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while an Abyssinian massaged his back. I said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The camel rushed with me. So Hisham ibn Sad narrated it. Qutayba ibn Said narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Zayd did not hear from Umar."
"85","92. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, that a man nicknamed Donkey would gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a skin of clarified butter and honey. When its owner came demanding him, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Give this his goods. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would only smile and order it be given. Al-Bukhari narrated from it: that a man nicknamed Donkey would make the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laugh..."
"86","Aswad ibn Yazid al-Nakhai Abu Amr al-Kufi the jurist from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 93. The Imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli, mufti of Isfahan, and Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us in Isfahan that Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed them, by reading upon her while they listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Bahir ibn Abd Allah ibn Muawiya ibn Bahir ibn Raysan al-Himyari narrated to us in Egypt; Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for his need, finding no one to follow him. Umar was alarmed and brought him a vessel of water from behind. He found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in a thicket. He withdrew from behind him until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, saying: You did well, O Umar, when you found me prostrating and withdrew from me. Jibril, peace upon him, came to me saying: Whoever sends one blessing upon you among your nation, Allah sends ten upon him and raises him ten degrees by it. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Amr ibn al-Rabi is alone in it."
"87","Al-Ashath ibn Qays from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 94. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abu Awana narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi, from Abd al-Rahman al-Musalli, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man is not asked about what he struck his wife for. Abu Dawud narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Harb."
"88","95. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi also informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in al-Harbiyya, it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Sulayman ibn Dawud, meaning Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated to us; Abu Awana informed us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from Abd al-Rahman al-Musalli, from al-Ashath ibn Qays, who said: I was guest of Umar; he took his wife and struck her, saying: O Ashath, remember from me three I remembered from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man is not asked about what he struck his wife for; do not sleep except upon witr; and I forgot the third. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid, from Abu Awana. Ibn Maja narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya and al-Hasan ibn Mudrik al-Tahhan, from Yahya ibn Hammad, and from Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur and Amr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, both from Abu Awana, the like."
"89","Jabir ibn Samura from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 96. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Shayban narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrating from Jabir ibn Samura al-Suwai, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed us at al-Jabiya, saying: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in my place among you, saying: Do good to my Companions, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man testifies to testimony not asked of him, and swears an oath not asked of him. Whoever among you wants the middle of Paradise, let him keep to the community, for Satan is with the one, and is farther from the two. None of you be alone with a woman, for Satan is their third. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."
"90","97. With this chain Abu Yala informed us; Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us; Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed at al-Jabiya and mentioned it, and in it: then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then lying will spread among them, the rest the like. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Jarir."
"91","98. Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sibt informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Your father Abu Ali al-Hasan informed you, he said: My father Abu Sad al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan informed us, he said: My grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Lalal, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us; Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Aws al-Muqri narrated to us; Abu Abd Allah Abd al-Hamid ibn Isam narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shuba informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr: I heard Jabir ibn Samura say: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us at al-Jabiya, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, saying: Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man testifies though not called to testify, and a man swears though not asked to swear. Whoever wants the middle of Paradise, let him keep to the community, for Satan is with the one, and is farther from the two. No man be alone with a woman, for their third is Satan. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abd Allah ibn al-Jarrah, from Jarir. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar, from Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Jarir ibn Hazim; and from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrates it, differing upon him in its chain. Several statements are said in it from him: Jarir ibn Hazim, Muhammad ibn Shabib al-Zahrani, Qurra ibn Khalid, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid, and it is said Shuba ibn al-Hajjaj narrate it from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, from Umar. A group of trustworthy opposed them, mentioning a group, narrating it from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umar. He mentioned other disagreement, saying at its end: The confusion in this chain resembles being from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, due to many trustworthy differing from him in the chain, and Allah knows best. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, from Abu Khaythama; and from Abu Yala, from Ali ibn Hamza al-Miwali, from Jarir ibn Hazim; and from Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi, from Abd al-Ala, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Jarir ibn Hazim."
"92","Jabir ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. 99. Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Ghanim ibn Khalid al-Isbahani informed us, with my reading upon him in it, I said to him: Your grandfather Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading upon him: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa ibn Shamma informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba informed us; Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sad informed us, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Umar, who said: I felt desire one day and kissed while fasting. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Today I did a grave matter; I kissed while fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What if you rinsed with water while fasting? He said: I said: There is no harm in that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then for what? Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Hajjaj, from Layth ibn Sad. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Abu al-Walid, from Layth."
"93","100. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Ibn al-Munadi, he is Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, narrated to us; Shababa narrated to us; Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I felt desire one day toward the woman and kissed her while fasting. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, one day I committed a grave matter; I kissed while fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What if you rinsed with water? He said: I said: No harm in it. He said: Then for what? Al-Haytham also narrated it from Hamdun ibn Abbad al-Baghdadi, from Shababa, from al-Layth with its chain, and in it: One day I committed a grave matter. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Yunus and Isa ibn Hammad, from al-Layth. Al-Nasai narrated it from Qutayba, from Layth, saying: This is a munkar hadith. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, from Abu al-Walid, from Layth."
"94","Another. 101. Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamza ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us, by reading while we listened, it was said to him: Abu Ali ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you by license. And it was said to him: Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every cause and lineage is cut on the Day of Resurrection except my cause and lineage."
"95","102. Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani also informed us by license that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by reading upon him: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Khayyat narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say to people when he married the daughter of Ali: Will you not congratulate me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every cause and lineage is cut on the Day of Resurrection except my cause and lineage. Al-Tabarani said: None perfected this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyayna except al-Hasan ibn Sahl. Others narrated it from Sufyan, from Jafar, from his father, without mentioning Jabir ibn Abd Allah. Al-Mustazill ibn Husayn narrated the like from Umar, coming in his biography."
"96","Another. 103. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us. And I said to our Shaykh: Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us, they said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us; Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Bishr, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umar, who said: Two men entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for something, and he aided them with two dinars. They went out praising good. I entered upon him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I saw so-and-so and so-and-so go out from you praising good. He said: But so-and-so does not say that, though I gave him between ten and a hundred, yet he does not say that. One of you leaves me with his charity under his arm, while it is Fire for him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you give him while you know it is Fire for him? He said: What shall I do? They come asking me, and Allah refuses for me miserliness."
"97","104. Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abd Allah al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us; Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Bishr, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Two men entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for something, and he aided them with two dinars. They went out from him praising good. I entered upon him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I met so-and-so and so-and-so go out from you, praising good. He said: But so-and-so does not say that, though I aided him between ten and a hundred, yet he does not say that. One of you leaves me with his charity under his arm, while it is Fire for him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you give him while you know it is Fire for him? He said: What shall I do? They ask me, and Allah refuses for me miserliness. In this narration: Mamar ibn Sulayman; in Dawud's narration: Mutamir ibn Sulayman; the correct is Mamar, and Allah knows best. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from Umar. Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid opposed, from al-Amash, from Atiyya, from Abu Said, from Umar. It is narrated from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Muawiya, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra. Abd Allah ibn Bishr narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umar, and Allah knows best the correct. It comes in the biography of Abu Said from Umar."
"98","Al-Harith ibn Amr al-Hudhali from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 105. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Ibn al-Munadi, he is Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, narrated to us; Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from al-Harith al-Hudhali, that Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ashari: The most rightful thing Muslims attend to is their religion. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray; I remembered of that what I remembered and forgot what I forgot. He prayed noon at midday heat and afternoon while the sun was alive. Al-Harith ibn Amr al-Hudhali: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him in his book without mentioning disparagement in him. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Barza."
"99","Al-Harith ibn Muawiya al-Kindi. 106. Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informs them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Mughira narrated to us; Safwan narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Muawiya al-Kindi, that he rode to Umar ibn al-Khattab asking him about three traits. He said: He arrived in Madina, and Umar asked him: What brought you? He said: To ask you about three traits. He said: What are they? He said: If I and the woman are in a narrow building and prayer comes: if I pray with her, she will be beside me; if she prays behind me, she leaves the building? Umar said: Screen between you and her with a garment, then pray beside you if you wish. And about the two rakats after afternoon? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me them. And about storytelling, for they wanted me for storytelling. He said: As you wish, as if disliking to forbid him. He said: I only wanted to end at your word. He said: I fear for you that you story-tell and rise over them in yourself, then story-tell and rise until it seems to you you are above them like the Pleiades, and Allah places you beneath their feet on the Day of Resurrection by that measure. As for prayer after afternoon, it is narrated in the Sahih from the narration of Ibn Abbas from Umar. The rest of the hadith is from Umar's statement."
"100","Haritha ibn Mudarrib from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 107. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib, who said: People of Syria came to Umar, saying: We have acquired wealth, horses and slaves, wishing to have in them zakat and purification. He said: What my two companions did before, I shall do. He consulted the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them Ali. Ali said: It is good, if it is not a jizya taken from them after you as regular. Haritha: Yahya ibn Main trusted him in al-Darimi's narration. Imam Ahmad said: Hasan al-hadith. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad the like, he said: I read upon Yahya ibn Said: Zuhayr; Abu Ishaq narrated to us; and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni narrated it in his book from al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar, from Abu Khaythama."
"101","Another. 108. ... ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan informed us in Nishapur that Wajih ibn Tahir informed them, by reading upon him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Musa informed us; Abu Yahya Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Harb informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us; Abd Allah ibn Hashim al-Tusi narrated to us; Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib al-Abdi, who said: Umar wrote to the people of Kufa: I have sent to you Ammar ibn Yasir as commander, and Abd Allah ibn Masud as teacher and minister. I preferred you with Ibn Umm Abd over myself. They are among the excellent of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of the people of Badr. Listen to them and obey."
"102","109. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr also informed us in Isfahan that Fatima bint Abd Allah informed him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib, who said: Umar wrote to the people of Kufa: I have sent Ammar as commander, and Abd Allah ibn Masud as teacher and minister. They are among the excellent of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of the people of Badr and Uhud. Follow them, listen to their word. I preferred you with Abd Allah over myself."
"103","110. ... Abu Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Qitrani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakhai narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, all from Abu Ishaq, from Haritha ibn Mudarrib... to Kufa: I have sent Ammar ibn Yasir and Abd Allah ibn Masud as teacher and minister. They are among the excellent of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Follow them, listen to their word. I preferred you with Abd Allah over myself, a preference."
"104","Hafsa bint Umar from her father, may Allah be pleased with them both. 111. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, by reading upon him in Isfahan, that Abu al-Wafa Mahmud ibn al-Hasan ibn Manda informed them, by reading upon him while he was present, and the Imam Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Manda by license: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Manda informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Umar ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani informed us, he said: It was read upon Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Hafiz Ibn al-Sunni in al-Dinawar: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sabbahi informed me; al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from his brother al-Numan, from Musab ibn Sad, from Hafsa, that she said to her father: Allah has increased good and widened provision; if you ate food softer than your food and better than your food, and wore a garment softer than your garment? He said: I shall dispute you to yourself. He said: He kept reminding her what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in and what she was with him, until he made her weep. He said: I told you I had two companions who took a path; if I take other than their path, I shall be taken other than their path. By Allah, I shall share with them their hard living, that I may attain with them their easy living. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his brother, unnamed, the like. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrates it, differing upon him. Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak and Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated it from Ismail, from his brother al-Numan, from Musab ibn Sad, from Hafsa. Abu Usama and Yazid ibn Harun opposed them, narrating it from Ismail, from Musab ibn Sad, without mentioning Ismail's brother between them. The statement of Ibn al-Mubarak and Muhammad ibn Bishr is more correct, and Allah knows best."
"105","Hanzal ibn Nuaym al-Anazi from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 112. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, with my reading upon him, on the western side of Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us; al-Muthanna ibn Awf al-Anazi, Basran, narrated to us, he said: al-Ghadban ibn Hanzala informed me that his father Hanzala ibn Nuaym came as delegation to Umar. When a man of the delegation passed Umar, he asked him: From whom is he? Until my father passed him, and he asked him: From whom are you? He said: From Anaza. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A tribe from here, wronged, victorious."
"106","113. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi also informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; Musa, he is Ibn Hayyan, narrated to us; Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, kunya Abu Ghadira al-Anazi, narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ghadban ibn Hanzala al-Anazi narrated to me, from his father Hanzala ibn Nuaym, who said: Imran ibn Isam came to him, saying: O Abu Rabah, what did the Commander of the Faithful Umar mention to you when you came to him among your people of Anaza? He said: I passed him, and he said: Who are you and from whom are you? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I am Hanzala ibn Nuaym al-Anazi. He said: Anaza? I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention your people one day. His Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Anaza? He pointed with his hand toward the east, saying: A tribe from here, wronged, victorious."
"107","114. With this chain Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan Abu Abd Allah al-Anazi narrated to us; Abu Ghadira Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ghadban ibn Hanzala narrated to me, from Abu Hanzala ibn Nuaym al-Anazi, Hanzala said: I was among those who came as delegation to Umar ibn al-Khattab. He began asking us man by man: Who are you, and from whom are you? Until he reached me, saying: Who are you and from whom are you? I said: I am Hanzala ibn Nuaym al-Anazi. He gestured with his hand toward the east, spread his fingers, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Anaza, a tribe from here, wronged, victorious."
"108","Khalid ibn Urfuta from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 115. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us; Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Khalifa ibn Qays, from Khalid ibn Urfuta, who said: I was sitting with Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, when a man of Abd al-Qays dwelling in al-Sus was brought. Umar said to him: Are you so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Abdi? He said: Yes. He said: Are you the one dwelling in al-Sus? He said: Yes. Umar struck him with a spear with him, saying: What is with me, O Commander of the Faithful? Umar said: Sit. He sat, and he recited upon him: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: Alif Lam Ra, those are the verses of the clear Book. We sent it down as an Arabic Quran that you may understand. We narrate to you the best of stories, to: among the heedless. He recited upon him thrice and struck him thrice. The man said to him: What is with me, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: Are you the one who copied the book of Daniel? He said: Command me with your command, I follow it. He said: Go and erase it with hot water and white wool, then do not read it nor teach it to anyone. If it reaches me that you read it or taught it to anyone, I shall punish you severely. Then he said to him: Sit. He sat before him, saying: I went and copied a book of the People of the Book, then brought it in leather. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this in your hand, O Umar? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a book I copied to increase our knowledge. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew angry until his cheeks reddened. Then it was called: Prayer in congregation. The Ansar said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is angered; weapons, weapons. They came until they surrounded the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O people, I have been given comprehensive speech and its seals; it was abridged for me. I have brought it to you white, pure. Do not be reckless, nor let the reckless deceive you. Umar said: I stood saying: I am pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and you as Messenger. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended. Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq: Muslim and Ibn Hibban produced for him."
"109","Abu Firas Rabi ibn Ziyad from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 116. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us; Mahdi narrated to us; Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Firas, who said: I witnessed Umar ibn al-Khattab addressing people, saying: O people, a time came upon me when I saw one who recited the Quran intending Allah and what is with Him. It seems to me that peoples recited it intending people by it and intending the world by it. Intend Allah by your deeds. We only knew you when revelation descended, with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among us, and when: Allah has informed us of your news. Revelation is cut, Allah's Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is gone. We only know you by what we say to you. Whoever we see good from, we think good of him and love him for it; whoever we see evil from, we think evil of him and hate him for it. Your secrets are between you and your Lord. I only send my workers to teach you your religion and teach you your sunna; I do not send them to strike your backs nor take your wealth. Whoever is doubted by anything of that, let him raise it to me. By Him in whose hand is Umar's soul, I shall retaliate you from him. He said: Amr ibn al-As rose, saying: O Commander of the Faithful, what if you sent a worker among your workers, and he disciplined a man of his subjects and struck him; would you retaliate him from him? He said: Yes. By Him in whose hand is Umar's soul, I shall retaliate from him. Shall I not retaliate, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) retaliate from himself? Do not strike Muslims, humiliating them; do not withhold their rights, disbelieving them; do not keep them in garrisons, trialing them; do not settle them in thickets, wasting them. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ismail, from al-Jurayri, the like."
"110","Zayd ibn Thabit Abi Said from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 117. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is al-Qawariri, narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us; Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, he is Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed from Kathir ibn al-Salt, who said: We were with Marwan, among us Zayd. Zayd said: We used to recite: The old man and old woman, stone them outright. Marwan said: Why did you not write it in the codex? He said: We mentioned that, among us Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: I shall satisfy you of that. He said: We said: How? He said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He mentioned such-and-such, mentioning stoning. He came to him, that man mentioned stoning, saying: O Messenger of Allah, write for me the verse of stoning. He said: I cannot now, this and the like. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Ghundar, from Shuba, from Qatada, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Kathir ibn al-Salt, from Zayd; and from Ismail ibn Masud, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, he said: I was informed from the nephew of Kathir ibn al-Salt, from Zayd; and it is said from Muhammad: I was informed from Kathir. Ibn Abbas narrated from Umar, he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, sent Muhammad with truth and sent down with him the Book. Among what He sent down upon him was the verse of stoning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and we stoned after him. This hadith is other than what we mentioned. Were it not for Shuba's narration, we would not have produced it, for Ibn Awn's narration is broken."
"111","Al-Saib ibn Yazid from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 118. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Haddad informed you, while you were present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us; Abu Bishr Ismail ibn Abd Allah al-Abdi narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Bukayr al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Yazid al-Nawfali, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in dawn prayer, shaking his head with water scattering from major ablution in Ramadan. I know I wrote this hadith only with this chain. Abd al-Malik ibn Yazid: al-Bukhari and Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him in their books. I fear he is Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik. I say: He is spoken about, for he narrates from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrates from him, and Allah knows best the correct of that."
"112","Abu Said Sad ibn Malik from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 119. Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abd Allah al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard so-and-so thank and speak good, claiming you gave him two dinars. He said: But so-and-so does not say that, though he received from me between a hundred and ten."
"113","120. Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us in it that Tamim ibn Abi Said informed them, by reading upon him: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us; Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us; Muhammad ibn Zuhayr Abu Yala narrated to us in al-Ubulla; Salm ibn Junada narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw so-and-so supplicate and mention good, mentioning you gave him two dinars. He said: But so-and-so I gave between such-and-such, yet he did not praise nor speak good. So Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it. Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated it from Umar."
"114","Suda bint Awf ibn Kharija ibn Sinan al-Murriyya, wife of Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, from Umar. 121. Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Tawus informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Ramadan of the year five hundred seventy-seven in Damascus, it was said to him: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami al-Mawazini informed you in the year five hundred thirteen, he said: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, he said: The judge Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayanaji informed us, he said: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, by reading upon him: Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad narrated to us, from Misar, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn Talha, from his mother Suda al-Murriyya."
"115","122. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ikhwa also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened, he said: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu al-Hasan al-Buhayri, I think him Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar, informed us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim al-Razi narrated to us; Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Misar. 123. Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib also informed us, by reading upon him while I listened, it was said to him: Abu al-Barakat Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Nahdi the Hanbali jurist informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Husayn Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Mihran informed us; Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us, by reading upon him, acknowledging it; Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us. 124. The Shaykh Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hibat Allah al-Ghazarani the grammarian also informed us, with my reading upon him in Baghdad, I said to him: Sitt al-Ikhwa bint Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed you, by reading upon her while you listened: Abu al-Husayn Asim ibn al-Hasan informed us; Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us; al-Husayn ibn Ismail narrated to us. 125. Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed us in it that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, by reading upon him while he listened: Abu Amr al-Musayyab ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab al-Arghiyani informed us; Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us, by reading upon him; the judge Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us; Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad narrated to us, from Misar, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn Talha, from his mother Suda al-Murriyya, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by Talha after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: What is with you downcast? Did your cousin's affair displease you? He said: No. But I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a word none says at death except it is light of the record, and his body and soul find rest by it at death. He said: I know it; it is what he offered his uncle. Had he known anything more saving for him than it, he would have commanded him with it. The wording of al-Musayyab's hadith from Ibn Mahdi. In Asim's narration: He said no, with: it is the word which. In Abu Yala's narration: What is with me seeing you downcast, does your cousin's affair displease you? He said: No, with: it is the word which, with: he would have commanded him with it, except it was light for him, with: it is the word he offered his uncle; had he known anything more saving for him than it, he would have commanded him. Ibn Maja narrated it in his Sunan. Al-Nasai in the book Deed of Day and Night from Harun ibn Ishaq the like. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Salm, from Harun ibn Ishaq."
"116","126. Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi the blind, may Allah have mercy on him, also informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad narrated to me, from Misar, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn Talha, from his mother Suda al-Murriyya, who said: Umar passed by Talha after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: What is with me seeing you downcast, does your cousin's affair displease you? He said: No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a word none says at death except it is light of the record, and his body and soul find rest by it at death. He said: I know it; it is what he offered his uncle. Had he known anything more saving for him than it, he would have commanded him with it."
"117","Sulayman ibn al-Rabi al-Adawi from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 127. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Samina al-Basri narrated to us; Abu Dawud Sulayman narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Ibn Burayda, from Sulayman ibn al-Rabi, from Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A party of my nation remains upon truth until the Hour rises. Abu Dawud, he is Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi, narrated it in his Musnad, saying in it: We met Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, saying: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us such-and-such. Umar said: Abd Allah ibn Amr knows best what he says. He said it thrice. We said: Then it was called: Prayer in congregation. People gathered to him, and Umar addressed them, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A party of my nation remains upon truth until Allah's command comes."
"118","128. The Hafiz Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us with it in his book that Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Ayyub ibn Ziyad al-Burji informed them, by reading upon him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us; Yunus ibn Habib informed us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from Sulayman ibn al-Rabi al-Adawi, who said: We met Umar ibn al-Khattab. Al-Bukhari narrated this hadith in al-Tarikh, saying: We do not know Qatada's hearing from Ibn Burayda, nor Ibn Burayda's from Sulayman. I say: Qatada narrated it from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, from Umar. This hadith has a witness in the Sahihayn from the hadith of Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan and al-Mughira ibn Shuba, and in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"119","Salim ibn Amir from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 129. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us; Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abd Allah al-Abdi narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us; Thabit ibn al-Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Amir al-Ansari say: I saw Umar not dye his gray at all, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grows a gray hair, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection, so I do not love to change my light. This Abu Amir's name is Salim ibn Amir. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He narrated from Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and Ammar ibn Yasir. Thabit ibn al-Ajlan narrated from him."
"120","130. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi also informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ziyadi al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Abu Bakr al-Warraq Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Balkhi, companion of Ahmad ibn Hanbal, narrated to us; al-Haytham ibn Kharija al-Baghdadi informed us; Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Thabit ibn al-Ajlan, from Sulaym ibn Amir, who said: I saw Abu Bakr dye with henna and katam, while Umar ibn al-Khattab did not dye. I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection, and I do not change it. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi, from al-Haytham ibn Kharija, who was called little Shuba."
"121","Sayyar ibn al-Marur from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 131. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us in it that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading upon him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us; Sallam, meaning Abu al-Ahwas, narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sayyar ibn al-Marur, who said: I heard Umar address, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) built this mosque, we with him, the Emigrants and Helpers. When crowding intensifies, a man among you prostrate upon his brother's back. He saw peoples praying in the road, saying: Pray in the mosque."
"122","132. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by reading upon him: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us; Abu Nuaym narrated to us; Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Sayyar ibn al-Marur, who said: I heard Umar addressing people: This mosque was built by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we with him, the Emigrants and Helpers. Pray in it; whoever among you finds no place to prostrate, let him prostrate upon his brother's back. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, saying: Simak ibn Harb narrates it from him. Abu al-Ahwas and Asbat ibn Nasr narrated it from Simak, agreeing it is Sayyar ibn Marur. Yahya ibn Main said: It is only Sayyar ibn Maghrur, with ghayn. I do not know whence he took this. This Sayyar is unknown; we know none narrated from him except Simak ibn Harb, nor know he raised a hadith other than this, and Allah knows best."
"123","Shurayh ibn al-Harith Abu Umayya the judge, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 133. Abu al-Mahasin Abd al-Razzaq ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Hamadhani informed us, in his book from Hamadhan, that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them, by reading upon him: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us; Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Abu Amir narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, from Shurayh: that he wrote to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asking him. He wrote to him: Judge by what is in Allah's Book; if not in Allah's Book, then by the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If not in Allah's Book nor the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), judge by what the righteous judged. If not in Allah's Book nor the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the righteous did not judge with it: if you wish, advance; if you wish, hold back. I see holding back only better for you. Peace."
"124","134. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah Shadhan informed us; Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us; Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, that Umar wrote to him: When something comes to you in Allah's Book, judge with it; men shall not overcome you in it. When what is not in Allah's Book, mighty and majestic, comes to you, look in the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and judge with it. If a matter not in Allah's Book, mighty and majestic, nor in the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), look at what people agreed upon and take it. If of what is not in Allah's Book, mighty and majestic, nor the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and none before you spoke in it, choose whichever of the two matters you wish: if you wish to exert your view and advance, advance; if you wish to hold back, hold back. Holding back is better for you."
"125","Al-Subayy ibn Mabad al-Taghlibi al-Kufi from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 135. al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali, known as Ibn al-Matush, informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading upon him: al-Husayn ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yahya narrated to us, from al-Amash; Shaqiq narrated to us; al-Subayy ibn Mabad narrated to me, a Christian man of Banu Taghlib, he said: I was Christian and accepted Islam, striving, sparing nothing. I entered ihram for Hajj and Umra. I passed al-Udhayb upon Salman ibn Rabia and Zayd ibn Suhan. One said: With both together? His companion said to him: Leave him, for he is more astray than his camel! He said: As if my camel were upon my neck. I came to Umar and mentioned that to him. Umar said: They said nothing; you were guided to your Prophet's sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sayyar narrated it from Abu Wail."
"126","136. Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir, Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi, and Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Misri informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Abi Mansur ibn Abi al-Fath al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading upon him while they listened: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Baqqal informed us; Abu Ahmad Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us; my grandfather Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us; Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Mani ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Hushaym narrated to us; Sayyar informed us, from Abu Wail, from al-Subayy ibn Mabad, that he was Christian then accepted Islam. He wanted jihad, but was told: Begin with Hajj. He came to Abu Musa, who commanded him to enter ihram for Hajj and Umra together. While entering ihram for them, he passed Salman ibn Rabia and Zayd ibn Suhan. One said to his companion: This is more astray than his family's camel. Al-Subayy ibn Mabad heard it, distressing him. He came to Umar and mentioned that to him. He said: You were guided to your Prophet's sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard him another time say: You were granted your Prophet's sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hushaym, from Sayyar."
"127","137. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Ubayd Allah, he is al-Qawariri, narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba, from al-Subayy ibn Mabad, that he entered ihram for Hajj and Umra. He mentioned that to Umar, who said: You were guided to your Prophet's sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He narrated it from al-Hakam and from al-Amash, both from Abu Wail. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shuba, from al-Hakam, and at its end al-Hakam said: I said to Abu Wail: Did al-Subayy narrate to you? He said: Yes. He narrated it from Sufyan, from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba, and at its end Abda said: Abu Wail said: Often I and Masruq went to al-Subayy asking him about it. He narrated it from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Abu Wail. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Uthman ibn Abi Shayba, from Jarir, from Mansur, from Abu Wail. Ibn Maja narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Hisham ibn Ammar, from Sufyan, from Abda; and from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki, Abu Muawiya al-Darir, and Yala ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi, from al-Amash. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Jarir; and from Ishaq also, from Musab ibn al-Miqdam, from Zaida, from Mansur; and from Imran ibn Yazid, from Said ibn Ishaq; and from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan, from Hajjaj, all from Ibn Jurayj, from Hasan ibn Muslim, from Mujahid, from a man of Iraq called Shaqiq, the like. Ibn Hibban narrated it from Musaddad, from Ibn Uyayna, from Abda. Abu al-Hasan was asked about the hadith of al-Subayy ibn Mabad, saying: Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, Sulayman al-Amash, al-Hakam ibn Utayba, Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, Habib ibn Abi Thabit, Amr ibn Murra, Mughira ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl, Habib ibn Hassan, Sayyar, Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhita, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, and Mujahid ibn Jabr narrated it from Abu Wail. At its end he said something good none other mentioned: Abu Wail said: I and Masruq ibn al-Ajda would visit al-Subayy ibn Mabad reminding him this hadith. At the end of his speech he said: It is a sahih hadith. The best in chain is the hadith of Mansur and al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from al-Subayy, from Umar."
"128","Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, wife of Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 138. Abu Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Hurdi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by reading upon him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ziyadi al-Khalili informed us; Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Shuayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us; Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi, from his father, from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, that she heard Umar ibn al-Khattab upon the pulpit say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever comes to a diviner, no prayer is accepted from him forty nights. In our hearing from Abu Bakr, from Nafi, from his father, I think it error; the correct is what was written, and Allah knows best. Al-Haytham also narrated it from al-Abbas al-Duri, from Ibrahim ibn Hamza ibn Muhammad ibn Hamza ibn Muayqib ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Nafi, from his father, from Safiyya, from Umar."
"129","With this chain from Abd al-Aziz, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"130","Talha ibn Ubayd Allah al-Taymi Abu Muhammad, one of the ten, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 139. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in al-Harbiyya, it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us; Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Asbat narrated to us; Mutarrif narrated to us, from Amir, from Yahya ibn Talha, from his father, who said: Umar saw Talha ibn Ubayd Allah heavy, saying: What is with you, O so-and-so, perhaps your cousin's command displeased you, O so-and-so? He said: No. I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith; nothing prevented me asking him about it except ability over it until he died. I heard him say: I know a word none says at death except his color brightens for it, and Allah relieves his distress. Umar said: I know what it is! He said: What is it? He said: Do you know a word greater than a word with which he commanded his uncle at death: There is no god but Allah. Talha said: You spoke truth. By Allah, it is it."
"131","140. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi also informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us; Abu Zubayd Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; Mutarrif narrated to us, from Amir, from Yahya ibn Talha, who said: Umar saw Talha ibn Ubayd Allah grieved, saying: What is with you? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a word none says at death except he is relieved and his color brightens for it, and he sees what pleases him. Nothing prevented me asking him about it except ability over it. Umar said: I know what it is. Talha said: What is it? He said: Do you know a word better than a word to which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called his uncle at death? Talha said: By Allah, it is it. Umar said: There is no god but Allah. So he narrated it, not saying: Yahya from his father. Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it in his Musnad from Asad ibn Amr, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Amir, from Yahya ibn Talha, from Talha. Al-Nasai narrated it in the book Deed of Day and Night from Ali ibn Hujr, from Ali ibn Mushir, from Mutarrif, he is Ibn Tarif, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn Talha, from his father, that Umar saw him gloomy and mentioned it."
"132","Abu al-Aswad Zalim ibn Amr ibn Sufyan al-Dayli from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 141. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Khaythama narrated to us; Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dayli, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed on Friday, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: A party of my nation remains upon truth until Allah's command comes to it. Sulayman ibn al-Rabi al-Adawi narrated it from Umar."
"133","142. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi also informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Abu Said, he is Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, narrated to us; Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dayli, who said: I and Zura ibn Damra went with al-Ashari, meeting Abd Allah ibn Amr. I sat at his right, Zura at his left. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: Soon none of the non-Arabs remains in Arab land except killed or captive, judged in his blood. Zura ibn Damra said to him: Will polytheists prevail over Muslims? He said: From whom are you? He said: From Banu Amir ibn Sasa. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: The Hour will not rise until the shoulders of Banu Amir ibn Sasa crowd at Dhu al-Khalasa, a structure or house named in ignorance. He said: We mentioned Abd Allah ibn Amr's statement to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said thrice: Abd Allah knows best what he says. He said: Umar addressed on Friday, saying: Allah's Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: A party of my nation remains upon truth, victorious, until Allah's command comes. He said: We mentioned Umar's statement to Abd Allah ibn Amr. He said: Allah's Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke truth; when that comes, what I said will be."
"134","Amir ibn Rabia al-Anazi, ally of Banu Adi, among those who witnessed Badr, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 143. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal and Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon them while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; al-Qawariri and Abu Khaythama narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabia, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umra, for following between them removes poverty and sins as the bellows removes dross of iron. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabia, from Umar, without saying: from his father."
"135","144. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: The Imam Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Shurayh ibn Miqal al-Shashi informed us; Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow Hajj with Umra, for following between them removes poverty and sins as the bellows removes dross of iron. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni was asked about this hadith, saying: Ibn Uyayna narrated it, clarifying the confusion in the chain is from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, not from who narrated from him. As for Ubayd Allah ibn Umar's narration from Asim: Zuhayr, Ibn Numayr, Abda ibn Sulayman, Abu Hafs al-Abbar, Abu Badr, and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated it from Ubayd Allah, agreeing upon one statement, raising it from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, from Umar. Ali ibn Mushir, Abu Usama, and Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi opposed them, narrating it from Ubayd Allah without mentioning Amir ibn Rabia in the chain. Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated it from Asim, perfecting its chain, clarifying Asim was confused in it: sometimes dropping a man from its chain, sometimes adding, sometimes stopping it upon Umar. Ibn Uyayna said: Most of that he said it from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Asim ibn Ubayd Allah is not a preserver. He mentioned much other disagreement in it. Abu Abd Allah Ibn Maja narrated it in his Sunan from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba, from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from his father, from Umar; and from Abu Bakr, from Ibn Uyayna, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Amir, from Umar, without saying: from his father."
"136","Aisha bint Abi Bakr from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. 145. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sufi informed them, by reading upon him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Asim informed us; Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Uways narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that Umar said to Abu Bakr: No, rather we pledge you, while you are our master, our best, and our most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"137","146. The Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghanayim al-Ansari the preacher also informed us, on the street between Cairo and Egypt, I said to him: Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Azdi informed us; Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Jarrahi al-Marwazi informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub al-Mahbubi informed us; Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawra al-Tirmidhi informed us; Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us; Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: Abu Bakr is our master, our best, and our most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Isa said: This is a sahih gharib hadith. Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, from Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari."
"138","Another. 147. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by reading upon him: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; Umar ibn Said ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to us, from Dhakwan, freedman of Aisha, from Aisha, that a small box was brought to Umar ibn al-Khattab. His companions looked at it, not knowing its value. He said: Do you permit me to send it to Aisha, due to the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) love of her? They said: Yes. It was brought to Aisha, and she opened it. It was said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sent it to you. She said: What was opened upon Ibn al-Khattab after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? O Allah, leave none to receive his gift after."
"139","Abd Allah ibn Unays from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. 148. Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, by reading upon him in Isfahan, it was said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba informed us; Harmala ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Amr, he is Ibn al-Harith, informed me that Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn... narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to him that he and Umar ibn al-Khattab mentioned charity of spoils one day. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when mentioning misappropriation of charity: whoever misappropriates a camel or sheep from it comes with it on the Day of Resurrection carrying it? Abd Allah ibn Unays said: Yes. Abu Abd Allah Ibn Maja narrated it from Amr ibn Sawwad al-Misri, from Ibn Wahb."
"140","Abd Allah ibn Habib al-Sulami Abu Abd al-Rahman from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. 149. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, by reading upon him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us; Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us; Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharaza al-Kufi narrated to us; Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, from Misar, from Abu Hasin, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Umar turned to people, saying: O people, knees are sunnated for you; hold the knees."
"141","150. Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi also informed us, by reading upon him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Your father informed you; Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Sarifini informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Habban informed us, by reading upon him: Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us; Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us; Shuba informed us, from Abu Hasin, he said: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami say: Umar said: Hold; knees are sunnated for you. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Hasin, saying: A hasan sahih hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu Dawud, from Shuba, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman; and from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Sufyan, from Abu Hasin, he said: Umar said: The sunna is only taking the knees. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni was asked about it, saying: A group narrated it, among them Shuba. Differing upon him: Abu Qutayba narrated it from Shuba, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Umar, erring in it. Abu Dawud narrated it from Shuba, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Umar, not followed upon it. The preserved is the hadith of Abu Hasin."
"142","Abd Allah ibn Khalifa from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. 151. Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwa informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading upon him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Khalifa, from Umar, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Supplicate Allah to admit me to Paradise. He said: He magnified the Lord, blessed and exalted, saying: His Kursi extends over the heavens and earth, and it creaks like the creaking of a new saddle when ridden, from His weight."
"143","152. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, with my reading upon him in Isfahan, I said to him: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading upon him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Ismail ibn Salim al-Sayigh narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Khalifa, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Supplicate Allah to admit me to Paradise. He said: He magnified the Lord, saying: His Throne is above seven heavens, and it creaks like the creaking of a new saddle when ridden, from His weight."
"144","153. Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad also informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail informed them, by reading upon him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Khalifa, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Supplicate Allah to admit me to Paradise. He magnified the Lord, then said: His Kursi extends over the heavens and earth, and He sits upon it, with four fingers excess from it. Then he said with his fingers, joining them: And it creaks like the creaking of a new saddle when ridden, from His weight. Shuba narrated it from Abu Ishaq."
"145","154. Abd Allah al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad, he said: Ghalib ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Banna informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Qadi narrated to us; Said ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Salm ibn Qutayba narrated to us; Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Khalifa, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah's mercy upon him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His statement: Upon the Throne He rose: He said: Until a creaking is heard like the creaking of a saddle."
"146","Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, 155 - Imam Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Lanjani informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Baghban informed you, by recitation to him: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tayyan informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshid informed us: Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur Zaj narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us: Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr delivering a sermon, saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab delivering a sermon, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, and he said: Honor my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then lying will appear, until a man will testify though he is not asked to testify, and a man will swear though he is not asked to swear. Whoever among you loves the middle of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the single one and is farther from two. No man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."
"147","156 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is grieved by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is the believer."
"148","157 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Shuja al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Isa ibn Ahmad al-Asqalani narrated to us: Shabbabah narrated to us: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to me, from Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn Zubayr, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed us at al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as I stand among you, and said: Honor my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then lying will spread until a man swears though he is not asked to swear, and testifies before he is asked to testify. Whoever is pleased to attain the middle of Paradise, upon him is the community, for the Hand of Allah is with the community, and Satan is with the single one and is farther from two. No man should be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. And whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abdul-Malik ibn Umayr. We have mentioned the disagreement concerning it in the hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah from Umar. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the narration of Suwayd ibn Ghafalah that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed at al-Jabiyah and said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk except for a space of two or three or four fingers. So Umar's sermon at al-Jabiyah is thus established, and each person among those present retained something of his sermon. And Allah knows best."
"149","Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had al-Laythi al-Hijazi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 158 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Uthman ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, from Zama'ah ibn Salih, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be modest, for Allah is not shy of the truth; and do not approach women in their backs. Al-Nasai narrated it from Said ibn Yaqub al-Talaqani, from Uthman ibn al-Yaman with his chain. He also narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Yazid ibn Abi Hakim, from Zamaah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement in this hadith and said: the statement of Uthman ibn al-Yaman is the most correct of them. And Allah knows best."
"150","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah al-Anazi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, 159 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Hurdi al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us, by recitation to him while we heard in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi, that is Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, he said: I witnessed Umar ibn al-Khattab when Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to him wearing a shirt of silk, and Umar said to him: Leave this off you, or remove this, for he mentioned, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Whoever wears silk and brocade in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks in vessels of gold and silver in this world will not drink in them in the Hereafter. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I hope to wear it in this world and the Hereafter. As for the mention of silk, it has been narrated in the two Sahihs from the narration of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from Umar."
"151","Another, 160 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, narrating from Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Sufyan once said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for following up between them removes poverty and sins as the bellows removes impurity. It has already come in the hadith of Amir ibn Rabiah from Umar."
"152","Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, 161 - Abul-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nuqur informed us: Abul-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Akhi Mimiyy informed us: Abdullah, that is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi, narrated to us: Uthman, that is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya informed us, from Salih al-Hamadhani. 162 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us: Yusuf ibn Buhlul informed us. 163 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us. 164 - And my maternal uncle, Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Abul-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi informed them, by recitation to him in Baghdad: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim al-Narsi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Buhlul narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Abu Salih ibn Salih, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah, then took her back. And Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban said in his narration: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had divorced Hafsah, then took her back."
"153","165 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Fath Ismail ibn al-Fadl al-Sarraj informed you, by recitation to him while you were present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Furak al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us: Abu al-Shatha and Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Salih, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah then took her back. Abu Dawud narrated it from Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Askari, from Yahya ibn Zakariyya. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abdah ibn Abdullah, from Yahya ibn Adam, and from Amr ibn Mansur, from Abu Said Sahl ibn Muhammad, he said: I was informed, from Yahya ibn Zakariyya. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah, Suwayd ibn Said, and Masruq ibn al-Marzuban, from Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Durayj, from Masruq ibn al-Marzuban, from Ibn Abi Zaidah."
"154","Another, 166 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi and Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to each of them: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah informed us: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: You have known that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it in the last ten, on the odd nights. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Husayn ibn Ali, from Zaidah, from Asim. Abu Yala also narrated it from Abu Khaythamah, from Muawiyah ibn Amr, from Zaidah, from Asim. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it in his Musnad from al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Duri, from al-Husayn al-Jufi, from Zaidah, from Asim. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Umar and the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"155","167 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, he said: My father said: and I narrated it to Ibn Abbas, he said: What pleased you of that? When Umar used to invite the elders among the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would invite me with them, and he said: Do not speak until they speak. He said: He invited us one day or one night and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning Laylat al-Qadr what you have known, so seek it in the last ten, on the odd nights; in which of the odd nights do you see it?"
"156","Another, 168 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Sufi al-Harawi informed us, with my recitation to him in Herat, I said to him: Abul-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abu Said Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather, Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us: Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Utbah ibn Abi Utbah, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abbas: that it was said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Narrate to us about the course of the hour of hardship. Umar said: We went out to Tabuk in severe heat, and we stopped at a camp where thirst struck us until we thought our necks would break, until a man would go seeking water and not return until he thought his neck would break, until a man would slaughter his camel and squeeze its dung and drink it, and put what remained on his liver. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate for us. He said: Do you wish that? He said: Yes. He raised his hands and did not bring them back until the sky spoke and clouded over, then poured, and they filled all they had with them. Then we went to look, and we did not find it had passed beyond the army. Imam Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salm, from Harmalah ibn Yahya, from Ibn Wahb. I say: its men from Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala to Umar, Muslim has narrated from them in his Sahih. Abul-Hasan al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ahmad ibn Salih and Yunus narrated it from Ibn Wahb with this chain, and Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri differed from them and narrated it from Ibn Wahb without mentioning Utbah in the chain, making it from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Nafi ibn Jubayr; and the statement is the statement of whoever mentioned Utbah ibn Abi Utbah, and he is Utbah ibn Muslim."
"157","169 - And Shaykh Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Muaddib informed us of it, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani al-Muaddil informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Malik narrated to us: Abul-Ahwas Muhammad ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: that Amr ibn al-Harith informed him, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Utbah ibn Abi Utbah, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Abbas: that it was said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Narrate to us a hadith about the course of hardship. Umar said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Tabuk in severe heat, and we stopped at a camp where thirst struck us until we thought our necks would break, until a man would go seeking water and then not return until we thought his neck would break, and until a man would slaughter his camel and squeeze its dung, and put what remained on his liver. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate for us. He said: Do you wish that? He said: Yes. He raised his hands and did not bring them back until it inclined and clouded over, then poured, and they filled all they had with them. Then we went to look, and we did not find it had passed beyond the army."
"158","Another, 170 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Nuh narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar al-Ijli narrated to us: Simak Abu Zumayl narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, like the hadith of Umar ibn Yunus in the story of Badr; and Abu Nuh added in his hadith, he said: When the day of Uhud came the next year, they were requited for what they did on the day of Badr in taking ransom: seventy of them were killed, and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fled from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his front tooth (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was broken, and the helmet was crushed on his head, and blood flowed on his face, and Allah Almighty revealed: When a disaster befell you though you had inflicted twice as much, you said: Whence is this? Say: It is from yourselves; indeed Allah is over all things Capable, for your taking ransom. Muslim did not produce this addition, though he narrated by way of Umar ibn Yunus from Ikrimah a long hadith in the story of Badr. Abu Nuh's name is Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan; al-Bukhari produced from him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Nuh."
"159","171 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Shukr al-Muaddib informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Masud narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah and Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah said: from Abu Zumayl, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: On the day of Badr captives were taken, and he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Asim added: Then spoils were made lawful for them. The next year at Uhud they were requited for what they did: seventy of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were killed and seventy taken captive, and his front tooth was broken, and the helmet was crushed off his head, and blood flowed on his face, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fled and climbed the mountain, and Allah revealed: When a disaster befell you though you had inflicted twice as much, to His saying: Knowing of what you do, then He sent down upon you after distress security."
"160","Another, 172 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr, Hashim ibn al-Qasim, narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal: Zuhayr ibn Hayyan narrated to us, and he used to visit Ibn Abbas and heard from him, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Umar invited me, and there was a mat before him with gold scattered on it like the scattering of handfuls. Ibn Abbas said: Do you know what handfuls are? He mentioned ore. He said: Come and divide among your people. By Allah, I know not, when He withheld this from His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and gave it to me, did He intend good for me or evil? He said: I was dividing, and I heard weeping, and it was Umar weeping, saying in his weeping: No, by Him who sent him with the truth, He did not withhold this from His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and from Abu Bakr intending evil for them, and give it to Umar intending good for him."
"161","Another, 173 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Bundar ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abu Dawud, author of al-Tayalisah, narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Uthman al-Makhzumi, he said: I saw Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, and he said: I saw my maternal uncle Ibn Abbas kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, and he said: I saw Umar kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it. As for kissing the Stone, it has been narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Umar by other paths; we intended here only the prostration upon it."
"162","Another, 174 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Umar ibn Yunus al-Hanafi narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us: Abu Zumayl narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah wrote to the people of Makkah, and Allah informed His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it, so he sent Ali and al-Zubayr after the letter, and they caught the woman on a camel and extracted it from her braids, and brought it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was read to him. He sent to Hatib and said: O Hatib, did you write this letter? He said: Yes. He said: What carried you to that? He said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I am indeed sincere to Allah and His Messenger, but I was a stranger among the people of Makkah, and my family were among them, and I feared for them, so I wrote a letter that harms neither Allah nor His Messenger, and perhaps there would be benefit in it for my family. Umar said: I drew my sword and said: O Messenger of Allah, let me have Hatib, for he has disbelieved, that I may strike his neck. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O son of al-Khattab, what informs you? Perhaps Allah looked upon this band of the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"163","175 - And Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, by recitation to him while we heard in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed you: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ziyadi al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: Musa ibn Masud Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abu Zumayl, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah wrote to the polytheists, and he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Hatib, what called you to what you did? He said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My family were among them, and I feared they would raid them, so I said: I will write a letter that harms neither Allah nor His Messenger. Umar said: I drew the sword and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I strike his neck, for he has disbelieved? He said: O son of al-Khattab, what informs you? Perhaps Allah looked upon this band of the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"164","176 - And Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili informed us, by recitation to him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn al-Zaghuni informed you, he said: Abul-Qasim Yahya ibn Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sisi informed us, he said: It was read to Shaykh Abu Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Harith al-Tamimi while I heard: Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Salm narrated to us: Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Basri narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abu Zumayl, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"165","177 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us: that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Amr Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Muslim narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abu Zumayl, from Ibn Abbas: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of Hatib, for he has disbelieved. He said: What informs you, O son of al-Khattab? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you. The wording of both is one, except that Abd al-Malik said: has looked towards the people of Badr. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr al-Humaydi mentioned that al-Barqani said: Muslim produced this hadith; he said: neither Abu Masud al-Dimashqi nor Khalaf al-Wasiti mentioned it in al-Atraf. I say: nor have we seen it in Sahih Muslim."
"166","Another, 178 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Ahmad, known as Ibn al-Saffar, informed us, with my recitation to him in Nishapur, I said to him: Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, he said: Abu Said Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated to us: Ayyash ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Abd al-Ala narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, he said: I said: O company of Ansar, O company of Muslims, the most entitled of people to the affair of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the second of the two when they were in the cave, is Abu Bakr, the foremost, the firm. Then I took his hand, and a man of the Ansar beat me to it and struck his hand before I struck his hand, then I struck his hand and the people followed. And it was said: Bashir ibn Sad al-Ansari Abu al-Numan was the first to pledge allegiance to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq."
"167","Another, 179 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Khazzaz narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Isa narrated to us: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that he heard Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out at midday and found Abu Bakr in the mosque, and said: What brought you out at this hour? He said: What brought you out brought me out, O Messenger of Allah. And Umar ibn al-Khattab came, and he said: O son of al-Khattab, what brought you out? He said: What brought you two out brought me out, O Messenger of Allah. Umar sat, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began narrating to us, then said: Have you two strength to go to these palms and get food and drink and shade? We said: Yes. He said: Take us to the house of Ibn al-Tayyihan, Abi al-Haytham al-Ansari. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went ahead of us, greeted and sought permission three times, while Umm al-Haytham behind the door heard the speech and wished the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would increase her greeting. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to leave, Umm al-Haytham came out hurrying after them and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah I heard your greeting, but I wished you would increase us of your greeting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said good to her, and said: Where is Abu al-Haytham? I do not see him. She said: He is near; he went to fetch us sweet water. Enter, for he will come soon, Allah willing. She spread for them a mat under a tree. Abu al-Haytham came, rejoicing at them, his eyes delighted with them, and climbed a palm and cut for them clusters. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enough, O Aba al-Haytham. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you will eat of its unripe dates and its ripe dates and its tadhnub. Then he brought them water and they drank over it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is of the bliss you will be asked about. Abu al-Haytham stood to slaughter a sheep for them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Beware the milch one. Umm al-Haytham stood kneading and baking for them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar laid their heads for the midday rest. They awoke with their food ready, it was placed before them, they ate and were satisfied and praised Allah, and Umm al-Haytham returned to them the rest of the clusters, and they ate of its ripe dates and tadhnub. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) greeted them and supplicated for them. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah. Abdullah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz: Abu Zurah al-Razi said: rejected in hadith; al-Tirmidhi and Abu Hatim ibn Hibban produced from him. I say: if this story is sound, their narration from Umar is more entitled, for he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Allah knows best."
"168","Another, 180 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by recitation to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Jawhari, brother of Abu Mamar, narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sent to me inviting me to suhur, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it the blessed morning meal. Al-Tabarani said: It is not narrated from Umar except by this path, and we know none who narrated it from Ibn Uyaynah except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, brother of Abu Mamar."
"169","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from his father, may Allah be pleased with them both, 181 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abul-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he sought his permission for Umrah, and he permitted him, and said: O my little brother, do not forget us in your supplication. And he said afterwards in Madinah: O my little brother, include us in your supplication. Umar said: I would not love to have for it all upon which the sun rose, for his saying: O my little brother."
"170","182 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi and Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: al-Qawariri narrated to us: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that Umar sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Umrah, and he permitted him, and said: O my little brother, include us in your righteous supplication."
"171","183 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muslim narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr and Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: Shubah informed us: Asim ibn Ubaydullah informed us, from Salim, from his father, from Umar: that he sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for an Umrah, and he permitted him and said: Do not forget us, O my little brother, in your supplication. He said: He said to him a word that would not please me to have the world for it. Shubah said: I met Asim in Madinah and he narrated it to me, and said: Include us, O my little brother, in your supplication."
"172","184 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us: that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us: Asim ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Umar: that he sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for an Umrah, and he permitted him and said: Do not forget us, O my little brother, of your supplication. He said to me a word that would not please me to have the world for it. Shubah said: Then I met Asim afterwards in Madinah and he narrated it to me, and said in it: Include us, O my little brother, in your supplication. Abu Dawud produced it from Sulayman ibn Harb from Shubah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Sufyan ibn Waki from his father from Sufyan from Asim, and said: a fair sound hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr from Waki from Sufyan in part."
"173","Another, 185 - Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar addressed us at al-Jabiyah and said: O people, I stood among you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, and said: I counsel you with my Companions, then those who come after them, then lying will spread until a man swears though he is not asked to swear, and the witness testifies though he is not asked to testify. No man should be alone with a woman but Satan is the third of them. Upon you is the community. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed, those are the believer. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Ali ibn Ishaq from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ibn Suqah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and said: a fair sound strange hadith by this path; Ibn al-Mubarak has narrated it from Ibn Suqah. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham al-Baghdadi from al-Nadr ibn Ismail similarly, and from Safwan ibn Umar from Musa ibn Ayyub from Ata ibn Muslim from Muhammad ibn Suqah from Abu Salih, he said: Umar came, and he mentioned it. And from al-Rabi ibn Sulayman ibn Dawud from Ishaq ibn Bakr from his father from Ibn al-Had from Ibn Dinar from Ibn Shihab: that when Umar came to Sham he mentioned the like. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Hibban ibn Musa from Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, from Ibn Suqah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-Nadr ibn Ismail, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak and al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated it from Muhammad ibn Suqah from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Ibn Umar from Umar; and Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had differed from them and narrated it from Abdullah ibn Dinar from al-Zuhri: that Umar addressed, and it is the correct. It has already come in Jabir ibn Samurah and Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from Umar."
"174","Another, 186 - Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Azhar ibn Sinan informed us: Muhammad ibn Wasi narrated to us, he said: I came to Makkah and my brother, son of Abdullah ibn Umar, met me, and narrated to me from his father from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters the market and says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is dominion and His is praise; He gives life and death, and He is Living, never dying; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Capable, there will be written for him a thousand thousand good deeds, and erased from him a thousand thousand evil deeds, and raised for him a thousand thousand ranks."
"175","187 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Azhar ibn Sinan informed us: Muhammad ibn Wasi narrated to us, he said: I came to Makkah and met there Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, and he narrated to me from his father from his grandfather Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever enters the market and says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is dominion and His is praise; He gives life and death, and He is Living, never dying; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Capable, Allah will write for him a thousand thousand good deeds and raise for him a thousand thousand ranks, or he said: and build for him a house in Paradise. He said: I came to Khurasan and went to Qutaybah ibn Muslim and said: I brought you a gift, and narrated the hadith to him. Qutaybah would ride in his procession until he came to the market and said it, then leave."
"176","188 - Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us, by recitation to him while we heard, it was said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you by ijazah: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Khallad informed us: al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Azhar ibn Sinan al-Qurashi informed us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, he said: I came to Makkah and met there Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he narrated to me from his father from his grandfather Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever enters the market and says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is dominion and His is praise; He gives life and death, and He is Living, never dying; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Capable, Allah will write for him a thousand thousand good deeds, and erase from him a thousand thousand evil deeds, and raise for him a thousand thousand ranks, and a house will be built for him in Paradise. He said: I came to Khurasan and went to Qutaybah ibn Muslim, I said: I brought you a gift, and narrated the hadith to him, and he would ride in his procession and say it, then leave. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Said from Hammad ibn Zayd from Amr ibn Dinar, freedman of Al al-Zubayr, from Salim from his father from Umar. Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah mentioned that Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, but I have not seen it in his Musnad; it may be that he narrated it elsewhere than the Musnad. And Allah knows best. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani and from Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi from Hammad ibn Zayd and al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman from Amr ibn Dinar, steward of Al al-Zubayr, from Salim, and said: a strange hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bishr ibn Muadh al-Darir from Hammad ibn Zayd from Amr, and from Ali ibn Muhammad from Waki from Kharijah ibn Musab from Abu Yahya Amr ibn Dinar, without mentioning Umar in its chain. Al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Abu Bakr Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Faqih and Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi from al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah from Yazid ibn Harun."
"177","Another, 189 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Hurdi al-Harawi informed us, by recitation to him while we heard in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abu Qilabah Abdul-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hafsah: Do not tell anyone; the mother of Ibrahim is forbidden to me. She said: Do you forbid what Allah made lawful for you? He said: By Allah, I will not approach her. He said: He did not approach her until she told Aishah, and Allah Almighty revealed: Allah has ordained for you the dissolution of your oaths."
"178","190 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abi Bakr, that is Ibn Ubaydullah al-Umari, narrated to us: Salim narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding us to wipe over the leather socks for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night. Khalid ibn Abi Bakr: al-Daraqutni said: he is not strong."
"179","191 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over his leather socks while traveling. Sharik followed him, from Asim. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Sharik from Asim ibn Ubaydullah. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Dawud. Qabisah ibn Uqbah and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated it from Hasan ibn Salih."
"180","192 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us: that Umar al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the leather socks with water while traveling. Al-Haytham also narrated it from Abu Abdah al-Sari ibn Yahya from Qabisah from Uqbah."
"181","Another, 193 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad informed us: Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ubaydullah, that is Ibn Umar, narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah. Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ubaydullah ibn Umar from Nafi from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bukhari narrated it from Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan from Abu Usamah from Ubaydullah, from the hadith of Ibn Umar."
"182","Another, 194 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by recitation to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Qurashi narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I placed my minbar upon a stream of the streams of Paradise. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Muadh al-Qurashi al-Basri narrated from Malik ibn Anas, Uthman ibn Talhah al-Qurashi and his father; my father heard from him in the days of al-Ansari, and Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Ghubari narrated from him, and he mentioned no disparagement in him."
"183","Another, 195 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us, by recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and al-Hajjaj said: I heard Shubah, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar: that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Have you seen what we act in, is it a matter already concluded or a thing begun anew or an invented matter? He said: In what has been concluded. Umar said: Shall we then rely? He said: Act, O son of al-Khattab, for each is facilitated. Whoever is of the people of felicity acts for felicity, and whoever is of the people of wretchedness acts for wretchedness."
"184","196 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi informed us, by recitation to him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi, that is Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Asim ibn Ubaydullah informed me: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: Have you seen what we act in, in a matter already concluded or a begun or invented matter? He said: In what has been concluded. Umar said: Shall we then rely? He said: Act, O son of al-Khattab, for each is facilitated for what he was created for. Whoever is of the people of felicity acts for felicity, and whoever is of the people of wretchedness acts for wretchedness. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ali ibn Abi Talib. Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it in his Musnad from Ubaydullah from Ibn Mahdi from Shubah similarly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar from Ibn Mahdi from Shubah from Asim from Salim from his father, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, making it of the Musnad of Ibn Umar, and said: a fair sound hadith. I say: much of the hadith of Ibn Umar in the two Sahih books is narrated..."
"185","197 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by recitation to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn Khallad informed us, by the selection of al-Daraqutni: Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, as in our hearing, though it is really Ibn Abi al-Sari: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abu Amr ibn al-Ala informed us: al-Walid ibn al-Simt narrated to us: Asim ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me: that Salim narrated to him from his father: that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Act upon what has been concluded, for each is facilitated for what he was created for. Whoever was created for Paradise is facilitated to the deeds of the people of Paradise, and whoever was created for the Fire is facilitated to the deeds of the people of the Fire. Asim said: O son of my brother, by Allah, Salim narrated to me that his father narrated to him that he heard from Umar, who heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"186","Another, 198 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, from Abdullah ibn Yasar al-Araj: that he heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrating from his father from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that he would say, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not enter Paradise: the disobedient to his parents, the dayyuth, and the masculine woman. The brother of Ismail, his name is Abd al-Hamid. This hadith, like the one before it, some narrated from the hadith of Umar, and some from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from the hadith of Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abdullah, from his brother Umar ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, freedman of Ibn Umar. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali from Yazid ibn Zuray from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Umari from Abdullah ibn Yasar, meaning al-Araj al-Madani, from Salim from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah from Yazid ibn Mawhab from Ibn Wahb from Umar ibn Muhammad, of the hadith of Umar."
"187","Another, 199 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, by recitation to him while we heard at al-Harbiyyah, it was said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yaqub narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Nafi, his freedman, narrated to me from him, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar would say: If a man has but one garment, let him wrap his waist with it, then pray; for I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying that, and saying: Do not wrap yourselves in the garment when it is single as the Jews do. Nafi said: If I told you he attributed that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I hope I would not have lied."
"188","200 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Ismail ibn Ishaq Abu Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Umar came in while I was praying in a waist-wrapper, and said: Were you not given two garments? I said: Yes. He said: What if I sent you on an errand, would you go as you prayed? I said: No. He said: Your Lord is more entitled to be adorned for. Then he narrated, and I know not whether he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or narrated from Umar, Nafi doubted, he said: If one of you has but one garment and wishes to pray, let him gird his loins with it, and not wrap as the Jews wrap."
"189","Another, 201 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, with my recitation to him, I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Said, that is freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah: that he was with Maslamah ibn Abd al-Malik in the land of Rum, and plundered war-booty was found in a man's goods, and he asked Salim ibn Abdullah. He said: Abdullah narrated to me, from Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find plunder in his goods, burn it. He said: and I think he said: and beat him. He said: He brought out his goods in the market. He said: He found therein a mushaf, and asked Salim, and he said: Sell it and give its price in charity. And it was narrated from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"190","202 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Muhammad ibn Muadh ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad Abu Zakariyya al-Madani narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you find has plundered, burn his goods. He said: Salim was with us in a campaign, and we found a man who had plundered, and found in his goods a mushaf, and all his goods were burned except the mushaf; I know not but he said: sell it and give it in charity. Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi narrated it in their books from the narration of Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Tirmidhi said: I asked Muhammad about this, and he said: Salih ibn Muhammad alone narrated it, and he is rejected in hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Salim from his father from Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this Abu Waqid is weak; the preserved is that Salim commanded this, without raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor mentioning it from his father nor from Umar."
"191","Another, 203 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, he said: I heard Aba al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, and he narrated from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat. Aba al-Hakam's name is Imran ibn al-Harith; Muslim narrated for him a hadith other than this. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muammal from Sufyan from Salamah from Imran, he said: I met Ibn Umar and asked him, and he informed me, as I think, from Umar, and mentioned it."
"192","204 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Said, that is al-Qawariri, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me, he said: I heard Aba al-Hakam, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about jar-nabidh, and he said: I heard Umar narrating: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, jarr and muzaffat. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Shubah. Abu Yala narrated it from Zuhayr from Hashim ibn al-Qasim from Shubah. Muslim has narrated in his Sahih from the narration of Tawus from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jar-nabidh and dubba."
"193","Another, 205 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us in Baghdad: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Said narrated to us: Israil narrated to us: Said ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Umar, from Umar: that he said: No, by my father. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hush; whoever swears by a thing besides Allah has associated. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus in al-Musnad in the Musnad of Umar; he also narrated it in the Musnad of Abdullah ibn Umar."
"194","206 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ubaydullah, that is Ibn Umar, narrated to us: Waki narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, he said: We were sitting with Ibn Umar in a circle, and he heard a man in another circle saying: No, by my father. He pelted him with pebbles and said: It was the oath of Umar, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him and said: It is shirk."
"195","207 - And Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us: that Umar ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Ibn Abi Gharzah Abu Umar narrated to us: Ubaydullah informed us: Israil informed us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar said: No, by my father. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by your fathers; whoever swears by a thing besides Allah has associated."
"196","Another, 208 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi, that is Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us: Ali ibn Bahr al-Qattan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid informed me, from al-Jahm ibn al-Jarud, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father: that Umar gave a fine she-camel of his as a gift and was offered three hundred dinars for it. Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I gave a fine she-camel of mine as a gift and was offered three hundred dinars for it; shall I buy it and buy camels with its price and slaughter them? He said: No; slaughter it itself. Al-Haytham al-Shashi thus produced it in the Musnad of Umar, though it resembles more the Musnad of Abdullah ibn Umar. And Allah knows best. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli from Muhammad ibn Salamah."
"197","Another, 209 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ubaydullah, that is Ibn Umar, narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: I know not but he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Blessed and Exalted said: Whoever humbles himself to Me thus, and Yazid gestured with his palm towards the earth, I raise him thus, and Yazid gestured with the inside of his palm towards the sky."
"198","210 - And Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Asim ibn Muhammad informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: I know not but he raised it, he said: Allah Almighty says: Whoever humbles himself to Me thus, I raise him thus; and he made the inside of his palm towards the earth and brought it near the earth, I raise him thus, and he raised the inside of his palm towards the sky and raised it towards the sky."
"199","211 - And Abul-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim informed us, by recitation to him in Isfahan: that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed them, by recitation to him: Muhammad ibn ... informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Murrah Abu al-Tahir al-Nasri, son-in-law of al-Hasan ibn al-Muthanna, narrated to us: Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Asim ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like. Al-Tabarani said: Asim alone narrated it. Imam Ahmad and Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun."
"200","Another, 212 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, freedman of Ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: We would say: What repentance is there for one put to trial? And they would say: Allah will accept nothing from us; we abandoned Allah and Islam through a trial that befell us after knowing it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, there was revealed concerning them: O My servants who transgressed against themselves, to His saying: while you perceive not. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I wrote it with my hand, then sent it to Hisham ibn al-As ibn Wail. Hisham said: When it came to me I climbed with it to a hill and began reading it without understanding it, then it occurred to me that it was revealed concerning us for what we used to say. He said: I sat upon my camel until I reached Madinah."
"201","213 - And with it al-Haytham informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Jabalah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said: Nafi informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Umar, and he mentioned it similarly; and in it: When it came to me I climbed to the top of a hill."
"202","214 - Abul-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, known as Qafak al-Khabbaz, informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Yunus informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa narrated to us: Khalifah ibn Khayyat and Amr ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I appointed with Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah and Hisham ibn al-As ibn Wail to emigrate to Madinah. I and Ayyash went out, and Hisham was tempted and yielded. There came to Ayyash his two brothers: Abu Jahl and al-Harith ibn Hisham, and said to him: Your mother has vowed that no shade shall shade her, nor washing touch her head, until she sees you. I said: O Ayyash, they intend only to tempt you from your religion. They took him away with it and tempted him, and he yielded. He said: There was revealed concerning them: O My servants who transgressed against themselves, despair not of the mercy of Allah. Umar said: I wrote it to Hisham, and he came."
"203","Another, 215 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Abul-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Sabbah al-Mismai narrated to us: Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from al-Rudayni ibn Abi Mijlaz, from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam overcame Musa, Adam overcame Musa, like the hadith of Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah."
"204","216 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Yahya ibn Yamar, he said: There was a man of Juhaynah in whom was frivolity, and he would seek vengeance, I think against his neighbors; then he read the Quran and learned some obligations and told people by his opinion, and it became of his affair that he claimed deeds are fresh: whoever wishes does good, and whoever wishes does evil. He mentioned speech, then said: We met Ibn Umar, and he mentioned speech, then said: Umar narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that Musa met Adam and said: O Adam, Allah created you with His Hand, made the angels prostrate to you, and settled you in Paradise; by Allah, were it not for what you did, none of your offspring would enter the Fire. He said: He said: O Musa, you whom Allah chose with His message and His word, do you blame me for what was written upon me before I was created? They disputed to Allah, and Adam overcame Musa; they disputed to Allah, and Adam overcame Musa. Al-Barqani mentioned this addition that Muslim produced it; Muslim narrated the hadith at length without mentioning this addition, then said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Ghubari, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari and Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to me, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Abdullah, from Yahya ibn Yamar, with the meaning of the hadith of Kahmas, its chain containing some addition and omission. Al-Barqani narrated it from the narration of Ahmad ibn Abdah with this addition; it may be that this addition is in Muslim's narration, and it may not be in his narration. And Allah knows best. Al-Haytham also narrated it similarly from al-Abbas al-Duri from Musa ibn Ismail from Aban from Matar."
"205","Another, 217 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Salih ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever eats, let him eat with his right, and whoever drinks, let him drink with his right, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"206","Another, 218 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should eat with his left, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left. Muslim narrated this hadith in his Sahih from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The like has been narrated in the two Sahihs; sometimes the hadith is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and sometimes from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Of that: Muslim narrated a hadith from Umar that he gave a horse in charity in the path of Allah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to a man, and the man kept it to sell it. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do not buy it nor take back your charity. He narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr from his father from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from Umar. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it from the narration of al-Zuhri from Salim from his father: that Umar gave a horse in charity, in the hadith of Ibn Umar. Muslim narrated from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr with it..."
"207","Another, 219 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Abu Musa informed us: Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubaydullah al-Umayri Abu Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: Umar said: Suspect opinion against religion; I saw myself opposing the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not falling short of the truth, and that was the day of Abi Jandal, with the document between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people of Makkah. He said: Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. They said: Do you see then that we have believed you in what you say? But we write: In Your name, O Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted, and I refused them until he said: O Umar, do you see that I have accepted and you refuse? He said: Then I accepted. Mubarak ibn Fadalah: some spoke well of him and some weakened him. Abu Zurah al-Razi said when asked about him: He does much tadlis; when he says: narrated to us, he is trustworthy. This hadith has a witness in al-Bukhari from the narration of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, his long hadith on al-Hudaybiyyah mentioned."
"208","Another, 220 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Hanbal ibn Ishaq ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates. This hadith is like what we presented: al-Bukhari and Muslim produced it in their Sahihs from the narration of Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar in his Musnad, without mention of Umar. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it and said: The correct is from Ubaydullah from Nafi from Ibn Umar from Umar, his statement."
"209","Another, 221 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid and al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us: that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar informed us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that the blood of a Muslim be shed except by one of three: a married adulterer, one who apostatizes after Islam, and one who kills a soul and is killed for it."
"210","Another, 222 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us: that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing women and children."
"211","Another, 223 - And Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed us in Baghdad: that Umar al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Ghiyath: Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Yamar and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: We met Abdullah ibn Umar, and they mentioned to him the hadith of qadar. Then he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, or: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, and he mentioned qadar and Jibril's questioning of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He mentioned the hadith with the meaning of the hadith of Matar al-Warraq. Uthman ibn Ghiyath added in his hadith, he said: A man of Muzaynah or Juhaynah asked him and said: O Messenger of Allah, in what do we act, in a thing already past and gone, or a thing begun anew now? He said: In a thing already past and gone. A man, or some of the people, said: O Messenger of Allah, then of what use is action? He said: The people of Paradise are facilitated to the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of the Fire are facilitated to the deeds of the people of the Fire."
"212","Another, 224 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn Abi Khaythamah Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Janab narrated to us: Isa ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Janub narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I circumambulated with Umar around the House; when we completed, we entered the second, and I said to him: We have completed. He said: I did not err, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combining, and I love to combine."
"213","Another, 225 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Khushui informed us, by recitation to him while we heard, it was said to him: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Karim ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed you, by recitation to him: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Kinani informed us: Abul-Qasim Tammam ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Razi informed us: Abul-Husayn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Murri al-Muqri informed us, by recitation to him: Abul-Qasim Akhtal ibn al-Hakam ibn Jabir al-Qurashi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us: Aban ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, he said: When Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, took authority, he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted mutah three times, then forbade it to us. By Allah, a righteous oath, I find no one among the Muslims fortified, practicing mutah, but I will stone him, unless he brings me four witnesses that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted it after he had forbidden it; and I find no man among the Muslims practicing mutah but I will flog him, unless he brings me four witnesses that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted it after he had forbidden it. Aban, that is Ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Hazim al-Bajali, Kufan; Yahya ibn Main deemed him trustworthy."
"214","226 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by recitation to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abul-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Tabarani narrated to us: Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: When Umar became Muslim, he said: Which of the people of Makkah spreads reports most? They said: Jamil ibn Mamar al-Jumahi. He went out to him, and I followed his tracks, a young boy understanding what I saw him do, until he came to Jamil and said: O Jamil, did you know I became Muslim? By Allah, he did not answer him a word until he stood dragging his cloak, until when he entered, meaning to Quraysh in their gatherings, he screamed at the top of his voice: O company of Quraysh, Umar ibn al-Khattab has apostatized. Umar said behind him: He lied, but I became Muslim. They rushed at him. By Allah, he kept fighting them and they fighting him until the sun stood over their heads. He tired and sat, and they stood over his head, while he said: Do what you will; by Allah, had we been a hundred men, you would have left it to us, and we shall leave it to you."
"215","Abu Tamim Abdullah ibn Malik al-Jayshani, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, 227 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Harith, known as Khurust al-Mujallidi, informed you, by recitation to him while you were present: Abul-Hasan Ubaydullah ibn al-Mutazz ibn Mansur ibn Abdullah ibn Hamzah al-Naysaburi, who came to us, informed us, he said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Muhammad informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan and Utbah ibn Abdullah al-Yuhmadi informed us, both said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us: Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah: that he heard Aba Tamim al-Jayshani saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If you relied upon Allah with His true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides the birds: they go out hungry and return full."
"216","228 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Bakr ibn Amr, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Abi Tamim al-Jayshani: that Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If you relied upon Allah with His true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides the birds: they go out hungry and return full. Imam Ahmad and Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Abdullah ibn Yazid. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ali ibn Said al-Kindi from Ibn al-Mubarak, and said: a fair sound hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Harmalah ibn Yahya from Abdullah ibn Wahb from Abdullah ibn Lahiah from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"217","Abdullah ibn Masud, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both, 229 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, the Ansar said: From us a leader and from you a leader. Umar ibn al-Khattab came to them and said: O company of Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer? Which of you is pleased to precede Abu Bakr? The Ansar said: We seek refuge in Allah from preceding Abu Bakr."
"218","230 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by recitation to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Naqur informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hasan informed us: al-Harith ibn Abi Usamah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from Abdullah: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, the Ansar said: From us a leader and from you a leader. Umar came to them and said: O company of Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people? He said: The Ansar said: We seek refuge in Allah from preceding Abu Bakr. The people said: You have spoken rightly, and have done rightly; we choose for our worldly affair him whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose for our religion."
"219","Another, 231 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us: that Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by recitation to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artaah, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khirash ibn Hawshab, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Aishah bint Qudamah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting Ramadan in travel is not of righteousness. Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi Shaybah, said similarly in his Musannaf. Waki said: It is not established from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this chapter except this. Abu Hatim al-Razi was asked about it and said: Khirash: he erring in this hadith; the people narrate it from Zayd ibn Jubayr from a man from Umar. Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, narrated from Zayd ibn Jubayr from Abi al-Wazi from a man from Umar."
"220","232 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr informed me, from Hajjaj, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khirash al-Kufi, from Umar: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I fast in travel? He said: If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break. This is more likely correct, and Allah knows best. Waki narrated in his book from Hajjaj from Zayd ibn Jubayr from Khirash from Umar, and Khirash's name is al-Harith ibn Hawshab."
"221","Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 233 - al-Qasim Abdul-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Naysaburi informed us there: that his grandfather Abul-Fadl Abd al-Karim informed him, by recitation to him, he said: Abu Bakr al-Shirawi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Hiri informed us: Abul-Abbas Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Umawi narrated to us: Abu Yahya Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us: Sufyan, that is Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj, from Mamar ibn Abi Habib, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed. Mamar: Yahya ibn Main deemed him trustworthy. The like has been narrated by Abu Yazid, coming in al-Kuna."
"222","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 234 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Yunus ibn Sulaym informed me, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli dictated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Qari: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would hear near his face a humming like the humming of bees. We waited a while, then he faced the qiblah and raised his hands and said: O Allah, increase us and do not diminish us, honor us and do not disgrace us, give us and do not deprive us, prefer us and do not prefer over us, be pleased with us and make us pleased. Then he said: Ten verses were revealed to me; whoever establishes them enters Paradise. Then he recited: The believers have succeeded, until he completed the ten. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yahya ibn Musa and Abd ibn Humayd and others, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yunus ibn Sulaym, from al-Zuhri, and from Muhammad ibn Aban from Yazid from al-Zuhri with his chain and meaning, and said: This is more sound than the first hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Abd al-Razzaq from Yunus ibn Sulaym, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid dictated to me, and said: This is a rejected hadith; we know none who narrated it but Yunus ibn Sulaym, and we do not know Yunus. And Allah knows best. Abu Abdullah al-Hakim narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Malik."
"223","Abu Uthman Abd al-Rahman ibn Mull al-Nahdi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 235 - Abu Hamid Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit ibn Zayd informed us in Baghdad: that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Khayrun, Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Taraiqi and others informed them, by recitation to them: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslim informed us: Abul-Fadl Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri informed us: Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Firyabi informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri and Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, both said: Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us: Maymun al-Kurdi narrated to us, from Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: I was with Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, and heard him saying in his sermon: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: What I fear most for my ummah is every hypocrite learned of tongue."
"224","236 - And with it Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Ziyad, from Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), more times than the number of these fingers of mine, saying: The most fearful thing I fear for this ummah is the learned hypocrite. It was said: How is the learned hypocrite? He said: Learned of tongue, ignorant of heart and deed. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Daylam ibn Ghazwan, and from Yazid ibn Harun from Daylam. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: al-Mualla ibn Ziyad narrated it from Uthman from Umar, stopped, not raised; likewise Hammad ibn Zayd narrated it from Maymun from Abi Uthman from Umar, his statement. Daylam ibn Ghazwan, kunya Abu Ghalib, differed from him, from Maymun al-Kurdi from Abi Uthman from Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar al-Jafari followed him, from Maymun al-Kurdi, raising it also to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The stopped is more like the correct. And Allah knows best."
"225","Another, 237 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us: Abul-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna al-Anazi narrated to us: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abi Nadrah, from Abi Said, from Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sit in groups contending, nor revile the dead, nor burden women, and if one of you must, let him say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me. Abd al-Ala alone narrated it thus; others narrate it from al-Jurayri from Abi Nadrah from Abi Said, but the first is more sound."
"226","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 238 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid: he performed Hajj with Umar, and Umar performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He stoned the jamrah with seven, saying Allahu Akbar with each pebble, then said: This is the standing place of him to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed. The wording is of Ibn Idris, and al-Hafiz Abu Musa al-Madini mentioned: that Ibn Abi Layla erring in it, and that the correct is from the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, and it is suspicion: fearing that al-Amash heard it from Ibrahim and Ibrahim heard from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid. Ibn Abi Layla alone narrated it from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla."
"227","240 - And Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Hurdi al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Makhlad al-Ashjai, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Umar: that he saw a man raising his hands before his face in supplication and said: Do not raise your hands except to your chest and supplicate. Al-Haytham and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated similarly from al-Ashjai. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated in their Sahihs in the hadith of Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not raise his hands in any of his supplications except in istisqa, until the whiteness of his armpits was seen. Abu Abdullah al-Bukhari said: what is intended is raising the hands above the head in istisqa. And a group narrated raising hands in qunut and in supplication unrestrictedly."
"228","Ubayd ibn Adam, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 241 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us: Yahya ibn Thabit ibn Bundar informed them, by recitation to him in Baghdad: Abul-Husayn ibn al-Naqur informed us: Abu Tahir al-Mukhallis informed us: Abu ... Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Faraj ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, from Ubayd ibn Adam: that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator has nothing. Hammad ibn Salamah followed him: he narrated from Humayd from Anas from Ubayd ibn Adam. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Affan; and Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Abu al-Walid; both from Hammad ibn Salamah with his chain."
"229","Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 242 - It was read to Shaykh Imam Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ashtah al-Isbahani while I heard, it was said to him: Abu Muhammad Hamzah ibn al-Abbas ibn Ali al-Alawi informed you, by recitation to him in Isfahan: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Hayyan informed us: al-Hasan ibn al-Jahm al-Jurjani narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, his property and blood are protected from me except by its right, and his reckoning is upon Allah. And of the hadith of Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said the like; and of Ubadah ibn al-Samit likewise; and of Abu Hurayrah likewise."
"230","Abayah ibn Rifaaah, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 243 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abayah ibn Rifaaah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that he heard him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever of you dies a Jew or a Christian and does not believe in me enters the Fire."
"231","Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah al-Adawi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 244 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ahmad, that is Ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sad Abu al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Abu Uthman al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid informed me, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah al-Adawi, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection; whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah with his equipment has the like of his reward; and whoever builds a mosque in which the name of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is mentioned, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. Ibn Majah narrated it in his Sunan from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Yunus ibn Muhammad from Layth ibn Sad. The mention of whoever builds a mosque was also narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Dawud ibn Abdullah al-Jafari from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, both from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had from al-Walid, adding in its chain Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated its beginning from Abu Yala al-Mawsili by this path we mentioned. I say: it may be that al-Layth heard it from Yazid and from al-Walid. And Allah knows best. He also narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Yunus."
"232","245 - Abul-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us: Layth informed us, and Yunus: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Uthman ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Suraqah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection; whoever equips a warrior until he departs has the like of his reward until he dies, Yunus said: or returns; and whoever builds for Allah a mosque in which the name of Allah Almighty is mentioned, Allah will build for him thereby a house in Paradise. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus. He also narrated it from Hasan ibn Musa from Ibn Lahiah from al-Walid."
"233","246 - And Abu Muslim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us of it in Isfahan: al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to me: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had al-Laythi, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection; whoever equips a warrior until he departs has the like of his reward until he dies or returns; and whoever builds a mosque, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"234","247 - Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Uthman ibn Suraqah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah Almighty will shade him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever equips a warrior until he departs has the like of his reward until he dies or returns."
"235","248 - And with it Abd al-Aziz informed us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from Uthman ibn Suraqah, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever builds a mosque in which the name of Allah is mentioned, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"236","Uthman ibn Affan, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 249 - Abu Muslim Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Humran ibn Aban: that Abu Bakr came upon Uthman and greeted him, and he returned a weak greeting. He mentioned that to Umar and said: I came upon him and greeted him, and he returned a weak greeting to me, as if he disliked what was of my affair. Umar met him and mentioned that to him, and he said: He is indeed the most entitled of people to it; he is al-Siddiq, the second of the two; but he came upon me while I was speaking to myself about something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away before clarifying it to us. He said: What is that? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I know a word no servant says truly from his heart and dies upon that but is forbidden to the Fire. Umar said: I will tell you it: the testimony that there is no god but Allah; it is the word the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his uncle to say at his death, but he refused him; and it is the word Muhammad and his Companions were made to adhere to: the testimony that there is no god but Allah."
"237","250 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us, by recitation to him while we heard in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bistami informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi, that is Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us: Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Humran ibn Aban, from Uthman ibn Affan, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I know a word no servant says truly from his heart and dies upon that but is forbidden to the Fire: There is no god but Allah. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement in it, and mentioned that this path is the best and most like the correct."
"238","Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 251 - Abul-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed us in his book, and from him my maternal uncle, Imam scholar Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us: Imam Abul-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us: Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Haywah informed me, he said: I heard Yazid ibn Abi Habib saying: Abdullah ibn al-Hakam narrated to me, from Ulayy ibn Rabah, from Uqbah ibn Amir: he narrated to him that he came to Umar with the conquest of Damascus. He said: I had leather socks on. Umar said to me: How long, O Uqbah, since you removed your leather socks? I recalled from Friday to Friday and said: Eight days. He said: You did well and hit the Sunnah."
"239","Amr ibn Said ibn al-As al-Umawi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 253 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Ishaq ibn Ismail and my maternal uncle Abu Jafar narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar al-Qurashi narrated to us: Said ibn Amr ibn Said narrated to us: that he heard his father claiming that he heard his father on the day of Marj saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: Were it not that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Almighty will protect religion by Christians of Rabiah on the bank of the Euphrates, I would not have left an Arab but I killed him or he submits."
"240","254 - And Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Abu Qilabah Abdul-Malik al-Raqashi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar al-Qurashi narrated to us: Said ibn Amr ibn Said narrated to me: that he heard his father on the day of Marj saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: Were it not that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah will honor this religion by Christians of Rabiah on the bank of the Euphrates, I would not have left an Arab but I killed him or he submits. Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri narrated it thus from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, likewise al-Haytham ibn Kulayb; perhaps he repeated hearing from his father. Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ismail from Yahya from Abdullah ibn Umar al-Qurashi from Said ibn Amr ibn Said: that his father Amr on the day of Marj says: I heard Umar. Abu Amr ibn Hamdan narrated it from Abu Yala, in it: Said ibn Amr ibn Said narrated to me that he heard his father saying: he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, without mentioning his father twice. And Allah knows best."
"241","255 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us of it there: Tamim ibn Abi Said ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them, by recitation to him: Abu Said Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan ibn Ali ibn Sinan informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ishaq ibn Ismail and my maternal uncle Abu Jafar narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar al-Qurashi narrated to us: Said ibn Amr ibn Said narrated to me: that he heard his father on the day of Marj saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah protects religion by Christians of Rabiah on the coast of the Euphrates, I would not have left an Arab but I killed him or he submits."
"242","Amr ibn Shurahbil al-Kufi Abu Maysarah, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 256 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Yahya, that is Ibn Abi Bukayr, narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shurahbil Abi Maysarah, from Umar, he said: When the prohibition of wine came down, Umar said: O Allah, clarify to us concerning wine a healing clarification. Then the verse in al-Baqarah came down: They ask you about wine and gambling. Umar was called and it was recited to him. He said: O Allah, clarify to us concerning wine a healing clarification. Then the verse in al-Nisa came down: Approach not prayer while intoxicated. The caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would, when he stood for prayer, say: Let no intoxicated one approach prayer. Umar was called and it was recited to him, and he said: O Allah, clarify to us concerning wine a healing clarification. Then what is in al-Maidah came down: Satan wishes only to cast enmity and hatred among you. Umar was called and it was recited to him; when it reached: Will you then desist, Umar said: We desist, we desist. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Khalaf ibn al-Walid from Israil. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abbad ibn Musa al-KhuttAli from Ismail ibn Jafar from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Amr ibn Shurahbil from Umar. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Yusuf from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Amr ibn Shurahbil from Umar, and from Muhammad ibn al-Ala from Waki from Israil from Abu Ishaq from Abi Maysarah that Umar, and mentioned it, and said: This is more sound than the hadith of Muhammad ibn Yusuf. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abu Dawud from Ubaydullah ibn Musa from Israil."
"243","Amr ibn Maymun, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 257 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us at al-Harbiyyah: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Said and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek refuge from five: miserliness, cowardice, the trial of the breast, the punishment of the grave, and evil old age. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus. He also narrated it from Waki from Israil."
"244","258 - And Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Isa ibn Ahmad al-Asqalani narrated to us: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek refuge from the five: cowardice, miserliness, evil old age, the trial of the breast, and the punishment of the grave."
"245","259 - And with it al-Haytham informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Amiri narrated to us: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking refuge from five: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness and cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from evil old age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the breast and the punishment of the grave. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Waki from Israil. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Ubaydullah from Israil; and from Ahmad ibn Fadalah from Ubaydullah from Israil; and from Sulayman ibn Salm from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl from Yunus; and from Imran ibn Bakkar al-Barrad from Ahmad ibn Khalid from Yunus; and from Hilal ibn al-Ala from Husayn ibn Ayyash from Zuhri from Abu Ishaq from Amr, he said: the Companions of Muhammad narrated to me; and from Ahmad ibn Sulayman from Abu Dawud from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from Amr ibn Maymun, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek refuge, mursal. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad from Waki. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Shabbabah from Yunus. Al-Hakim Abu Abdullah narrated it in al-Mustadrak from Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi from Said ibn Masud from Ubaydullah ibn Musa from Israil. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it; he said: The correct is the statement of whoever said from Abu Ishaq from Abi Maysarah from Umar. And Allah knows best."
"246","Umayr, freedman of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 260 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, it was said to him: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed you, while you were present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Khashshab al-Raqqi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Amr, from Umayr, freedman of Umar, he said: A group of the people of Iraq came to Umar and said: What brought you? They said: We came to ask you about three. He said: What are they? They said: A man's voluntary prayer in his house, what is it? What is lawful for a man of his menstruating wife? And washing from janabah? Umar said: Are you sorcerers? They said: No, by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, we are not sorcerers. He said: Are you soothsayers? They said: No. He said: You have asked me about three none asked me since I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them before you. He said: As for a man's voluntary prayer in his house, illuminate your house as you can. As for the menstruating one, for you is what is above the waist-wrapper, and what is beneath it is not for you. As for washing from janabah: pour with your right upon your left, then enter your hand into the vessel and wash your private part and what touched you, then perform ablution as for prayer, then pour upon your head three times, rubbing your head each time."
"247","261 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadham informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar, from Umayr, freedman of Umar, he said: A group of the people of Iraq came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said to them: Did you come with permission? They said: Yes. He said: What brought you? They said: We came to ask you about three. He said: What are they? They said: A man's prayer in his house, what is it? What is proper for a man of his wife while menstruating? And washing from janabah? He said: Are you sorcerers? They said: No, by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, we are not sorcerers. He said: You have asked me about three none asked me since I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them before you. As for a man's voluntary prayer in his house: illuminate your house as you can. As for the menstruating one: for you is what is above the waist-wrapper, and nothing beneath it. As for washing from janabah: pour with your left upon your right and wash it, then enter your hand into the vessel and wash your private part and what touched you, then perform ablution as for prayer, then pour upon your head three times, rubbing your head each time, then wash the rest of your body. Abu Abdullah ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Husayn from Abdullah ibn Jafar. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it. He said: The hadith is the hadith of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and whoever followed him, from Abu Ishaq; he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, Raqabah ibn Masqalah and Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari narrated it, saying: from Asim ibn Amr from Umayr; the hadith is the hadith of Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and whoever followed him, from Abu Ishaq."
"248","Iyad al-Ashari, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 262 - Abul-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abul-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Iyad al-Ashari saying: I witnessed Yarmuk under five commanders: Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan, Ibn Hasanah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, and Iyad, and this Iyad is not the one who narrated to Simak. He said: Umar said: When there is fighting, upon you is Abu Ubaydah. He said: We wrote that death had surged towards us, and sought reinforcement. He wrote to us: Your letter seeking my reinforcement has come to me; I point you to one mightier in aid and more present in troops: Allah Almighty, so seek His aid; Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was aided on the day of Badr with fewer than your number. When this letter of mine comes to you, fight them and do not refer back to me. He said: We fought them, routed them and killed them for four farsakhs. He said: We took spoils and consulted; Iyad advised us to give ten for each head. He said: Abu Ubaydah said: Who will race me? A youth said: I, if you will not be angry. He said: He outran him; I saw the two braids of Abu Ubaydah bouncing behind him on an Arabian horse. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus in al-Musnad. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hilali from Muhammad ibn Yasar from Muhammad from Shubah similarly."
"249","Farrukh, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 263 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated to us: Isa ibn Ahmad al-Asqalani narrated to us: al-Nadr informed us: al-Haytham ibn Rafi al-Bahili informed us, he said: I heard Aba Yahya al-Makki saying: I heard Farrukh, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab came out of the mosque and saw piled food, and said: What is this food? They said: This is food brought to us. He said: May Allah bless it and whoever brought it. They said: O Commander of the Faithful, it has been hoarded. He said: Who hoarded it? They said: Farrukh, freedman of Uthman, and a freedman of Umar. He called them and said: What carried you to hoard the food of the Muslims? They said: O Commander of the Faithful, we buy with our wealth and sell in the market. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever hoards their food against the Muslims, Allah will strike him with leprosy and paralysis. He said: As for Farrukh, he said: By Allah, I will neither sell nor buy food after it, and turned to cloth. As for the freedman of Umar, he persisted. Abu Yahya al-Makki said: I saw him crippled, leprous. Abu Yahya said: al-Nadr said: al-Haytham said: I said to Abu Yahya: What is makhduj? He said: Severed. Al-Haytham also narrated it similarly from Ibn al-Munadi from Yunus ibn Muhammad from al-Haytham. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from al-Haytham. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, from al-Qasim similarly. Ibn Majah narrated it from Yahya ibn Hakim from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi from al-Haytham similarly."
"250","Qays ibn Abi Hazim al-Bajali, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 264 - Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, with my recitation to him at al-Harbiyyah, I said to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, by recitation to him: Yahya, that is Ibn Said, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us, at Harran: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abdullah ibn Rawahah: Would you move the mounts for us? He said: I have left my poetry. Umar said to him: Listen and obey. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, have mercy on him. Umar said: It is assured. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Harrani."
"251","Qays ibn Marwan al-Jufi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 265 - Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn al-Akhdar informed us, by recitation to him while we heard in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abul-Qasim Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallas informed us: Abdullah, that is al-Baghawi, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah: that Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever wishes to recite the Quran moist as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm Abd recites."
"252","266 - And with it Ibn Zunbur narrated to us also: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Qays ibn Marwan, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like."
"253","267 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from Qays ibn Marwan, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran moist as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."
"254","268 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, by recitation to her while you heard: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, and from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Qays ibn Marwan, he said: A man came to Umar and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I left in Iraq a man dictating copies of the Quran from memory. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, became angry until his face reddened. Umar said to him: Know what you say, repeatedly. He said: I came to you only with truth. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Who is he? He said: Ibn Umm Abd. He calmed until anger left him, then said: None on the face of the earth is more entitled to that than he. I shall narrate to you about that: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conversed at night in the house of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, one night for some of his need until it darkened. Then he returned between me and Abu Bakr until I reached the mosque, when a man of the Muhajirun was praying. He stood listening to his recitation; neither I nor my companion knew who he was. He said: When he stood a while I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man of the Muhajirun praying; had you returned, though it darkened. He said: He nudged me, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept listening to his recitation. He said: He bowed and prostrated, then sat supplicating. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: Ask, you will be given; ask, you will be given. Neither I nor my companion knew who he was until we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm Abd recites. He said: Then I and my companion knew who he was. He said: I went early to Abdullah to give him glad tidings, and he said: Abu Bakr already preceded you. By Allah, I never raced Abu Bakr to good but he preceded me. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim from al-Amash from Ibrahim from Alqamah, and from Abu Muawiyah from al-Amash from Khaythamah from Qays similarly. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Zunbur by both paths, and from Muhammad ibn Aban from Abu Fudayl abridged. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, and said: al-Amash ضبط his chain and hadith, and it is the correct. It was said to him: al-Bukhari, as Abu Isa reported from him, judged by the hadith of al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, meaning he narrated it from Ibrahim from Alqamah from al-Qartha from Qays or Ibn Qays, a man of Jufa. Al-Daraqutni said: In my view the hadith of al-Amash is the correct, and al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah is not strong; then he said: al-Hasan is not measured against al-Amash."
"255","Kab ibn Ujrah al-Ansari, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 269 - Imam scholar Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: that Abu Zurah Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them, by recitation to him in Baghdad: Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us: Abu Talhah al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us: Abul-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah al-Qattan informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from Umar, he said: The travel prayer is two rakahs, the Friday prayer is two rakahs, Fitr and Adha are two rakahs, complete without shortening upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yazid ibn Abi al-Jad narrated it from Zubayd from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah from Umar; Sufyan al-Thawri differed from him, and there is disagreement from him: Muadh ibn Muadh said from al-Thawri from Zubayd from Ibn Abi Layla from his father from Umar; Yahya al-Qattan said from al-Thawri from Zubayd from Abi Layla from the trustworthy from Umar. Their companions of al-Thawri differed from both: Zaidah, Abu Nuaym, Waki, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Adani, Mihran ibn Abi Umar, Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari and others narrated it from al-Thawri from Zubayd from Ibn Abi Layla from Umar, without mentioning anyone between them."
"256","Kulayb ibn Shihab al-Jarmi Abu Asim, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 270 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr, that is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, he said: I met Umar while at the season and called from behind the tent: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Jarmi; a nephew of ours has a captive brother among so-and-so, and we offered him the ordinance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar raised the side of the tent and said: Do you know your companion? He said: Yes; he is that one. He said: Take you two him until he executes for you the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We used to say the judgment was four camels."
"257","Kahmas al-Hilali, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, 271 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah informed us: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Yazid ibn Muslim, that is al-Minqari, narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, he said: Kahmas said to me: Shall I not narrate to you something I heard from Umar? I said: Yes. He said: I heard Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of my ummah are the generation in which I am, then those who come after them, then those who come after them; then will arise a people whose oaths precede their testimonies, and they testify before they are asked to testify; they have clamor in their markets. Hammad ibn Yazid: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him without mentioning disparagement in him, and mentioned that a group narrated from him."
"258","272 - Hafiz Abu Musa al-Madini informed us in his book: that Ghanim al-Burji informed them, by recitation to him: Abu Nuaym informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Jafar informed us: Yunus ibn Habib informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah al-Madani, he said: I came to al-Mirbad at the time of dried cheese and ghee, with Bedouins coming; I saw a man with roving gaze looking at people, and thought him a stranger. I approached him and greeted him; he returned greeting and said to me: Are you of these people? I said: Yes, and we sat with him. I said: Of whom are you? He said: Of Banu Hilal, my name Kahmas; or he said: Of Banu Salul, my name Kahmas. Then he said to me: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I witnessed from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him? I said: Yes. He mentioned a story, then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of my ummah are the generation of which I am, then the second, then the third; then will arise a people whose oaths precede their testimonies, testifying without being asked to testify; they have clamor in their markets."
"259","Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nasri, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 273 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nasri: that he was sitting with Umar, and al-Abbas and Ali came disputing. Ali said: O Commander of the Faithful, judge between me and this. Umar said: A group; bear witness, and I ask you by Allah by whom the heaven and earth stand: Do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity? They said: He said that. He turned to Ali and al-Abbas and said: I ask you by Allah: Do you both know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that? They said: Yes. He said: I shall narrate to you about this fay: Allah singled His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with something of it He gave none else: And what Allah restored to His Messenger from them, you spurred neither horse nor camel for it. Banu al-Nadir was for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exclusively; by Allah, he did not take it to your exclusion nor appropriate it besides you; he would distribute it among you until this property remained, from which he would spend a year's maintenance on his family, then put what remained in the property of Allah. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Abu Bakr said: I am the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he took it and did in it what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would do. And Allah knows he was in it truthful, righteous, rightly guided, following the truth. Then Abu Bakr passed away, and I am the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the successor of Abu Bakr, so I took it for two years of my rule, doing in it what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did and what Abu Bakr did. And Allah knows I am in it truthful, righteous, rightly guided, following the truth. Then you two came to me, both your speech one and your affair one: you, O Abbas, came to me asking me your share from your nephew, and this, meaning Ali, came to me asking me his wife's share from her father. I said to you: If you wish, I hand it to you, on that Allah takes a covenant from you that you act in it with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted, and what Abu Bakr and I acted; else do not speak to me about it. You said: Hand it to us on that. Then you came to me to judge between you otherwise. By Allah, I judge between you with no judgment but that until the Hour is established. If you are unable, return it to me. This hadith is in the two Sahihs by various paths."
"260","276 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us of it in Isfahan: that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, while he was present: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad informed us: Humayd ibn al-Aswad informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artaah, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, from Khirash ibn Hawshab, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Umm Qudamah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting Ramadan in travel is not of righteousness. Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Abu Umar al-Hawdi narrated it from Shubah from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Ata from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Fasting in travel is not of righteousness. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated similarly from Shubah from Hamzah al-Zayyat from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla."
"261","Another, 277 - Umar ibn Muhammad informed us: that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad informed them by recitation: Ahmad informed us: al-Qasim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Nufayli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab mentioned the fay one day and said: I am no more entitled to this fay than you, and none of us is more entitled to it than another, except that we are upon our stations from the Book of Allah Almighty and the distribution of His Messenger: a man among us and his precedence, a man and his trial, a man and his dependents, a man and his need. Abu Dawud narrated it thus. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Muyassar al-Saghani from Muhammad ibn Ishaq similarly. He added in it: By Allah, if I remain for them, the shepherd at the mountain of Sanaa will receive his share of this wealth while pasturing his place."
"262","Murrah ibn Sharahil al-Hamdani al-Kufi, known as al-Tayyib, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 278 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar informed us: Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Murrah al-Hamdani: Umar said: Three, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had clarified them to us, are dearer to me than the world and what is in it: riba, the caliphate, and kalalah."
"263","279 - And Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Qurashi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Murrah al-Hamdani, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Three, had the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified them to us, are dearer to me than the world: the caliphate, kalalah and riba. Abu Abdullah ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Ali ibn Muhammad from Waki. This Abu Khalid I deem Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban. We relied in the hadith only upon Waki's narration. Shubah has narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah."
"264","280 - Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us in his book: that Abul-Qasim Ghanim al-Burji informed them, by recitation to him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Yunus ibn Habib informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah: he heard Murrah saying: Umar said: Three, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had clarified them, are dearer to me than red camels: the caliphate, kalalah and riba. I said to Murrah: Who doubts kalalah? It is what is besides child and parent. He said: They doubt concerning the parent."
"265","Mustazill ibn Husayn, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 281 - Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us: that Abu Shuja al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: Abu Qilabah Abdul-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us: Umar ibn Amir and Bishr ibn Mihran narrated to me, both said: Sharik narrated to us, one of them said: he narrated to us at Makkah, the other did not mention: he narrated from Shabib ibn Gharqadah, from al-Mustazill ibn Husayn: that Umar ibn al-Khattab proposed to Ali for his daughter, and he excused himself by her young age, saying: I have prepared her for my nephew Jafar. Umar said: By Allah, I did not intend thereby boast; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every cause and lineage is cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my cause and lineage."
"266","Masruq ibn al-Ajda al-Hamdani, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 282 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there: Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them, by recitation to him: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Nahhati informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us: Abu Arubah informed us: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks people to enrich his wealth, it is but a hot stone of the Fire he swallows; whoever wishes, let him take little, and whoever wishes, let him take much. Ibn Hibban narrated it thus."
"267","283 - Imam Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Silafi al-Isbahani informed us in writing: that ... ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Misri informed them, therein by recitation to him in Isfahan, he said: I said to him: Qadi Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Razi narrated to you by dictation: Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman Yazdad informed us: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Baghandi narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Sulami narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks people to enrich thereby his wealth, it is but a hot stone of the Fire he swallows; whoever wishes, let him take little, and whoever wishes, let him take much. Abu Hafs said: Yahya ibn al-Sakan alone narrated this hadith from Hammad from Dawud; I know none else who narrated it, and it is a sound strange hadith. I say: al-Baghandi we mentioned only for consideration."
"268","284 - Barakat ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi informed us of it: that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed them, by recitation to him: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kinani informed us: Tammam ibn Muhammad al-Razi informed us: Abul-Qasim Ali ibn Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Aqil Anas ibn al-Salm ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Salm ibn Mansur al-Khawlani al-Antarsusi narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Sulayman al-Rusafi, known as Ibn Mutain, imam of Salamiyyah, narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us with its chain similarly. Except that he said: to enrich his wealth; it is but a hot stone of the Fire he swallows."
"269","Nusaybah Umm Atiyyah, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, 285 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: that Said ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he gathered the women of the Ansar in a house, then sent to us Umar ibn al-Khattab. He stood at the door and greeted us, and we returned his greeting, and said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. He said: Will you pledge to me that you will not associate with Allah, nor steal, nor kill your children, nor bring slander you invent between your hands and feet, nor disobey him in good? They said: Yes. She said: We extended our hands from inside the house, and he extended his hand from outside. He commanded us to bring out the menstruating and secluded in the two Eids, and forbade us following funerals, with no Friday upon us. She said: I said: What is the good you were forbidden? She said: Wailing."
"270","286 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us. 287 - And Abu Jafar also informed us: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, by recitation to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri informed us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Umm Atiyyah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and with him Umar, and women pledged to him. He said to us: Pledge that you will not associate with Allah, nor disobey him in good. There was among us an old woman with trembling hand, and she said to her: What do we pledge him upon? She said: That you pledge him not to wail. We extended our hands from outside the house, and he extended his hand, and we pledged him. She said: He commanded us to bring out in the two Eids the secluded and menstruating, and forbade us going out in a funeral or attending Friday. I said to her: What is: you will not disobey him? She said: Wailing. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abi al-Walid and Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Ishaq ibn Uthman. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Aban from Waki. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Khalifah from Abi al-Walid."
"271","Nuaym ibn Dajajah al-Asadi al-Kufi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 288 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by recitation to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hani, from Nuaym ibn Dajajah, he said: I heard Umar saying: No hijrah after the passing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali from Ibn Mahdi."
"272","Nuaym ibn Rabiah, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 289 - Abul-Hasan al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Tusi informed us, with my recitation to him in Nishapur, I said to him: Abu Muhammad Hibatullah ibn Sahl ibn Umar ibn Muhammad al-Sayyidi informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abu Uthman Said ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi informed us: Abu Ali Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Musa al-Tanukhi informed us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Musa al-Hashimi informed us: Abu Musab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri informed us: Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab: he informed him, from Muslim ibn Yasar al-Juhani: that Umar ibn al-Khattab was asked about this verse: When your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their backs, their offspring, and made them witness over themselves: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes; we testify, lest you say on the Day of Resurrection: We were unaware of this. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah created Adam, then wiped his back with His right and brought forth offspring from him, and said: I created these for Paradise, and with the deeds of the people of Paradise they act. Then He wiped his back and brought forth offspring from him, and said: I created these for the Fire, and with the deeds of the people of the Fire they act. A man said: Of what use is action, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah creates a servant for Paradise, He employs him with the deeds of the people of Paradise until he dies upon a deed of the deeds of the people of Paradise and admits him thereby to Paradise; and when He creates a servant for the Fire, He employs him with the deeds of the people of the Fire until he dies upon a deed of the deeds of the people of the Fire and admits him thereby to the Fire."
"273","290 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us, with my recitation to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abul-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed you, by recitation to him while you heard: Abul-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Umar ibn Jafar or Jusham al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated to me, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Nuaym ibn Rabiah, he said: I was with Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he mentioned the like. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it from al-Qanabi from Malik, and from Muhammad ibn Musaffa from Baqiyyah from Umar al-Qurashi from Zayd, as we produced it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ishaq ibn Musa from Man from Malik, and said: A fair hadith; Muslim did not hear from Umar, and some mentioned in this chain between Muslim and Umar a man. Al-Nasai narrated it from Qutaybah from Malik. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Umar ibn Said ibn Sinan and al-Husayn ibn Idris al-Ansari, both from Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrates it from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muslim ibn Yasar from Nuaym ibn Rabiah from Umar; Yazid ibn Sinan Abu Farwah al-Rahawi narrated it thus, perfecting its chain and joining it. Malik ibn Anas differed from him and narrated it from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah without mentioning Nuaym ibn Rabiah in the chain, sending it from Muslim ibn Yasar from Umar. The hadith of Zayd ibn Sinan is joined, and it is more entitled to correctness. And Allah knows best. Umar ibn Jusham followed him and narrated it from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah; thus Baqiyyah said from him."
"274","Harim ibn Abi Nasib al-Basri Abu al-Ajfa, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 291 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us: that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informs them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin: he heard it from Abi al-Ajfa: I heard Umar saying: Do not be excessive in women's dowries; had it been honor in this world or piety in the Hereafter, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to it among you. He married none of his daughters nor wives for more than twelve uqiyyahs. And another you say in your campaigns: So-and-so was killed a martyr, so-and-so died a martyr; perhaps he loaded the rear of his mount or the side of his saddle with gold and silver seeking trade. Do not say that; but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is in Paradise."
"275","292 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Ibn Awn and Hisham, that is Ibn Hassan, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abi al-Ajfa al-Sulami, he said: Umar addressed us and said: Do not be excessive in women's dowries; had it been honor in this world or piety with Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled and most deserving of it among you. He gave no wife of his wives, nor was any daughter of his daughters given, more than twelve uqiyyahs. One of you exaggerates his wife's dowry until it becomes enmity in himself, until he says: I toiled to you the hanging of the waterskin. Abu al-Ajfa said: I was a mawlid Arab and knew not what the hanging of the waterskin is. And another you say: So-and-so was killed in these campaigns of yours, or died; so-and-so was killed a martyr; perhaps he burdened the rear of his mount or the side of his saddle with gold or silver seeking the world. Do not say that; but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or as Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah or dies in the path of Allah is in Paradise."
"276","293 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Abu Muhammad Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abi al-Ajfa al-Sulami, he said: I heard Umar saying: Do not exaggerate in women's dowries; had it been honor in this world or piety with Allah Almighty, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to it among you. I know not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marrying a wife of his wives or marrying a daughter of his daughters for more than twelve uqiyyahs. One of you today exaggerates his woman's dowry until it becomes enmity in himself, until he says: I toiled to you the hanging of the waterskin; and I was a young boy and knew not what the hanging of the waterskin is."
"277","294 - And with it Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abi al-Ajfa, he said: I heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: And another you say of some killed in these campaigns of yours: So-and-so was killed a martyr and died a martyr; perhaps he loaded his mount or the rear of his mount with gold or silver seeking trade. Do not say that; but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or as Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah Almighty is a martyr."
"278","295 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn Ishaq ibn Ali ibn Jabir al-Jabiri informed us, by recitation to him: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Muthanna narrated to us: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abi al-Ajfa al-Sulami, he said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Do not exaggerate women's dowries; had it been honor or piety, your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been most entitled to that. He gave no wife of his wives, nor dowered his daughters, but twelve uqiyyahs. A man exaggerates a woman's dowry until it bequeaths enmity between them, saying: I toiled to you the sweat of the waterskin. And another you say in your campaigns: So-and-so was killed a martyr; perhaps he loaded between the two sides of his mount to its rear with gold or silver seeking trade. But say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr. Abu Dawud produced it in his Sunan up to his saying: uqiyyah, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd from Hammad ibn Zayd. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it likewise from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani, as we produced it, and said: A fair sound hadith. Al-Nasai produced it from Ali ibn Hujr from Ibn Ulayyah from Ayyub, Ibn Awn, Salamah ibn Alqamah and Hisham ibn Hassan from Ibn Sirin; Salamah ibn Alqamah said from Ibn Sirin: I was informed from Abi al-Ajfa. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Yazid ibn Harun from Ibn Awn, and from Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami from Yazid ibn Zuray from Ibn Awn from Ibn Sirin, all up to his saying: uqiyyah only. And Allah knows best. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, Ibn Awn, Hisham ibn Hassan, Mansur ibn Zadhan, Ashath ibn Sawwar, Matar al-Warraq, al-Salt ibn Dinar, Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ansari, Awf al-Arabi, Ismail ibn Muslim, Mujjaah ibn al-Zubayr, Ubaydah ibn Hassan, Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Shanni, Yahya ibn Atiq, Abu Khayrah and his brother narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abi al-Ajfa. Ibn Uyaynah, Hammad ibn Salamah, Ibn Ulayyah, al-Harith ibn Umayr and Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata agreed from Ayyub; Amr ibn Abi Qays differed from them and narrated it from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin from Abi al-Ajfa from his father. Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated it from Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed from Abi al-Ajfa. Muadh ibn Muadh said: from Ibn Awn from Ibn Sirin from Ibn Abi al-Ajfa from Abi al-Ajfa from Umar. Mansur ibn Zadham said: from Ibn Sirin: Abu al-Ajfa narrated to us. If Amr ibn Abi Qays preserved it from Ayyub, it resembles that Ibn Sirin heard it from Abi al-Ajfa and preserved it from Ibn Abi al-Ajfa from his father. And Allah knows best. That is for the statement of Mansur, of the trustworthy memorizers, from Ibn Sirin: Abu al-Ajfa narrated to us, and for the multitude who followed him of those who narrated it from Ibn Sirin from Abi al-Ajfa. And Allah knows best. He mentioned a group who narrated it from other than the path of Abi al-Ajfa, and said: This hadith is sound only from Abi al-Ajfa."
"279","Hashim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 296 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal al-Adib informed them, by recitation to him: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Razi informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Umm al-Numan bint Amir ibn Masud al-Thaqafiyyah, from her brother al-Walid ibn Amir, from her uncle Hashim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: that he used to supplicate: O Allah, make me live Islam wakeful, obey me not an envious enemy in me, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You hold by its forelock, and I ask You of the good all of which is in Your Hand. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah, and said: Umar ibn al-Khattab passed away while Hashim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr was nine years old. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim al-Razi said: Hashim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Umar, mursal; Mualla ibn Rubah narrated from him."
"280","Yala ibn Umayyah, he is Ibn Munabbih, a Companion; Umayyah his father and Munyah his mother, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 297 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there: that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from Yala ibn Umayyah, he said: I circumambulated with Umar ibn al-Khattab; when I was at the corner by the door towards the Stone, I took his hand that he touch it. He said: Did you not circumambulate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. He said: Did you see him touching it? I said: No. He said: Then pass on from you; you have in the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a good example."
"281","298 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Atiq narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Babah, from some of the sons of Yala ibn Umayyah, from his father, he said: I circumambulated with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he touched the corner. Yala said: I was on the side of the House; when I reached the corner by the Black Corner, I pulled his hand. He said: What is with you? I said: Will you not touch? He said: Did you not circumambulate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. He said: Did you see him touching these two corners? I said: No. He said: Is there not for me in him a good example? I said: Yes. He said: Then pass on from you. Imam Ahmad and Abu Khaythamah narrated it likewise from Rawh ibn Ubadah, in it: from some of the sons of Yala, from Yala. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Ibn Jurayj with its chain. He said: Yala said: I circumambulated with Uthman. He mentioned it in the Musnad of Umar and in the Musnad of Uthman."
"282","Yazid ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 299 - Abu Hamid Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit informed us in Baghdad: that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzar informed them, by recitation to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kaysan informed us: Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Who of our present was on the day of al-Qahah? Abu Dharr said: I. A man came with a rabbit, and a man said: Did you not see it menstruating? As if he avoided it, and he commanded that they eat of it. The man was fasting, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is your fast? He mentioned something I know not what it is. He said: Where are you of the white radiant: thirteen, fourteen and fifteen? Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Hajjaj from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab from Musa ibn Talhah from Yazid ibn al-Hawtakiyyah. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim al-Razi said: I know none who named Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah but al-Hajjaj ibn Artaah, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab. Imam Ahmad narrated it in the Musnad of Umar from Abi al-Nadr from al-Masudi from Hakim ibn Jubayr, making Ammar instead of Abu Dharr."
"283","300 - And Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us in his book: that Abul-Qasim Ghanim al-Burji informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Yunus ibn Habib informed us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah, he said: Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, was brought a rabbit and said: Were it not fear that I add or omit, I would narrate to you the hadith of the Bedouin when he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the rabbit, and mentioned that he saw blood in it, and he commanded them to eat it. He said to the Bedouin: Come near and eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: What fast do you fast? He said: From the beginning of the month and its end. He said: If you fast, fast the white days: thirteen, fourteen and fifteen. But send to Ammar; they sent to him and he came, and he said: Are you witness to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the Bedouin came to him with the rabbit and said: I saw it menstruating? Ammar said: Yes. Al-Masudi's name is Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Masud; it was said he became confused at the end of his life, and his narration is corroboration for another's narration."
"284","Abu Hurayrah al-Dawsi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, 301 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad: that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, by recitation to him: Ali Abu al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Abu Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to me: Ata ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Hakim ibn Sharik al-Hudhali, from Yahya ibn Maymun al-Hadrami, from Rabiah al-Jurashi, from Abu Hurayrah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not sit with the people of qadar nor open discourse with them. Abu Abd al-Rahman once said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"285","302 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: that Said al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah, Harun ibn Maruf and others narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Ata ibn Dinar, from Hakim ibn Sharik, from Yahya ibn Maymun al-Hadrami, from Rabiah al-Jurashi, from Abu Hurayrah, from Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sit with the people of qadar nor open discourse with them."
"286","303 - Abu Ahmad Abdul-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad: that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, from Ata ibn Dinar, from Hakim ibn Sharik, from Yahya ibn Maymun, from Rabiah al-Jurashi, from Abu Hurayrah, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sit with the people of qadar nor open discourse with them."
"287","304 - And with it al-Haytham said: Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, with its chain, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sit with the people of qadar nor open discourse with them. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Ahmad ibn Hanbal; and from Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani from Ibn Wahb from Amr ibn al-Harith, Said ibn Abi Ayyub and Ibn Lahiah from Ata with its chain. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala from Abu Khaythamah."
"288","Abu Yazid, father of Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 305 - Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah, also named al-Mu'ayyad, informed us: that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from his father: he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Sufyan."
"289","306 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim, he and Umm Habibah Aishah bint Mamar ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by recitation to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sat in al-Hijr and sent to a man of Banu Zuhrah of our household who had reached jahiliyyah. He came to him. He said: I went with him and he came to him. He said: He asked him about the building of the Kaaba, and he said: Quraysh strengthened in its building, fell short of its expense, and deemed small; they built and left part of it in al-Hijr. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You spoke truly. He asked him about births of jahiliyyah births, and the shaykh said: The seed from so-and-so, and the child upon the bed of so-and-so. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: You spoke truly; but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by the bed. The like has been narrated by Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar from Umar."
"290","Ibn Hujayr al-Adawi, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, 307 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us at Dar al-Qazz: that al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, by recitation to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit informed us: Abul-Qasim ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lului informed us: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath al-Sijistani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware sitting upon the roads. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we must have our sittings to converse in. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you refuse, give the road its right. They said: What is the right of the road, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Lowering the gaze, withholding harm, returning greeting, commanding good and forbidding evil."
"291","308 - With the same chain he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Isa al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd, from Ibn Hujayr al-Adawi, he said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this story, he said: And you aid the distressed and guide the stray. Abu Dawud narrated it thus in his Sunan."
"292","Aban ibn Uthman from his father, may Allah be pleased with him - 309 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, by my reading to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to me, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abu Mawdud, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: In the name of Allah, with Whose name nothing harms on earth nor in heaven, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, three times, no sudden affliction will strike him until the night, and whoever says it in the evening, no sudden affliction will strike him until morning, if Allah wills. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Surayj, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father, from Aban ibn Uthman similarly."
"293","310 - The Imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini the Hafiz informed us by letter that Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Abi Nasr al-Tanukhi informed them, by reading to him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Yunus ibn Habib informed us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father from Aban ibn Uthman, he said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no servant who says every morning of each day or every evening of each night: In the name of Allah, with Whose name nothing harms on earth nor in heaven, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, except that nothing will harm him. He said: Aban had been struck by a wind of paralysis, and a man visited him and saw his condition, so Aban ibn Uthman perceived it and said: The hadith is as I narrated to you, but I did not say it that day so that Allah's decree would take effect. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Yazid ibn Firas, from Aban. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it in his Sunan from al-Qanabi, from Abu Mawdud, from one who heard Aban ibn Uthman, and from Nasr ibn Asim al-Antaki, from Anas ibn Iyad, from Abu Mawdud, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Aban similarly, without mentioning the story. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah both narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abu Dawud, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father similarly, and al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it in Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun, from al-Qanabi, from Abu Mawdud, from a man, and from Qutaybah, from Anas ibn Iyad, from Abu Mawdud, from Muhammad ibn Kab, from Aban; and from Bundar, from Abu Dawud; and from Duhaym, from Ibn Abi Fudayk, from Yazid ibn Firas, from Aban ibn Uthman, without the story. Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Khaythamah, from Qudamah ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Madini, from al-Mundhir ibn Abd Allah al-Hizami, from Aban. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah, and from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Bistami, both from Anas ibn Iyad. Abu Mawdud is Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sulayman. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated it from his father, and this is continuous and is the best of them in chain."
"294","Another - 311 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ismail Abu Mamar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Taifi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Musa ibn Imran ibn Mannah, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman that he saw a funeral and stood for it, saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) see a funeral and stand for it."
"295","312 - With the same chain Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to me, Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Imran ibn Mannah, he said: Aban ibn Uthman saw a funeral and stood for it, then said: Uthman ibn Affan saw a funeral and stood for it, then reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a funeral and stood for it."
"296","313 - With the same chain Abd Allah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Musa ibn Imran ibn Mannah, from Aban ibn Uthman that he saw a funeral approaching, and when he saw it he stood, saying: I saw Uthman do that, and he told me that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it. Abd Allah mentioned it from his father Imran ibn Mannah, and narrated it from other than his father, saying: Musa ibn Imran, and perhaps the mention of Musa dropped. Allah knows best. Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it in his Musnad stating therein: from Musa ibn Imran."
"297","314 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi al-Sari and Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Musa ibn Imran, from Aban ibn Uthman, that he saw a funeral, and when he saw it he stood, then said: I saw Uthman do that, and he told me that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ismail ibn Ayyash, Musab ibn Sadaqah the father of Muhammad ibn Musab, and Said ibn Maslamah narrate it, and they agreed on raising it as marfu, unlike Yahya ibn Sulaym, who stopped it as mawquf on Ismail ibn Umayyah, and its raised form is correct; it is said that only Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani stopped it from Yahya ibn Sulaym. Al-Humaydi, Suwayd ibn Said, Abu Mamar al-Hudhali, and Abu al-Sari Sahl ibn Mahmud narrated it from Yahya as marfu."
"298","Another - 315 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us, by reading to him, in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad al-Muqri informed them, by reading to him while present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Nafi ibn Abd Allah ibn Ashras al-Madani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father, from Aban ibn Uthman, he said: I heard Uthman say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does a favor to anyone of the children of Abd al-Muttalib and is not recompensed for it in this world, then upon me is his recompense tomorrow when he meets me. Al-Tabarani said: This hadith is not narrated from Uthman except by this chain; Yusuf ibn Nafi is alone in it. Yusuf ibn Nafi was mentioned by Ibn Abi Hatim in his book, saying: He narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated from him, and he mentioned no criticism of him."
"299","Another - 316 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us, Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah the nephew of al-Zuhri ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shihab, Salih ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to me that Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him that he heard Aban ibn Uthman say: Uthman ibn Affan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you think, if there were a flowing river at the courtyard of one of you in which he bathed five times every day, what would remain of his dirt? They said: Nothing. He said: Then the prayers remove sins as dirt is removed."
"300","317 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Salih ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to me that Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him that he heard Aban ibn Uthman say: Uthman, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What do you think, if there were a flowing river at the courtyard of one of you from which he bathed five times every day, what would remain of his dirt? They said: Nothing. He said: Then the prayers remove sins as water removes dirt. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, and Abd ibn Humayd likewise narrated it from him in his Musnad. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"301","Asad ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari Abu Umamah from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him - 318 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, al-Qawariri, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, and his copy is from the hadith of al-Qawariri, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: I was with Uthman in the house while he was besieged, and we would enter a passage such that when we entered it we heard the speech of those on the courtyard. One day he entered that passage, then came out to us with changed color, saying: They are threatening me with killing just now. We said: O Commander of the Faithful, Allah will suffice you against them. He said: And why would they kill me, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except in one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after chastity, or kills a soul without a soul. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam ever, nor did I love to exchange my religion since Allah guided me to it, nor did I kill a soul, so for what would they kill me?!"
"302","319 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, by my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you, by reading to him while you were present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Musab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Mabad informed us, Yahya ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Umamah, he said: We were with Uthman while he was besieged in the house; we would enter a passage, and whoever entered it heard the speech of those on the courtyard. He came out to us with changed color, saying: They are threatening me with killing!! We said: Then Allah will suffice you against them, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: And for what would they kill me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, a man who commits adultery after chastity, or kills a soul without a soul. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam ever, nor did I love to have a substitute for my religion since Allah guided me, nor did I kill a soul, so for what would they kill me? Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Sulayman ibn Harb and Affan, from Hammad ibn Zayd. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah narrated it from Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Hammad ibn Zayd similarly. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub, from Muhammad ibn Isa, from Hammad ibn Zayd."
"303","Busr ibn Said al-Madani from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 320 - Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Hurfi informed us by letter that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan informed them, by license if not by hearing: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Nasai informed us, Muammal ibn Ihab informed us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, from Uthman ibn Affan, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: that he commits adultery after chastity, or kills a person and so is killed, or disbelieves after his Islam and so is killed. Al-Nasai narrated it thus."
"304","Thumamah ibn Hazn al-Qushayri al-Basri from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 321 - Abu Muslim Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, by my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Masud al-Jurayri, from Thumamah ibn Hazn al-Qushayri, he said: I witnessed the house when Uthman looked down upon them, saying: Bring me these two companions of yours who incited them against me. They were brought as though they were two camels, or as though they were two donkeys, and he said: I adjure you by Allah and Islam, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon Thabir with Abu Bakr, Umar and me, and the mountain moved until its stones fell to the foot, so he kicked it with his foot, saying: Be still, Thabir, for upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Allah is Most Great, they bore witness for me, by the Lord of the Kabah, that I am a martyr. He said that three times."
"305","322 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, by my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you, by reading to him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Uthman ibn Said Abu Amr and Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Al-Jurayri narrated to me, from Thumamah ibn Hazn al-Qushayri, he said: I witnessed the house on the day Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was struck; he looked down upon us from above the house and said: O people, bring me your two companions who set you upon me. The people gathered. They were brought, dragged as though they were two camels or two donkeys, and he said: I adjure you by Allah and Islam, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when there was no sweet well except Rumah, and he said: Who will buy the well of Rumah and make his bucket therein like the buckets of the Muslims, for better than it for him in Paradise? They said: O Allah, yes. So I bought it with my wealth; why do they prevent me from breaking fast upon it, so that I break fast upon seawater? I adjure you by Allah and Islam, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, when the mosque became crowded for its people: Who will buy the plot of so-and-so and expand the mosque thereby, for better than it for him in Paradise? So I bought it with my pure wealth? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah and Islam, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and I were upon Thabir of Makkah, and it shook, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with his foot, saying: Be still, Thabir, for upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: Then I heard him say: Allah is Most Great, they bore witness, by Allah, that I am a martyr; then he was entered upon and killed. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abbas al-Duri, from Said ibn Amir similarly, saying: A hasan hadith. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ayyub al-Tusi, from Said similarly. I say: As for the mention of the well of Rumah, al-Bukhari narrated it from the narration of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from him."
"306","Al-Harith, the freedman of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, also said to be named Barakat Abu Salih - 323 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqil informed me that he heard al-Harith, the freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, say: Uthman sat one day and we sat with him; the caller to prayer came, so he called for water in a vessel, I think about a mudd, and performed ablution, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution like this ablution of mine. He said: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then stands and prays Zuhr, he is forgiven what was between it and the Fajr prayer; then prays Asr, he is forgiven what is between it and Zuhr; then prays Maghrib, he is forgiven what was between it and Asr; then prays Isha, he is forgiven what was between it and Maghrib; then perhaps he sleeps tossing through his night; then if he rises, performs ablution and prays Fajr, he is forgiven what was between it and Isha. These are the good deeds that remove evil deeds. They said: These are the good deeds, so what are the enduring righteous deeds, O Uthman? He said: They are: There is no god but Allah, glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, Allah is Most Great, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah."
"307","324 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Abu Aqil informed me that he heard al-Harith, the freedman of Uthman, say: Uthman sat one day and we sat with him; the caller came, so he called for water in a vessel, I think it would contain a mudd, and performed ablution, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution like this ablution of mine, then said: Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then stands and prays Zuhr, he is forgiven what was between it and Fajr; then prays Asr, he is forgiven what is between it and Zuhr; then prays Maghrib, he is forgiven what is between it and Asr; then prays Isha, he is forgiven what is between it and Maghrib; then perhaps he sleeps tossing through his night; then if he rises, performs ablution and prays Fajr, he is forgiven what is between it and Isha, and these are the good deeds that remove evil deeds. They said: These are the good deeds, so what are the enduring ones, O Uthman? He said: They are: There is no god but Allah, glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, Allah is Most Great, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah. Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated it in his Musnad from al-Muqri, from Said ibn Ayyub and Haywah together, from Abu Aqil similarly."
"308","Another - 325 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, my father narrated to me, Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Zuhrah ibn Mabad al-Qurashi narrated to me, from Abu Salih, the freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, he said: I heard Uthman say upon the pulpit: O people, I concealed from you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), out of dislike that you disperse from me; then it occurred to me to narrate it to you so that each man may choose for himself what seems best to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Guarding a day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in other dwellings."
"309","326 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Misri informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed me, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Zuhrah ibn Mabad al-Qurashi narrated to us, and he mentioned with his chain the like of it, saying: O people, I concealed from you..."
"310","327 - Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Harimi informed us in his book that Abu Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them, by reading to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Abu Man narrated to us, Zuhrah ibn Mabad narrated to us, from Abu Salih, he said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in other than it. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Ibn al-Mubarak. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad from Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Layth. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, from Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik, saying: A hasan gharib hadith from this aspect. Al-Nasai narrated it as we narrated it from him, and from Amr ibn Mansur, from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, from al-Layth as we presented from him in abridged form. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Abu Man. Abu Man is Muhammad ibn Man al-Ghifari."
"311","Humran ibn Aban, the freedman of Uthman, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 328 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan informed us, saying: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, saying: Humran narrated to me, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan perform ablution: he washed his hands three times, washed his face three times, washed his forearms three times, wiped his head three times, and washed his feet three times, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution thus, saying: Whoever performs ablution less than this, it suffices him. We intended from this hadith only the wiping of the head three times. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Musa."
"312","Another - 329 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed us there that Abu al-Mahasin Asad ibn Ziyad informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar al-Dawudi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hurayth ibn al-Saib narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan say: Humran narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Affan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam has no right in other than these qualities: a house he lives in, a garment with which he covers his nakedness, coarse bread, and water."
"313","330 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud informed us, by reading to him, in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hurayth ibn al-Saib narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Humran ibn Aban, from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything in excess of the shade of a house, coarse bread, a garment covering the son of Adam's nakedness, and everything in excess of that, the son of Adam has no right in it."
"314","331 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hurayth ibn al-Saib narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan say: Humran narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Affan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything besides the shade of a house, coarse bread, a garment covering his nakedness, and water, whatever is in excess of this, the son of Adam has no right in them. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Hurayth. Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it in his Musnad from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan, from Muslim al-Azdi, from Hurayth, and from Ishaq ibn Abi Israil and Abu Khaythamah together. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd, saying: A sahih hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Hurayth ibn al-Saib narrated it from al-Hasan, from Humran, from Uthman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), erring in it; the correct is from al-Hasan, from Humran, from some of the People of the Book."
"315","Another - 332 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed me, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us. 333 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd informed us in al-Harbiyyah that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qatii narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Humran ibn Aban, that Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a word that no servant says truthfully from his heart except that he is forbidden to the Fire. Umar ibn al-Khattab said to him: I will tell you what it is: it is the word of sincerity that Allah, blessed and exalted, obligated Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to, and it is the word of piety that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pressed upon his uncle Abu Talib at death: the testimony that there is no god but Allah. The wording is Imam Ahmad's hadith; in Ibn Mani's narration he said: Uthman said, with him: truthfully from his heart and dies upon that except that Allah forbids him to the Fire. Umar said: Shall I not inform you of it: it is the word of sincerity, the word of piety, the word that he pressed upon his uncle at death: the testimony that there is no god but Allah. We have mentioned it in the Musnad of Umar ibn al-Khattab. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated it from Qatadah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Humran. Ayyub Abu al-Ala narrated it from Qatadah, from Humran, without mentioning Muslim ibn Yasar; the correct is the قول of whoever mentioned Muslim ibn Yasar."
"316","Rabah al-Kufi from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 334 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, the freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Rabah, he said: My family married me to a Roman slave girl of theirs; I had intercourse with her and she bore a black boy like me, so I named him Abd Allah. Then I had intercourse with her and she bore me a black boy like me, so I named him Ubayd Allah. Then a Roman boy of my family named Yuhannis took a fancy to her and spoke to her in his tongue, and she bore a boy like a gecko. I said to her: What is this? She said: He is Yuhannis's. So we were raised to the Commander of the Faithful Uthman. Mahdi said, and I think he said: He questioned them both and they confessed. He said to them both: Do you accept that I judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He judged that the child belongs to the bed. Mahdi said: I think he lashed him and her, and they were both slaves."
"317","335 - With the same chain Abu Yala informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Rabah, and he mentioned the like of it or close to it."
"318","336 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, by my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail informed you, by reading to him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan al-Araj informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, Rabah narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, in a story raised to him: I shall judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the child belongs to the bed. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Jarir ibn Hazim and Mahdi ibn Maymun. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad at length from Bahz and Yazid ibn Harun, from Mahdi. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Ismail, from Mahdi. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Mahdi ibn Maymun and Jarir ibn Hazim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Rabah, from Uthman; Hajjaj ibn Artah opposed them, narrating it from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from his father, with the hadith ascribed from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the first قول is more correct."
"319","Ribi ibn Hirash from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 337 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us, by reading to him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Bazzar informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Abu al-Faraj Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn al-Fadl ibn Jafar al-Majnazi informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hibban informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us, Yusuf ibn Musa, Ahmad ibn Mansur and others narrated to me, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Abu Sidan Ubayd ibn al-Tufayl, saying: Ribi ibn Hirash narrated to me, from Uthman, that he proposed to Umar for his daughter and he refused him; it reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when Umar went to him in the evening, he said: O Umar, shall I guide you to a son-in-law better for you than Uthman, and guide Uthman to a son-in-law better than you? He said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Marry me your daughter, and I shall marry Uthman my daughter. This is a chain with no harm in it, but in the Sahih is that Umar offered Hafsa to Uthman to marry her to him, and he replied: It has occurred to me not to marry, or to that meaning; then he offered her to Abu Bakr, who gave him no answer, the hadith."
"320","Saib ibn Yazid from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - 338 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: I heard Uthman say: Avoid wine, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named it the mother of evils."
"321","Said ibn al-Musayyib ibn Hazn from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 339 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shuayb Abu Shaybah narrated to me, saying: I heard Ata al-Khurasani say: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib say: I saw Uthman sitting at al-Maqaid; he called for food touched by fire and ate it, then rose to prayer and prayed. Then Uthman said: I sat at the sitting place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ate the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and prayed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"322","Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - 340 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Isbahani informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, he said: Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, adjured the people one day, saying: You know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended Uhud with Abu Bakr, Umar and me, and Uhud shook with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and me upon it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be firm, Uhud; upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs. Al-Bukhari narrated the like of it in his Sahih from the hadith of Said, from Qatadah, from Anas."
"323","Shaqiq ibn Salamah al-Asadi Abu Wail al-Kufi from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 341 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us, by reading to him, in Isfahan, it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, by reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated to us, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf met al-Walid ibn Uqbah and said: Why do I see you have shunned the Commander of the Faithful Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him? Abd al-Rahman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Convey to him that I did not stay back from Badr. That was conveyed to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: As for his قول that he did not stay back from Badr: I was nursing Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until she died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a share for me, and whoever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strikes a share for has indeed witnessed. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muawiyah longer than this."
"324","342 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Asim, from Shaqiq, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf met al-Walid ibn Uqbah, and al-Walid said to him: Why do I see you have shunned the Commander of the Faithful Uthman? Abd al-Rahman said to him: Convey to him that I did not flee on the day of Aynayn; Asim said, meaning the day of Uhud; nor did I stay back on the day of Badr, nor did I abandon the sunnah of Umar. He went and conveyed that to Uthman, who said: As for his قول that he did not flee on the day of Aynayn, how does he reproach me for a sin Allah has pardoned? He said: Those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met, Satan only caused them to slip because of some of what they earned, and Allah has pardoned them. As for his قول that he stayed back on the day of Badr: I was nursing Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until she died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck my share for me, and whoever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strikes his share for has indeed witnessed. As for his قول that he did not abandon the sunnah of Umar: neither I nor he can bear it, so go and convey that to him. Abu Yala narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Khaythamah, from Muawiyah ibn Amr."
"325","Another - 343 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir and Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed me, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri informed us, from Israil, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wail, he said: I saw Uthman perform ablution: he washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped his head, ran his fingers through his beard, wiped his ears, their outer and inner, washed his feet three times, and ran water between his fingers three times, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution."
"326","344 - Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil informed us in Baghdad that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn al-Fadl al-Mukhbiri informed us, Abd Allah ibn Hababah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq, he said: I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution: he washed his palms three times, rinsed three times, sniffed three times, washed his feet three times, ran water between his fingers, and ran his fingers through his beard when he washed his face, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do. As for the description of ablution, it was narrated in the Sahih from more than one aspect, without mention of running fingers through or wiping the ears. Allah knows best."
"327","345 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by reading to him while present: Abu Nuaym informed us, Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, he said: I saw Uthman perform ablution: he washed his palms three by three, rinsed, sniffed three by three, washed his face three times - he said, and I thought he said: and his forearms three by three - wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner, then washed his feet three by three, ran water between his fingers, and ran his fingers through his beard when he washed his face before washing his feet, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, from Khalaf ibn al-Walid, from Israil, and from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, declaring it sahih."
"328","346 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, by my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed you, while you were present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ishaq narrated to us, saying: We read to Abd al-Razzaq, from Israil ibn Yunus, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, that Uthman performed ablution and ran his fingers through his beard, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated the running of fingers through the beard from Yahya ibn Musa. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Khalaf, both from Abd al-Razzaq."
"329","347 - Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn al-Fadl ibn Jafar informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Hababah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah al-Baghawi informed us, Ali ibn al-Jad ibn Ubayd al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban informed us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, he said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salamah say: I witnessed Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, perform ablution three by three, separating rinsing from sniffing, then saying: Thus the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution. Ibn Majah narrated it similarly from Mahmud ibn Khalid, from al-Walid, from Thawban."
"330","Dahhak ibn Qays al-Tamimi Abu Bahr al-Ahnaf from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 348 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Hudbah narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Jawan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays. 349 - Ibn Abi Asim said: Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Jawan, from al-Ahnaf, he said: We came to Madinah intending Hajj; Uthman came, and it was said: This is Uthman. He wore a yellow wrap with which he had covered his head, and said: Is Ali here? They said: Yes. He said: Is Talhah here? They said: Yes. He said: Is al-Zubayr here? They said: Yes. He said: Is Sad here? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides Whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys the drying-yard of so-and-so, Allah will forgive him? So I bought it for twenty thousand or twenty-five thousand, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought it. He said: Place it in our mosque, and its reward is yours? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides Whom there is no god, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the faces of the people and said: Whoever equips these, he is forgiven - meaning the army of hardship - so I equipped them until they lacked neither halter nor tether? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness - three times. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys Rumah, Allah will forgive him? So I bought it for such and such, then came to him and said to him: I have bought it. He said: Make it a watering place for the Muslims, and its reward is yours."
"331","350 - Al-Muayyad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umar ibn Jawan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, he said: I heard him say: We came to Madinah intending Hajj; while we were in our lodging laying down our baggage, it was said: The people have rushed to the mosque and gathered therein, so we went, and it was crowded with its people; if you threw a pebble it would fall upon a man. When I drew near, there were Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas. No sooner had Uthman come, covered with a yellow sheet, and some said: This is Ibn Affan, and he came until he drew near them, saying: Is Ali here? They said: Yes. Then he said: Then so-and-so, then so-and-so? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides Whom there is no god: Do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys the drying-yard of so-and-so, Allah will forgive him? So I bought it, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought the drying-yard of so-and-so. He said: Place it in the mosque, and its reward is yours? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys Rumah, Allah will forgive him? So I bought it, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have bought it. He said: Make it a watering place for the Muslims, and its reward is yours? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah besides Whom there is no god, do you know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the faces of the people on the day of the army of hardship and said: Whoever equips these, Allah will forgive him? So I equipped them until they lacked neither tether nor halter, so I equipped them? They said: Yes indeed. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Awanah similarly. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Bahz, from Abu Awanah. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Idris, from Husayn, from Umar ibn Jawan; and from Ishaq, from al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman, from his father, from Husayn, from Amr ibn Jawan similarly, without mentioning al-Zubayr. It is said Umar ibn Jawan is correct. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Bukhari narrated, and Abdan said: My father narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that Uthman looked down upon them and said: I adjure you by Allah, and I adjure none but the Companions of Muhammad the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips the army of hardship, for him is Paradise? So I equipped them. Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever digs the well of Rumah, for him is Paradise? So I dug it. He said... He said: So they affirmed what he said."
"332","Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 351 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Asim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, my father informed me, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan say: Nothing prevents me from narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that I be the most retentive of his Companions from him; but I bear witness that I heard him say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"333","352 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from his father, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that he heard Uthman ibn Affan."
"334","353 - Abu Yala said: Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us from his father, from Amir ibn Sad, that he heard Uthman say: Nothing prevented me from narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that I not be the most retentive of his Companions; but I bear witness that I heard him say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ishaq ibn Isa, Surayj and Husayn, all from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from his father. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"335","Abbad ibn Zahir Abu al-Ruwa from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 354 - Abu Tahir ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah informed us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abbad ibn Zahir Abu Ruwa say: I heard Uthman preach, saying: By Allah, we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in travel and residence; he would visit our sick, follow our funerals, fight with us, and console us with little and much. Yet people inform me about him; perhaps one of them never saw him at all."
"336","355 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ghundar, from Shubah, from Simak. 356 - Al-Haytham said, and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Abbad ibn Zahir Abu Ruwa say: I heard Uthman preach, saying: By Allah, we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in residence and travel."
"337","357 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abbad ibn Zahir Abu Ruwa say: I heard Uthman preach, saying: By Allah, we accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in travel and residence; he would visit our sick, escort our funerals, fight with us, and console us with little and much. Yet people inform me about him; perhaps one of them never saw him at all. He said: Ayan, the son of al-Farazdaq's wife, said to him: O Nathal, you have altered. He said: Who is this? They said: Ayan. He said: Rather you, O slave. The people leapt upon Ayan, and a man of Banu Layth kept restraining them from him until he brought him into the house."
"338","Abd Allah ibn Habib al-Sulami Abu Abd al-Rahman from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 358 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: When Uthman was besieged, he looked down upon them from above his house, then said: I remind you by Allah, do you know that when Hira shook, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be firm, Hira, for upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr? They said: Yes. He said: I remind you by Allah, do you know that no one drank from Rumah except for a price, so I bought it with my wealth, then made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer? They said: Yes. He said: I remind you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the army of hardship: Whoever spends an accepted expenditure, while the people that day were strained and poor, so I equipped a third of that army from my wealth? They said: Yes, among things he enumerated."
"339","359 - Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dimashqi informed us, by reading to him more than once, it was said to him: Your grandfather Abu al-Qasim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Missisi informed us, by reading to him: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn al-Qasim ibn Aban ibn Abi Nasr informed us, Abu al-Hasan Hamad ibn Sulayman ibn Haydarah al-Qurashi informed us, Abu Umar Hilal ibn al-Ala al-Raqqi narrated to us, my father, Abd Allah ibn Jafar and Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: When Uthman was besieged in his house, the people gathered around his house, and Uthman looked down upon them, saying: I adjure by Allah a man who heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Hira shook with us, saying: Be firm, for upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr? And people who heard that said: We heard it. Then he said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends an accepted expenditure for the army of hardship, while the people that day were strained and poor, so I equipped the army from my wealth? They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that Rumah, no one drank from it except for a price, so I bought it with my wealth for the poor, the rich, the wayfarer, and people generally? They said: Yes. Among things he enumerated to them."
"340","360 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us, by reading to him in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Bazzar informed you, by reading to him: Abu al-Faraj Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn al-Fadl ibn Jafar al-Muhzi informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad, Abd Allah ibn Jafar and Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us - the wording is Abu Nasr's - Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, he said: When Uthman, may Allah have mercy on him, was besieged and his house surrounded, he looked down upon the people, saying: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when Hira shook with us, said: Be firm, Hira, for upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the campaign of hardship: Whoever spends an accepted expenditure, while the people that day were poor and strained, so I equipped a third of the army from my wealth? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that Rumah, no one drank from it except for a price, so I bought it with my wealth and made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer? They said: O Allah, yes. Among things he enumerated. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Jafar, saying: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from the hadith of Abu Abd al-Rahman. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Wahb, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah similarly. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar, from Abu Nasr al-Tammar, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abu Ishaq al-Sabii narrates it, with disagreement from him: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, Shubah and Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami; Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq and Israil opposed them, narrating it from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman; the قول of Shubah and whoever followed him is more like correct. We already stated that al-Bukhari mentioned part of this hadith in his book without mentioning his hearing it from Abdan; in this is the addition of Hira shaking, with a witness in al-Bukhari from the narration of Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: This narration is more like correct. Allah knows best."
"341","Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 361 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us, by reading to him while we listened, in Isfahan, it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, by reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zayd informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said while preaching upon the pulpit: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); nothing prevented me from narrating it to you except miserliness toward you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Guarding a night in the path of Allah is better than a thousand nights whose night is stood in prayer and whose day is fasted. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Rawh, from Kahmas, from Musab, from Uthman."
"342","362 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi narrated to us, al-Ansari narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Musab ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Uthman ibn Affan said while preaching upon the pulpit: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); nothing prevented me from narrating it to you except miserliness. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Guarding a night in the path of Allah is better than a thousand nights whose day is fasted and whose night is stood in prayer. Some imams criticized Musab ibn Thabit, but this supports what preceded from the hadith of Abu Salih, the freedman of Uthman. Ibn Majah narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Musab. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri and Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated it from Kahmas, from Musab, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Uthman; Muslim ibn Ibrahim said it from Jafar. Khalid ibn Abi Yazid al-Qarani said: from Jafar, from Kahmas, from Musab ibn Thabit, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Uthman as mursal; that is what Abd Allah ibn Idris, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, Ghundar and Rawh ibn Ubadah said from Kahmas, and it is correct."
"343","Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah al-Anazi from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - 363 - Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Harimi informed us, by license, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad al-Duni informed them, by license if not by hearing: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai informed us, Ibrahim ibn Yaqub informed us, Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Umamah ibn Sahl and Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah narrated to me, saying: We were with Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was besieged; when we entered a passage we heard the speech of those on the courtyard. Uthman entered one day, then came out, saying: They are threatening me with killing. We said: Allah will suffice you against them. He said: And why would they kill me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after chastity, or kills a soul without a soul. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam, nor did I wish to exchange my religion since Allah guided me, nor did I kill a soul, so for what would they kill me? Al-Nasai narrated it thus in his Sunan. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba Abu Jafar narrated it from Hammad, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl and Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Uthman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); others narrate it from Hammad, from Yahya, from Abu Umamah alone, from Uthman; the hadith of Abd Allah ibn Amir is another hadith stopped as mawquf upon Uthman; Muhammad ibn Isa erred in joining him with Abu Umamah in this hadith."
"344","Abd Allah ibn Darah, the freedman of Uthman, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 364 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: Al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Maryam, he said: I visited Ibn Darah, the freedman of Uthman, and he heard me rinsing; he said: O Muhammad. I said: At your service. He said: Shall I not tell you about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I saw Uthman at al-Maqaid call for ablution water; he rinsed three times, sniffed three times, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped his head three times, and washed his feet, then said: Whoever loves to look at the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then this is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The hadith of Abu Salamah from Humran about wiping the head three times has preceded, which is what we intended with the hadith here. Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Safwan ibn Isa with his chain, mentioning it."
"345","Abd Allah ibn Abbas from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - 365 - Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Sultan ibn al-Bayyi informed us, by my reading to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf al-Urmawi informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar, known as Ibn al-Muslimah, informed us, by reading to him, while I listened: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Bazzar, known as al-Adami, informed us, by reading to him: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ashath al-Sijistani al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar, Ibn Abi Adi and Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Awf ibn Abi Jamilah informed us, saying: Yazid al-Farisi narrated to me, saying: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, narrated to me, he said: I said to Uthman: What led you to take al-Anfal, which is of the Mathani, and Baraah, which is of the Miin, joining them without writing between them: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, placing them among the seven long ones? What led you to that? Uthman said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as time passed over him with numerous surahs descending upon him, when something descended upon him would call one of those who wrote, saying: Place these verses in the surahs in which such and such is mentioned. Al-Anfal was among the earliest revealed in Madinah, and Baraah was among the last of the Quran; their stories were similar, so I thought it was of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away without clarifying to us that it was of it; for that reason I joined them without writing between them the line: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, placing it among the seven long ones."
"346","366 - With this chain Abd Allah, that is Ibn Abi Dawud, narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Awf al-Arabi narrated to us, from Yazid al-Farisi, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: I said to Uthman, and he mentioned the like of it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ismail ibn Ibrahim and Yahya ibn Said, both from Awf. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it from Amr ibn Awn, from Hushaym, from Awf, and from Ziyad ibn Ayyub. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, saying: A hasan hadith known only from the hadith of Awf from Yazid. Al-Nasai narrated it in Fadail al-Quran from Muhammad ibn Muthanna, from Yahya ibn Said. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Musa ibn Hilal al-Abdi narrated it from Awf, from Asas ibn Salamah, from Uthman; Yahya al-Qattan, Ibn Ulayyah, Ghundar and Ibn Abi Adi opposed him, narrating it from Awf, from Yazid al-Farisi, from Ibn Abbas, from Uthman, and it is correct."
"347","Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - 367 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, saying: I heard Mughirah ibn Muslim mention, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that Uthman looked down upon his companions, saying: For what are they killing me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who commits adultery after chastity, upon him is stoning; or kills, upon him is retaliation; or apostatizes after his Islam, upon him is killing. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam ever, nor did I kill anyone so that I requite myself from him, nor did I apostatize since I embraced Islam. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"348","368 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Mughirah ibn Muslim Abu Salamah mention, from Matar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Uthman looked down upon his companions while besieged, saying: For what are they killing me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: a man who commits adultery after chastity, upon him is stoning; or kills deliberately, upon him is retaliation; or apostatizes after his Islam, upon him is killing. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam, nor did I kill anyone so that I requite myself from him, nor did I apostatize since I embraced Islam. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abu al-Azhar al-Naysaburi, from Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi."
"349","Abd Allah ibn Mawhab al-Filistini from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 369 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah narrate, from Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, that Uthman said to Ibn Umar: Go and be a judge. He said: Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: Go and judge among people. He said: Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: I insist upon you, you must go and judge. He said: Do not hasten; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks refuge by Allah has sought a refuge. He said: Yes. He said: I seek refuge by Allah from being a judge. He said: And what prevents you, when your father used to judge? He said: Because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is a judge and judges unjustly is of the people of the Fire; whoever is a judge and judges ignorantly is of the people of the Fire; whoever is a knowledgeable judge and judges by truth or justice will ask to escape even. Then what do I hope from it afterward? Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman, from Abd al-Malik, saying: Gharib, and its chain is in my view not continuous. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Umayyah ibn Bistam with his chain, with Abd Allah ibn Wahb therein, saying: Abd Allah ibn Wahb is Abd Allah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah ibn al-Aswad al-Qurashi, of the people of Madinah; al-Zuhri narrated from him. Allah knows best what is correct of that. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah is unknown. Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated part of it from Umayyah ibn Bistam with his chain, saying: Abd Allah ibn Wahb. Hamdan ibn Amr al-Mawsili narrated the like of it from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Sallam, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, that Uthman ibn Affan said to Abd Allah ibn Umar: Judge among people."
"350","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 370 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Mansur Mahmud al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ismail ibn Masud al-Jahdari and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi narrated to us, saying: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me, from his father, he said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan preach to us, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Avoid the mother of evils, for there was a man among those before you. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"351","371 - The Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi informed us in his book that Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Qaydas al-Hattab informed them, by his reading to him: Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Nashwan al-Sukkari the witness informed us in his license: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Jawri informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abi al-Dunya al-Qurashi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi al-Basri narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith informed me, from his father Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Uthman preaching, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Avoid the mother of evils, for there was a man among those before you who worshipped and kept apart from people, and a seductive woman became attached to him and sent her servant to him, saying: We call you for testimony. He entered, and each time he entered a door she locked it behind him, until he came to a beautiful seated woman, with a boy beside her and a jar containing wine. She said: We did not call you for testimony; rather I called you to kill this boy, or lie with me, or drink a cup of this wine; if you refuse, I shall scream and disgrace you. When he saw there was no escape, he said: Give me a cup of this wine to drink. She gave him a cup of wine, then he said: Give me more. He did not move until he lay with her and killed the soul. So avoid wine, for by Allah, faith and addiction to wine never combine in a man's breast; one of them is bound to expel the other. Ibn Abi al-Dunya narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, from his father, from his grandfather, from Uthman, saying: Wine is the جمع of evils, mentioning the like of it stopped as mawquf from Uthman's قول. Al-Nasai narrated it from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Abd Allah, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri with his chain stopped as mawquf. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi with his chain at length, saying: Umar ibn Said ibn Surayh is of the trustworthy of Madinah; Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Madani narrated from him. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Umar ibn Said ibn Surayh raised it from al-Zuhri, while Yunus, Mamar, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah and others stopped it from al-Zuhri; the stopped form is correct."
"352","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Dhubab from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 372 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala informed us, Musa, that is Ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, Abu Attab Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to me, from his father, that Uthman prayed with them at Mina four units, then turned to them, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a man marries in a land, he is of its people. I only completed because I married here since I arrived."
"353","373 - With the same chain Abu Yala said: Ubayd Allah, that is Ibn Umar, narrated to us, Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Dhubab of the people of Madinah narrated to me, my father Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to me, that Uthman ibn Affan prayed with the people of Mina four units, mentioning the like of it."
"354","374 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim al-Bahili narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to us, from his father, that Uthman ibn Affan prayed at Mina four units and the people objected to him, so he said: O people, I married in Makkah since I arrived, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever marries in a land, let him pray the prayer of the resident."
"355","Ata ibn Farrukh, the freedman of Quraysh, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 375 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ata ibn Farrukh, the freedman of the Qurashis, that Uthman bought land from a man who delayed upon him; he met him and said to him: What prevents you from taking your money? He said: You overcharged me, and I meet no one among people but he blames me. He said: Is that what prevents you? He said: Yes. He said: Then choose between your land and your money. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, admitted to Paradise a man who was easy as buyer and seller."
"356","376 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, my father narrated to me, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, narrated to us, Ata ibn Farrukh, the freedman of the Qurashis, narrated to me, that Uthman bought land from a man who delayed upon him; he met him and said to him: What prevents you from taking your money? He said: You overcharged me, and I meet no one among people but he blames me. He said: Is that what prevents you? He said: Yes. He said: Then choose between your land and your money. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, admitted to Paradise a man easy as buyer, seller, payer and claimant. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Yunus. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, both from Ismail ibn Ibrahim Ibn Ulayyah similarly. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrates it from Ata ibn Farrukh; Yunus has two other chains therein: from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, said by Mughirah ibn Muslim from Yunus; and from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, said by Ibrahim ibn Tahman from Yunus; and it is said: from Yunus, from a man, from al-Maqburi. The hadith of Ata ibn Farrukh is the most famous of them from him, and all are preserved from Yunus."
"357","Alqamah ibn Qays al-Nakhai Abu Shibl from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 377 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ismail narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: I was with Ibn Masud while he was with Uthman, and Uthman said to him: What remains of you for women? When women were mentioned, Ibn Masud said: Come near, O Alqamah. I was a young man. Uthman said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to youths of the Emigrants, saying: Whoever among you has means, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards the private part; whoever cannot, then fasting is a shield for him. Imam Ahmad narrated it thus in his Musnad. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Zurarah, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim. Yahya ibn Main was asked about the hadith of Abu Mashar and said: An error; al-Amash opposed him. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abu Mashar Ziyad ibn Kulayb narrates it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah; Yunus ibn Ubayd, Khalid al-Hadhdha and Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated it from him. Mansur, al-Amash, Abu Hamzah, Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, al-Mughirah and al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah opposed him, narrating it from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah; the preserved is from Ibn Masud, and Abu Mashar was not followed in his قول: from Uthman."
"358","Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan from his father, may Allah be pleased with him - 378 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: I heard my uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Musa say: Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, he said: My father said to me: O my son..."
"359","379 - With the same chain Abu Yala said: Ishaq ibn Ismail al-Talqani narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to me, saying: I heard my father Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Musa say: I heard my uncle Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Musa say: Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Amr ibn Uthman, he said: My father Uthman ibn Affan said: O my son, if you are put in charge of any affair of people, honor Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him."
"360","380 - I heard Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi al-Harawi there, saying: I heard my grandfather Abu Nasr Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Asim al-Sufi, and al-Darimi, that is Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad, saying: We heard Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Farisi say: I heard Abu Bakr al-Qarrab, that is Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Bishr, say: I heard Abu Ahmad, meaning Muhammad ibn Hamid ibn Mamar al-Sami, say: I heard Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi al-Basri say: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad say: I heard my father say: I heard my uncle say: I heard Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman say: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib say: I heard Amr ibn Uthman say: My father said to me: O my son, if you are put in charge of any affair of people, honor Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him. Al-Ghallabi was criticized by al-Daraqutni; we only brought it as supporting evidence. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hafs. The judge Abu Bakr ibn Abi Asim narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Ubayd Allah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala, from Ishaq al-Talqani. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, mentioned the disagreement, and said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Ayshi narrated it from his father thus, ضبط his chain."
"361","Another - 381 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us at Dar al-Qazz in Baghdad that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them. 382 - Abu al-Yumn Zayd ibn al-Hasan al-Kindi and Abu al-Barakat Dawud ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadiyyan informed us at Zahir Dimashq that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them, saying: Abu al-Ghanaim Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mamun informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Abu Yahya Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan narrated to me, from his father Uthman ibn Affan, he said: The most Quraysh harmed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that I saw him one day - Amr said: I saw Uthman's eyes shed tears at recalling that - Uthman ibn Affan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was circumambulating the House with his hand in Abu Bakr's hand, while in al-Hijr sat three men: Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt, Abu Jahl ibn Hisham and Umayyah ibn Khalaf. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed, so I drew near him until I placed myself between him and Abu Bakr, and he interlaced his fingers in mine, until we circled together. When he came parallel to them, Abu Jahl said: By Allah, we shall not make peace with you as long as sea wets wool, while you forbid us to worship what our fathers worshipped. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am that. Then he passed them, and they did the like to him in the third circuit, until in the fourth circuit they confronted him; Abu Jahl leapt wanting to seize his garment at the chest, so I pushed him in the chest and he fell upon his backside; Abu Bakr pushed Umayyah ibn Khalaf, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pushed Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt. Then they moved away from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he stood, then said to them: By Allah, you shall not desist until His punishment befalls you swiftly. Uthman said: By Allah, there was not a man among them but his lying seized him while he trembled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Evil people you are to your Prophet. Then he went to his house and we followed behind him until he reached his door, stood at the bench, then turned to us, saying: Rejoice, for Allah, mighty and majestic, shall make His religion prevail, perfect His word, and aid His Prophet. These whom you see are among those Allah shall slaughter soon by your hands. Then we went to our houses; by Allah, I saw Allah slaughter them by our hands. Al-Daraqutni said: This is a gharib hadith from the hadith of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, from his father; Abd Allah ibn Urwah is alone in it from his father, none narrated it from him but his son Salamah, and his son Abd Allah is alone in it from him."
"362","Mahmud ibn Labid al-Ansari from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 383 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed him, by reading to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub al-Tabarani informed us, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us. 384 - Al-Tabarani said: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Nasr ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from his father, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Uthman, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"363","385 - This Abu Jafar also informed us that al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them while present: Abu Nuaym informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat al-Razi narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi informed us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from his father, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Uthman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Bakr Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi. Muslim brought it in his Sahih: narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi with his chain. It already preceded in the narration of Amir ibn Sad similarly."
"364","Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 386 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us, by my reading to him in Isfahan, I said to him: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Qari al-Hafiz informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Hazmi al-Sukkari informed us, Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi narrated to us, Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Main informed us, Sawwar ibn Umarah, a shaykh at al-Ramlah, narrated to us, Massarrah ibn Mabad al-Lakhmi narrated to me, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah led us in Asr, then turned to us, saying: I prayed behind Marwan ibn al-Hakam and he prostrated these two prostrations, then turned to us informing us that he prayed behind Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he prostrated the like of these two prostrations, saying: I was with your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came, greeted him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I prayed and did not know whether I prayed even or odd. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him, saying: If Satan plays with you in your prayer and one does not know even or odd, let him prostrate two prostrations, for they complete his prayer. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Massarrah ibn Mabad, from Yazid, from Uthman. His son Abd Allah narrated it after him from Yahya ibn Main and Ziyad ibn Ayyub with his chain, with Marwan's mention similarly. Abu al-Qasim Tammam ibn Muhammad al-Razi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, Abu Yaqub al-Adhrui, Ali ibn Yaqub ibn Abi al-Aqib and others, saying: Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Nadri narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Umarah Abu Umarah al-Rabi at al-Ramlah in the year 214 narrated to us - I saw him dictating to Yahya ibn Main - Massarrah ibn Mabad narrated to us with his chain the like of it. Ali ibn Yaqub added in his hadith, saying: I heard Abu Zura say: This hadith is the capital."
"365","Mughirah ibn Shubah al-Thaqafi from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them - 387 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Al-Awzai informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, that he narrated to him from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that he visited Uthman while besieged, saying: You are the imam of the people, and what you see has befallen you; I offer you three options, choose whichever: either you go out and fight them, for with you are numbers and strength, you upon truth and they upon falsehood; or you open a door other than the one they hold, mount your camels and join Makkah, for they shall not deem you lawful while you are therein; or you join al-Sham, for they are the people of al-Sham with Muawiyah among them. Uthman said: As for going out to fight, I shall never be the first to succeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his nation by shedding blood. As for going out to Makkah, for they shall not deem you lawful therein: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man of Quraysh shall commit sacrilege at Makkah, upon him half the punishment of the world; I shall never be him. As for joining al-Sham, for they are the people of al-Sham with Muawiyah among them: I shall never leave my house of emigration and neighborhood of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"366","Hani, the freedman of Uthman, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 388 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Buhayr narrated to us, that Hani, the freedman of Uthman, narrates from Uthman, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished burying a man, he said: Seek forgiveness for your brother and ask firmness for him, for he is now being questioned. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Musa, from Hisham ibn Yusuf."
"367","Another - 389 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to me, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Buhayr al-Qass narrated to me, from Hani, the freedman of Uthman, he said: When Uthman stood at a grave, he wept until his beard was wet. It was said to him: Paradise and Hell are mentioned and you do not weep, yet you weep at this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grave is the first station of the Hereafter; if one escapes it, what follows is easier; if one does not escape it, what follows is harder. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I never saw a sight but the grave is more dreadful than it."
"368","390 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq, that is Ibn Abi Israil, narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Buhayr narrated to me, that he heard Hani, the freedman of Uthman, report from Uthman that when he stood at a grave he wept until his beard was wet. It was said to him: Paradise and Hell are mentioned and you do not weep, yet you weep at this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grave is the first station of the Hereafter; if one is saved from it, what follows is easier; if one is not saved from it, what follows is harder. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I never saw a sight but the grave is more dreadful than it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad, from Yahya ibn Main, saying: A hasan gharib hadith known only from the hadith of Hisham ibn Yusuf. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya."
"369","Abu Sahlah, the freedman of Uthman, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 391 - Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: Qays said: Abu Sahlah narrated to me that Uthman said on the day of the house when besieged: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a covenant to me, and I am patient upon it. Qays said: They used to view it as that day."
"370","392 - Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Khallal informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Sahlah, that Uthman said on the day of the house: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a covenant to me, and I am patient upon it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Sufyan ibn Waki, from his father, and Yahya ibn Said, from Ismail, saying: A hasan sahih hadith known only from the hadith of Ismail. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki. Sufyan narrated it from Ismail."
"371","393 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Musa, that is Ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Sahlah, the freedman of Uthman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall be tried after me, so do not fight."
"372","394 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dimashqi informed us there that his grandfather al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Missisi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Musa informed us, Khaythamah ibn Sulayman informed us, Hilal ibn al-Ala narrated to us, my father and Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim: Abu Sahlah, the freedman of Uthman, narrated to us, he said: I said to Uthman on the day of the house: Shall I fight, O Commander of the Faithful? And Abd Allah said: Fight, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: No, by Allah, I shall not fight; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised me a matter, and I am patient upon it."
"373","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him - 395 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, my father narrated to me, Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Uthman looked down from the palace while besieged, saying: I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hira when the mountain shook and he kicked it with his foot, then said: Be still, Hira; upon you is only a Prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr, and I was with him? And men responded to him. He said: I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Pledge of Ridwan when he sent me to the polytheists, to the people of Makkah. He said: This is my hand and this is Uthman's hand, and he pledged for me? And men responded to him. He said: I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Who will expand for us this house in the mosque, for a house for him in Paradise? So I bought it with my wealth and expanded the mosque with it? And men responded to him. He said: And I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the army of hardship say: Who will spend today an accepted expenditure? So I equipped half the army from my wealth. He said: And men responded to him. And I adjure by Allah whoever witnessed Rumah whose water was sold to the wayfarer, so I bought it with my wealth and made it free for the wayfarer? And men responded to him."
"374","396 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us, Ibn al-Munadi informed us, Ali ibn Bahr al-Qattan informed us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Uthman ibn Affan looked down upon them when they besieged him, mentioning the like of it, adding at its end: But my life seemed long to you, and you hastened, wanting to strip a garment Allah clothed me with; by Allah, I shall not remove it until I die or am killed. Al-Nasai narrated it from Imran ibn Bakkar ibn Rashad, from Khattab ibn Uthman, from Isa ibn Yunus similarly. Al-Daraqutni mentioned that the narration of Abu Abd al-Rahman which preceded is more deserving of correctness. I say: It is not far that both narrations are correct, for this narration has an addition over that narration; Abu Ishaq may have heard it from both, narrating it once from this and once from that. Allah knows best."
"375","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From the hadith of the Commander of the Faithful Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abi Talib, upon him be peace. Asid ibn Safwan from Ali, upon him be peace - 397 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Barakah ibn Mahfuz al-Daybaqi informed us, from the basis of his correct hearing before his confusion, I said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed you, by reading to him while you listened in the year 534: The Sharif Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muhtadi Billah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, by reading to him, and he acknowledged it: Muhammad ibn Makhlad and al-Husayn ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Mansur Zaj narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Musab al-Marwazi informed us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Madani narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Asid ibn Safwan, who had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, passed away and was covered, Madinah shook with weeping as on the day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. Ali, upon him be peace, came weeping, hastening, saying: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, saying: Today the succession of the Prophet is cut off, until he stood at the door of the house in which Abu Bakr lay covered, saying: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr; you were the intimate of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his companion, his rest, his trust, the place of his secret and consultation. You were the first of the people in Islam, the purest in faith, the firmest in certainty, the most fearful of Allah, the greatest in service to Allah's religion, the most watchful over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the most devoted to Islam, the most trusted over his Companions, the best in companionship, the most in virtues, the most in precedences, the highest in degree, the nearest in means, the most resembling him in guidance, conduct, mercy and excellence, the noblest in station, the dearest to him, the most firmly trusted with him. May Allah reward you for His Messenger and Islam with good. You were to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as hearing and sight. You believed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when people, meaning mankind, belied him, so Allah named you in His revelation a truthful one, saying: And he who brought the truth and believed in it, Abu Bakr. You consoled him when they were miserly, were with him at hardships when they sat back from him, accompanied him in severity with the noblest companionship, the second of two, his companion in the cave, upon whom tranquility was sent, his companion in emigration, his successor in Allah's religion and his nation with the best succession when people apostatized. You upheld the matter as no successor of a prophet ever did. You were strong when your companions weakened, prominent when they were weak, and held to the path of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they hesitated. You were truly the successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), uncontested and undivided, despite hypocrites, the plotting of disbelievers, envy of enviers, rancor of transgressors, and rage of rebels. You upheld the matter when they failed, spoke when they stammered, went with Allah's light when they sat. They followed you and were guided. You were the lowest in voice, the highest above, the fewest in speech, the soundest in قول, the longest in silence, the most eloquent, the most in opinion, the most generous in soul, the most knowledgeable of affairs, the noblest in knowledge. By Allah, you were the chief of the religion, first when people fled from it, last when they accepted. You were to believers a merciful father when they became dependent upon you; you bore the burdens they were too weak for, tended what they neglected, preserved by your knowledge what they obeyed of what they ignored, were diligent when they submitted, rose when they panicked, were patient when they despaired, attained the traces they sought, and they regained their right guidance by your opinion, succeeding and attaining through you what they did not expect. You were upon disbelievers a poured and flaming punishment, and to believers mercy, comfort and fortress. By Allah, you attained its richness, won its gift, carried its virtues, attained its precedences. Your proof never weakened, your heart never swerved, you never cowered. You were like a mountain storms do not move nor violent winds remove. You were as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most gracious of people to him in your companionship and wealth. You were as the Messenger of Allah said: Weak in body, strong in Allah's command, mighty and exalted. Humble in yourself, great with Allah, eminent in believers' eyes, great in their souls. None had a slur against you, no speaker a taunt, none a covetous hope in you, no creature indulgence with you. The weak humbled with you is strong and mighty until you take his right for him; the strong mighty with you is weak and humbled until you take the right from him; near and far alike in that. Nearest to you are the most obedient to Allah, mighty and exalted, and most God-fearing. Your concern is truth, sincerity and gentleness; your قول is judgment, your command decisive, your opinion knowledge and resolve. You conveyed, the path laid, difficulty eased, fires extinguished. By you religion straightened, faith strengthened, you led Islam and Muslims. Allah's command appeared though disbelievers disliked. You unveiled them and they saw. By Allah, you preceded a distant precedence and wearied those after you severely. You won good with manifest winning. You transcended weeping, your loss was great in heaven, your calamity crushed mankind. To Allah we belong and to Him we return. We are pleased with Allah's decree and submit to His command. By Allah, Muslims shall never after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be afflicted with the like of you ever. You were to religion might, protection and cave; to believers party, fortress and aid; upon hypocrites harshness and rage. May Allah join you to your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not deprive us your reward, nor mislead us after you. To Allah we belong and to Him we return. He said: The people held back until he finished his speech, then wept until their voices rose, saying: You spoke truth, by Allah, O son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"376","398 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that the Imam Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Umar al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us, Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Awwam al-Wasiti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Asid ibn Safwan, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, died and they covered him with a garment, Madinah shook with weeping and the people were stunned as on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came weeping, saying: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, saying: Today the succession of the Prophet is cut off, until he stood at the door of the house in which Abu Bakr lay, saying: May Allah have mercy on you, O Abu Bakr; you were the first of the people in Islam, the purest in faith, the firmest in certainty, the most fearful of Allah, the greatest in service, the most watchful over His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the most devoted to Islam, the most trusted over his Companions. The best in companionship, the most excellent in virtues, the most in precedences, the highest in degree, the nearest to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the most resembling him in guidance, character, conduct and excellence, the noblest in station, the dearest to him, the most firmly trusted with him. May Allah reward you for Islam, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Muslims with good. You believed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when people belied him, so Allah named you in His Book a truthful one: And he who brought the truth, Muhammad the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and believed in it, Abu Bakr. You consoled him when they were miserly, stood with him when they sat back from him. You accompanied him in severity with the noblest companionship, the second of two and his companion, upon whom tranquility was sent, his companion in emigration and places of hardship. You succeeded him over his nation with the best succession when people apostatized, upheld Allah's religion with an upholding no successor of a prophet ever did. You were strong when your companions weakened, prominent when they submitted, risen when they weakened, holding to the path of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they hesitated, undivided despite hypocrites, rancor of transgressors, rage of disbelievers, and envy of enviers. You upheld the matter when they failed, spoke when they stammered, went with Allah's light when they stopped, and they followed you and were guided. You were the lowest in voice, the highest above, the fewest in speech and soundest in قول, the longest in silence, the most eloquent in قول. You were the greatest in opinion, the bravest in heart, the firmest in certainty, the best in deed, the most knowledgeable of affairs. By Allah, you were the chief of the religion, first when people dispersed from it, last when they accepted. You were to believers a merciful father when they became dependent upon you; you bore of burdens what they were too weak for, preserved what they wasted, tended what they neglected, were diligent when they submitted, rose when they panicked, were patient when they despaired. You attained the traces they sought, and they attained through you what they did not expect. You were upon disbelievers a poured punishment and flame, and to Muslims rain and fertility. By Allah, you were endowed with its richness, won its gift, carried its virtues, secured its precedences. Your proof never dulled, your heart never swerved, your insight never weakened, your soul never cowered nor betrayed. You were like a mountain storms do not move nor violent winds remove. You were as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most gracious of people to him in your companionship and wealth. And as he said: Weak in body, strong in Allah's command. Humble in yourself, great with Allah, eminent on earth, great with believers. None had a taunt against you, no speaker a slur, none a covetous hope in you, nor indulgence with you for anyone. The weak humbled with you is strong and mighty until you take his right for him; the strong mighty with you is weak until you take the right from him; near and far with you alike in that. Your concern is truth, sincerity and gentleness; your قول is judgment and decree, your command forbearance and resolve, your opinion knowledge and determination. You conveyed, the path laid, difficulty eased, fires extinguished. By you religion straightened and faith strengthened. Allah's command appeared though disbelievers disliked; Islam and believers stood firm. By Allah, you preceded a distant precedence and wearied those after you severely, won good with manifest winning. You transcended weeping, your loss was great in heaven, your calamity crushed mankind. To Allah we belong and to Him we return. We are pleased with Allah's decree and submit to His command. By Allah, Muslims shall never after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) be afflicted with the like of you ever. You were to religion might and cave, to believers fortress, party and comfort, and upon hypocrites harshness and rage. May Allah join you to your Prophet, upon him be peace, may Allah not deprive us your reward nor mislead us after you. To Allah we belong and to Him we return. The people fell silent until his speech ended, and wept as on the day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died. They said: You spoke truth, O son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it thus in his Musnad."
"377","399 - The Imam Hafiz Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us, by license, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by reading to him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, by dictation: Salamah ibn Nahid and Muhammad ibn al-Khuzaz narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Walid al-Tabarani narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Asid ibn Safwan, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, died, they covered him with a garment; Madinah shook with weeping, and people were stunned as on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came weeping, saying: To Allah we belong and to Him we return, mentioning the hadith at length, with therein: and the greatest in virtues; therein: in guidance, conduct, character and demeanor; therein: and the soundest in قول, the firmest in certainty, the bravest in heart, the best in intellect, the most knowledgeable of affairs. By Allah, you were the chief of the religion, first when people dispersed from it, last when they were few. Abd Allah ibn Abi Dawud narrated it from Ali ibn Harb, from Dalham ibn Yazid, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Asid. Imran al-Qattan narrated it from Abu Hafs al-Adawi, that is Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Malik, from Asid. Hammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hammad narrated it from Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr. Umar ibn Ibrahim is Abu Hafs al-Abdi al-Basri. Yahya ibn Main said: Trustworthy. Abu Hatim said: Not used as proof. Our قول already preceded: Abu Hatim al-Razi, may Allah have mercy on him, said of more than one of the men of the Sahih: not used as proof, without clarifying the criticism, so criticism is not accepted without clarifying what it is. Allah knows best. As for the narration of Hammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hammad and his addition of Ismail ibn Ayyash in the chain, it may be he memorized it, and may be he erred, for most narrations come without mentioning Ismail. Allah knows best what is correct. This Hammad, I did not see him in al-Bukhari's book nor in Ibn Abi Hatim's book."
"378","Iyas ibn Amir al-Ghafiqi, counted among Egyptians, from Ali, upon him be peace - 400 - Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit, known as Ibn Jawaliq, informed us, by reading to him while we listened, in Baghdad, it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed you, by reading to him: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi: My uncle Iyas ibn Amir narrated to me that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"379","401 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali, known as Ibn al-Matush, informed me, by my reading to him on the west side of Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Abd al-Rahman informed us, Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, my uncle Iyas ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would glorify Allah at night while Aishah lay across between him and the qiblah. Musa ibn Ayyub was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Main. Iyas ibn Amir, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: He narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib and Uqbah ibn Amir. His nephew Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi narrated from him, counted among Egyptians. I heard my father and Abu Zura say that."
"380","Burayd ibn Asram from Ali, upon him be peace - 402 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to me, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Utaybah, that is the blind, informed us, from Burayd ibn Asram, he said: I heard Ali say: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, he left a dinar and a dirham. He said: Two brands; pray over your companion."
"381","403 - With the same chain Abd Allah narrated to us: My father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Utaybah narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Asram, he said: I heard Ali say: A man of the people of al-Suffah died, leaving two dinars or two dirhams. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over your companion. Burayd ibn Asram was mentioned by Ibn Abi Hatim in his book without mentioning criticism of him. Thalabah ibn Yazid al-Himmani from Ali, upon him be peace, some saying Yazid ibn Thalabah."
"382","404 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by reading to him while present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah informed us, Said, that is Ibn Sulayman, informed us, Abbad informed us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Hakam, from Thalabah ibn Yazid or Yazid ibn Thalabah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me not to leave a raised grave in Madinah but level it, nor an image but efface it. I did so, then came to him, and he said: Did you do it? I said: Yes. He said: O Ali, do not be a trial-maker, a tax-collector, nor a merchant, except a merchant of good; for those are preceded in deeds. Its beginning was brought in the Sahih from the narration of Abu al-Hayyaj. Thalabah ibn Yazid, al-Bukhari said: He heard Ali; Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated from him. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit and Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated from him; I heard my father say that."
"383","Another - 405 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr informed us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Thalabah al-Himmani, he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. I bear witness that among what he confided to me: This shall be dyed from the blood of this, meaning his beard from the blood of his head. Its beginning was brought in the two Sahihs similarly from the narration of Ribi ibn Khirash, from Ali, upon him be peace."
"384","Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai the Companion from Ali, upon him be peace - 406 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh ibn Mahmud informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith informed us, Abu Hudhayfah al-Thalabi informed us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, for three qualities for my nation; He granted me two and withheld one. I said: O Lord, do not destroy my nation by hunger. He said: Yours is this. I said: O Lord, do not empower over them an enemy from other than them, meaning the people of polytheism, who would exterminate them. He said: Yours is that. I said: O Lord, do not place their violence among them. He withheld this from me. Abu Hudhayfah, his name is Hammad ibn Umayr; Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him in his book. Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah was criticized by some scholars. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Thawban."
"385","Jurayy ibn Kulayb al-Nahdi from Ali, upon him be peace - 407 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb al-Nahdi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the one with broken horn and ear."
"386","408 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Husayn ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj informed us, Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Jurayy ibn Kulayb say: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking of horn and ear. Qatadah said: I asked Said ibn al-Musayyib, saying: What is breaking of the ear? He said: When it is half or more than that. Ibn al-Madini said: Jurayy is unknown; I know none narrated from him but Qatadah. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani said: None narrated from him but Qatadah. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Qatadah and Abu Ishaq al-Sabii narrated from him. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Yahya ibn Said, from Hisham, from Qatadah; and from Affan, from Hammam, from Qatadah. Abu Dawud narrated it similarly from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Hisham, from Qatadah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad, from Yahya ibn Said, from Qatadah, saying: A hasan sahih hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Humayd ibn Masadah, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Said. Al-Nasai narrated it from Humayd ibn Masadah, from Sufyan ibn Habib, from Shubah, without mentioning the ear."
"387","Habib ibn Himaz al-Asadi al-Kufi from Ali, upon him be peace - 409 - Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, by reading to him there, I said to him: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Fudayl informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Muhallim ibn Ismail al-Dabbi informed us, al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sarraj informed us, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Habib ibn Himaz, he said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib when a man asked him about Dhu al-Qarnayn, how he reached east and west? He said: Glory be to Allah; the cloud was subjected to him, means extended for him, and light spread for him. He said: Shall I add for you? The man fell silent, and Ali fell silent. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Habib ibn Himaz narrated from Ali and Abu Dharr. Simak ibn Harb and Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated from him."
"388","Hujr al-Adawi from Ali, upon him be peace - 410 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja al-Waiz informed us at Zahir al-Qahirah that Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur al-Harawi informed them, by reading to him: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim al-Azdi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Jarrahi informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub informed us, Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us, al-Qasim ibn Dinar al-Kufi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Israil, from al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from al-Hakam ibn Jahl, from Hujr al-Adawi, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: We have taken the zakat of al-Abbas of last year for this year. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it thus. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, mentioned it, mentioned the narration of Hujayyah ibn Adi, and that it is an error. He said: Correct is what Mansur narrated from al-Hakam, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim ibn Yannaq, mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"389","Hujayyah ibn Adi al-Kindi, also said al-Asadi, al-Kufi from Ali, upon him be peace - 411 - The judge Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii informed us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from al-Hakam, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, from Ali, that al-Abbas asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about advancing his charity before its time, and he permitted him. Ahmad and Abu Dawud narrated it from Said ibn Mansur. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli, both from Said ibn Mansur. Abu Dawud said: Hushaym narrated it from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Hakam, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Hushaym's hadith is more correct."
"390","Another - 412 - Abu Muslim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, he said: A man came to Ali, saying: I bought a cow. He said: Slaughter it for seven. He said: With broken horn? He said: It does not harm you. He said: Lame? He said: When it reaches the place of slaughter, slaughter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to inspect the eye and ear. Ibn Mahdi narrated it from Sufyan."
"391","413 - Abu al-Majd al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Ubayd Allah, that is al-Qawariri, narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, he said: I asked Ali about the cow. He said: For seven. He said: The one with broken horn? He said: No harm in it. He said: The lame? He said: When it reaches the place of slaughter. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to inspect the eye and ear. Shubah and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Salamah ibn Kuhayl. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Hujayyah's lineage is unknown. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shubah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ali ibn Hujr, from Sharik, from Salamah, saying: A hasan sahih hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from Khalid, from Shubah, from Salamah."
"392","Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib from his father, may Allah be pleased with them - 414 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Yala ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, that he fell ill and Amr ibn Hurayth visited him, and Ali visited him, saying: O Amr, you visit al-Hasan while in the soul is what is therein? He loved Uthman ibn Affan. He said: O Ali, you are not the lord of my heart to turn me as you wish. He said: That does not prevent me from giving you counsel. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no Muslim servant who visits a sick person but seventy thousand angels pray for him from the hour he visits him; if in daytime, until the sun sets; if at night, until the sun rises. Amr ibn Hurayth narrated the like of it from Ali, and it shall come, Allah willing, in his biography."
"393","Al-Hasan ibn Yasar al-Basri from Ali, upon him be peace, also said: He did not hear from him, Allah knows best - 415 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed me, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ali, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The pen is lifted from three: from the child until he understands, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the insane until it is removed from him. Or he said: he recovers. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai, from Busr ibn Umar, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, saying: A hasan gharib hadith from this aspect; we do not know of al-Hasan hearing from Ali. Al-Nasai narrated it from Abu Dawud al-Harrani, from Affan, from Hammam; and from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Ali as his قول, saying: The hadith of Yunus is more deserving of correctness. Our narration is from Yunus, raised as marfu. It is said Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated it from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan raised as marfu."
"394","Husayn ibn Ali from his father, upon them be peace - 416 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali al-Azdi narrated to me, Ali ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali informed me, my brother Musa ibn Jafar narrated to me, from his father Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"395","417 - Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Dimashqi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bukhari informed them, by reading to him. 418 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Ghanaim Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Mahdi informed them, by reading to him. 419 - Said ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Attaf al-Hamdani informed us in Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi informed them, by reading to him, saying: Abu al-Tayyib Tahir ibn Abd Allah al-Tabari informed us, by reading to him: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn ... informed us. 420 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hamid ibn Usayyah al-Harbi informed us there that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khalaf Lulu informed us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us. 421 - Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli al-Mufti informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Khallaf al-Bahili al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us. Al-Bahili said: narrated to us; Ibn al-Mughirah said: Ali ibn Jafar informed us. Al-Bahili said: from; Ibn al-Mughirah said: Musa ibn Jafar narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Ali, upon him be peace, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hands of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: Whoever loves me and loves these two, their father and their mother, shall be with me in my rank on the Day of Resurrection. In al-Bahili's narration: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hands of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: Whoever loves them, their father and their mother, shall be with me in my rank on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from this Nasr, saying: A gharib hadith known from the hadith of Jafar only from this aspect."
"396","Another - 422 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us in Naysabur that his grandfather Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Khalaf al-Adib informed us, al-Hakim Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Jafar ibn Harun al-Nahwi informed us in Baghdad, Ishaq ibn Sadaqah ibn Subh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us. 423 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us. 424 - This Abu Jafar also informed us that Abu Adnan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Nizar informed them, by reading to him while present: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Ali informed us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrate from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The miser is one before whom I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me. The wording is one, except that in al-Hakim's narration: Indeed the miser. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yahya ibn Musa and Ziyad ibn Ayyub, from Abu Amir al-Aqadi, from Sulayman, saying: A hasan gharib hadith. Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated it from Umarah likewise. Others than Yahya ibn Musa narrated it from Abu Amir without mentioning Ali. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, mentioned the disagreement, saying: The قول of Sulayman ibn Bilal is more like correct. Allah knows best. I say: Thus al-Daraqutni brought it in the biography of al-Husayn ibn Ali, from his father and others, and that is not clear to me; for the narration of Abd Allah, from his father, from Ali, from his grandfather, is either Ali or al-Husayn."
"397","Another - 425 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ikrimah, he said: I stood with al-Husayn, and I kept hearing him say: Here I am, here I am, until he stoned the jamrah. I said: O Abu Abd Allah, what is this calling? He said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib call until he reached the jamrah, and he told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called until he reached it."
"398","426 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ikrimah, he said: I set out with Husayn ibn Ali from Muzdalifah, and I kept hearing him say: Here I am, here I am, until he reached the jamrah. I said: What is this calling, O Abu Abd Allah? He said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib call until he reached the jamrah, and he told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called until he reached it."
"399","427 - With the same chain Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ikrimah, he said: I set out with al-Husayn ibn Ali from Muzdalifah, mentioning it."
"400","Another - 428 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Jafar ibn Ibrahim of the offspring of Dhu al-Janahayn narrated to us, Ali ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Husayn, that he saw a man come to a gap near the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), enter it and supplicate, so he forbade him, saying: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from my father, from my grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Do not take my grave as a festival, nor your houses as graves; your greeting reaches me wherever you are."
"401","Another - 429 - My maternal uncle the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abu Hanifah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Misri informed us, the judge Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Razi narrated to us, by dictation: Abu al-Fadl Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Musab ibn Mansur ibn Zayd ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said, he said: Whoever reads Surat al-Kahf on Friday is protected for eight days from every trial that occurs; if the Dajjal emerges, he is protected from him."
"402","430 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Muaddib informed me in Isfahan that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Musab ibn Manzur ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani Abu Dhuayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reads Surat al-Kahf on Friday is protected for eight days from every trial that occurs; if the Dajjal emerges, he is protected from him. Abd Allah ibn Musab was mentioned by neither al-Bukhari nor Ibn Abi Hatim in their books."
"403","Another - 431 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi al-Isbahani informed us, in his letter to us, that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Duni informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Miqsami informed us, Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Shaybah narrated to me that Muhammad ibn Ali informed him, saying: My father Ali informed me that Husayn ibn Ali said: My father Ali called me for ablution water, so I brought it near him; he began washing his palms three times before inserting them into his ablution, then rinsed three times and sniffed three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand to the elbow three times, then the left likewise, then wiped his head once, then washed his right foot to the ankles three times, then the left three times. Then he stood up, saying: Hand me. So I handed him the vessel containing the remainder of his ablution, and he drank from the remainder of his ablution standing. I was amazed; when he saw me, he said: Do not be amazed, for I saw your father the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do the like of what you saw me do. He says for this ablution of his, drinking the remainder of his ablution standing. Al-Nasai narrated it thus. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, mentioning the disagreement, mentioning this طريق, from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, that he perfected its chain, joining and ضبط it, saying: Shaybah is Ibn Abi Rashid."
"404","Husayn ibn Qabisah al-Fazari from Ali, upon him be peace - 432 - Hibat Allah ibn Ali al-Busiri informed us in Egypt that Murshid ibn Yahya al-Madini informed them, by reading to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Naysaburi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hanun informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb al-Nasai informed us, Qutaybah ibn Said and Ali ibn Hujr informed us, the wording Qutaybah's: Ubaydah narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ali, upon him be peace, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see madhiy, wash your organ and perform your ablution for prayer; when you ejaculate water, then bathe. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Rahman and others, from Zaidah, from al-Rukayn."
"405","433 - Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Zahir ibn Tahir informed them, by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Sadi and Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, saying: Qabisah narrated to us, from Ali, he said: I was a man given to madhiy, so I would bathe in winter until my back cracked. He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or it was mentioned to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not do so; when you see madhiy, wash your organ and perform your ablution for prayer; when you spurt, in one narration: gush, then bathe. I say: The mention of madhiy was mentioned in the Sahih, but herein is the mention of bathing. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ubaydah ibn Humayd. Abu Dawud narrated it from Qutaybah. Al-Nasai likewise narrated it in his book. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Bishr ibn Muadh."
"406","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari from Ali, upon him be peace - 434 - Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi informed us at Zahir Dimashq that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kattani informed us, Tammam ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Razi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hubaysh al-Farghani informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Said al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Anazi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Harun ibn Ibrahim al-Ahwazi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Love your beloved moderately; perhaps he shall be hated to you one day. Hate whom you hate moderately; perhaps he shall be beloved to you one day."
"407","435 - With the same chain Tammam ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Jahwash Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jahwash al-Harbi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Khuraqi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Harun ibn Ibrahim al-Ahwazi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Ali, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, mentioning the like of it."
"408","436 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Abd al-Karim ibn Ali ibn Furajah informed them, by reading to him while present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Harun ibn Ibrahim al-Ahwazi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Love your beloved moderately; perhaps he shall be hated to you one day. Hate whom you hate moderately; perhaps he shall be beloved to you one day. I do not know Yahya ibn al-Fadl by criticism or approval. These three imams narrated from him: the judge Ahmad ibn Ali, the Imam Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah, and the Imam Abu Arubah. Abu Amir al-Aqadi is Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, brought from in the two Sahihs. Harun al-Ahwazi was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Main. Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Isa al-Tirmidhi said: Al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated it, a weak hadith with its chain, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); correct is from Ali stopped as mawquf. I do not think al-Tirmidhi came upon the طريق of al-Aqadi, for al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar is no proof. Allah knows best what is correct. Ibrahim al-Nakhai narrated from Alqamah ibn Qays, from Ali, upon him be peace, the like of it from Ali's قول stopped as mawquf. Al-Daraqutni was asked about the hadith of Ubaydah, from Ali: Love your beloved moderately, the hadith, saying: Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrates it from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Rashdin, from Ubaydah, from Ali as his قول. Harun ibn Ibrahim al-Ahwazi opposed him, narrating it from Ibn Sirin, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ali raised as marfu. Abu Amir al-Aqadi said it from Harun. Zayd ibn al-Hubab said: from Harun, from Ibn Sirin, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, mursal. Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar opposed him, narrating it from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, without mentioning Ibn Sirin, from Ali, raising it. Allah knows best what is correct."
"409","Hanzalah ibn Nuaym from Ali, upon him be peace - 437 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Abu Mamar narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayd, from Hanzalah, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, secure my fright, cover my nakedness, guard my trust, and settle my debt."
"410","Khalid ibn Ararah from Ali, upon him be peace - 438 - It was read to Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi, while we listened: Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Ismail al-Qadi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn Ararah, he said: When Uthman was killed, I was seized with severe fright, and drawing the sword among us was grave, so I sat in my house. I had a need in the market for clothes I bought, so I went out, and there was a group sitting in shade, about forty men, with a chain hung displayed upon the door. I said: I shall enter and look. He said: I went to enter, and the doorman prevented me; they said: Leave the man. So I entered, and there were the nobles of people, with a cushion displayed, so I sat. A handsome man came wearing a suit without shirt or turban, and he was Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Then he sat, recognizing none of the people but me, saying: Ask me, and ask me only about what benefits and harms. A man said: Since you spoke until you loved to speak, I ask you. He said: Ask, and ask only about what benefits or harms. He said: What are: By those scattering broadcast, by those bearing weight, by those running ease, by those distributing command? The angels. Then he said: Tell me about what I ask you. He said: Ask, and ask only about what benefits or harms. He said: What is: By the raised roof? He said: The heaven. He said: What is: By the storming winds? He said: The winds. He said: What is: The retreating stars? He said: The planets. He said: What is: By the frequented House? Ali said to his companions: What do you say? They said: We say: It is the Sacred House. He said: Rather it is a house in heaven called al-Surah, opposite this House; its sanctity in heaven is as this one's sanctity on earth. Seventy thousand angels enter it daily, then never return to it. Then he recited this verse: The first House established for mankind is that at Bakkah, blessed and guidance for worlds; therein are clear signs, the station of Ibrahim; whoever enters it is safe. Then he said: Yet it is not the first house that was; Nuh was before it, among houses; Ibrahim was before it and among houses; but it is the first house established for people with blessing therein. Therein are clear signs, the station of Ibrahim; whoever enters it is safe. Then he narrated that Ibrahim, upon him be peace, when commanded to build the House, was constrained and did not know how to build it, so Allah sent al-Sakinah, a swift wind with a head, which encircled for him the Hajj; he would build upon it a course daily. Makkah is intensely hot. When he reached the Stone, he said to Ismail: Go seek for me a stone to place. He went roaming the mountains, and Jibril came with the Stone and placed it. Ismail came, saying: From where is this? He said: Brought by one who did not rely upon my building and yours, so he placed it. It remained as Allah willed, then collapsed; the Amalekites built it, then collapsed; Jurhum built it, then collapsed; Quraysh built it. When they wanted to place the Stone, they disputed its placing. They said: The first to emerge from this door shall place it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emerged from the door of Banu Shaybah; he ordered a garment spread, placed the Stone in the middle of the garment, and ordered from each thigh a man to take a side of the garment. They took it and lifted it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and placed it. A different man stood, saying: Tell me about this verse: If a woman fears from her husband ill-conduct or aversion, there is no sin upon them, until he completed the verse. He said: Ask about the like of this; this is knowledge. It is a man with two wives, one aged and unattractive, whom he reconciles to visit every day, three, or four. Another man stood to him asking about this verse: They ask you about women; say: Allah gives you verdict about them. Prayer was established and he stood. Qutaybah narrated from Abu Awanah, from Simak, from Khalid ibn Ararah, he said: I heard Ali, a man asking him about: By those scattering, by those bearing weight, by those distributing."
"411","439 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr, that is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Khalid ibn Ararah, from Ali, he said: When they wanted to place the Black Stone, meaning Quraysh, they disputed over it, saying: We appoint as judge between us the first man to emerge from this door. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the first to emerge upon them, so he judged between them that it be in a cloak lifted by all tribes together, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day was a young man."
"412","Ribi ibn Hirash al-Ghatafani from Ali, upon him be peace - 440 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Abi al-Fath informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him while present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No servant believes until he believes in four: testimony that there is no god but Allah, that I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with truth, until he believes in resurrection after death, and until he believes in all decree. Zaidah narrated it from Mansur."
"413","441 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Ubayd Allah, that is al-Qawariri, informed us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No servant believes until he believes in four: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with truth, he believes in resurrection after death, and believes in decree. Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Mansur."
"414","442 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Baqqal informed us that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed me, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None believes until he believes in four: he testifies there is no god but Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with truth, until he believes in decree and believes in resurrection after death."
"415","443 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us, Abu Said al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan al-Amiri narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari Umar ibn Sad al-Fazari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he believes in four: he testifies there is no god but Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me with truth, and in resurrection after death, and in decree. Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated it from Mansur."
"416","444 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Hasan al-Qazzaz informed them, by reading: The Sharif Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad al-Muhtadi Billah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Muhammad al-Allaf narrated to us, by dictation: Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he believes in decree and in resurrection after death... Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shubah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud, from Shubah, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali; and from Mahmud, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Shubah, from Mansur, from Ribi, from a man, from Ali. He said: The hadith of Abu Dawud from Shubah is in my view more correct than the hadith of al-Nadr. I say: Abu al-Ahwas narrated it from Mansur, from Ribi, from a man of Banu Asad. Waki narrated it from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ribi, from a man, from Ali. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah, from Sharik, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Sharik, Warqa, Jarir and Amr ibn Qays narrated it from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali. Al-Thawri, Zaidah, Abu al-Ahwas and Sulayman al-Taymi opposed them, narrating it from Mansur, from a man of Banu Asad, from Ali, and it is correct. I say: The narration of Zaidah, the narration of Abu Nuaym and Abu Dawud al-Hafari from Sufyan already preceded without mentioning anyone between Ali and Ribi, contradicting al-Tirmidhi's and al-Daraqutni's قول. Ribi may have heard it from Ali and heard it from a man from him, narrating it once from Ali and once from a man from him. Allah knows best."
"417","Another - 445 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Aswad ibn Amir informed us, Sharik informed us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Ali, he said: People of Quraysh came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Muhammad, we are your neighbors and allies; some of our slaves came to you with no desire for religion nor desire for understanding; they only fled our lands and wealth, so return them to us. He said to Abu Bakr: What do you say? He said: They spoke truth; they are your neighbors. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed. Then he said: What do you say? He said: They spoke truth; they are your neighbors and allies. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed."
"418","446 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us on the west side of Baghdad that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Karkhi informed them, by reading to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Two slaves went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning on the day of Hudaybiyyah, before the treaty; their masters wrote to him, saying: O Muhammad, by Allah, they did not go out to you desiring your religion; they only went out fleeing slavery. People said: O Messenger of Allah, return them to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, saying: I do not see you desisting, O company of Quraysh, until Allah sends upon you one who strikes your necks for this. He refused to return them, saying: They are Allah's freedmen, mighty and majestic. Abu Dawud narrated it thus in his Sunan. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it similarly from Sufyan ibn Waki, from his father, from Sharik, saying: A hasan sahih gharib hadith."
"419","Rabiah ibn Najidh al-Asadi from Ali, upon him be peace - 447 - Abu Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn al-Khurayf informed us in Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us. 448 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us, by my reading to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabiah ibn Najidh, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered Banu Abd al-Muttalib, among them a group each of whom would eat a young camel and drink a faraq. He made for them a mudd of food; they ate until full. He said: The food remained as it was, as though untouched. Then he called for a small cup and they drank until quenched; the drink remained as though untouched or undrunk. He said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, I was sent to you specially and to people generally. You saw of this sign what you saw; which of you will pledge to me to be my brother and companion? None stood to him. He said: I stood to him, being the youngest of the people. He said: Sit. He said: Three times, each time I stood to him and he said to me: Sit, until the third time he struck his hand upon my hand. The wording is al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib's. In al-Jawhari's narration: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered, or: The Prophet of Allah called Banu Abd al-Muttalib; therein: he called for a large cup and they drank; therein: Sit, then he said three times, the rest like it. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Abu Sadiq is Muslim ibn Yazid al-Azdi, Kufan; also said: His name is Abd Allah ibn Najidh; also said: He is the brother of Rabiah ibn Najidh. Abu Hatim said: He is upright in hadith."
"420","Another - 449 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Haradi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us, al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, al-Fayd ibn al-Fadl al-Bajali narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabiah ibn Najidh, he said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The leaders are from Quraysh."
"421","450 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani informed us that Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Fayd ibn al-Fadl al-Bajali narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabiah ibn Najidh, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The leaders are from Quraysh; the righteous of them are commanders of their righteous, the wicked of them commanders of their wicked. Each has a right, so give each rightful one his right. Even if an Abyssinian mutilated slave is appointed over you, listen to him and obey, unless one of you is given choice between his Islam and striking his neck, then let him extend his neck, may his mother be bereaved of him, for he has neither world nor Hereafter after his Islam departs. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This matter shall remain in Quraysh as long as two remain among people."
"422","Abu Umar Zadhdhan al-Kindi, their freedman, from Ali, upon him be peace - 451 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji and Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Imran al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, this the wording of Muhammad ibn Aban: from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Zadhdhan, from Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leaves a hair's place of impurity untouched by water shall have such and such done to him of the Fire. Ali said: From then I treated my hair as you see."
"423","452 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them: Al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Zadhdhan, that Ali ibn Abi Talib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leaves a hair's place of his body of impurity untouched by water shall have such and such done to him of the Fire. Ali said: From then I treated my head."
"424","453 - Abd Allah ibn Dhuhayl ibn Ali ibn Karih al-Harbi informed us there that Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Banna informed them: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar al-Hafiz informed us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us, Ali ibn Sahl ibn al-Mughirah and Isa ibn Jafar narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah and Shubah narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Zadhdhan, that Ali said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever leaves a hair's place of his body untouched by water shall have such and such done to him of the Fire. Ali said: From then I treated my head. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Ismail. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from al-Aswad, both from Hammad ibn Salamah similarly. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, mentioning the disagreement, saying: The preserved is from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"425","Another - 454 - The judge Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Umari informed us in Baghdad that the Hafiz Ismail ibn Ahmad al-Samarqandi informed them, by reading to him: Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Shihab al-Nafari informed us, Muhammad, that is Ibn Nuh ibn Abd Allah al-Jundaysaburi, narrated to us, Harun, that is Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Uthman ibn Qays, from Zadhdhan, from Ali about His قول, mighty and majestic: Every soul is held for what it earned, except the companions of the right. He said: They are the children of believers."
"426","Zirr ibn Hubaysh al-Asadi Abu Maryam from Ali, upon him be peace - 455 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Rabiah al-Kinani narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, that he heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, asked about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he washed his hands three times, his face three times, his forearms, wiped over his head until water dripped, and washed his feet three by three, then said: Thus was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Rabiah ibn Ubayd, said Abu Hatim al-Razi. Al-Bukhari said: Ibn Utbah. Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy. Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu Nuaym, from Rabiah ibn Utbah; thus in Abu Dawud's narration."
"427","Another - 456 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed me, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple."
"428","457 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hashim and Hasan narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Ibn Jurmuz sought permission upon Ali. He said: Who is this? They said: Ibn Jurmuz seeks permission. He said: Permit him; the killer of al-Zubayr shall enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr. Imam Ahmad also brought it from Affan, from Hammad, from Asim; and from Muawiyah ibn Amr. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani, saying: A hasan hadith. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement therein, saying: The preserved is the hadith of Zirr, meaning this. This hadith has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"429","Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad from Ali, upon him be peace - 458 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, by my reading to him in Baghdad, I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, al-Rabi, meaning Ibn Abi Salih al-Aslami, narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib adjure people, saying: I adjure by Allah a Muslim man who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Ghadir Khumm what he said? And twelve Badris stood and testified. This Ziyad is not al-Jassas, the criticized; for al-Jassas did not meet Ali. Some scholars said: Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad are seven, none criticized but al-Jassas. The like of this hadith shall come in the biography of Zayd ibn Yuthay and others."
"430","Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani from Ali, upon him be peace - 459 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, Sharik informed us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zura, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: People of Basrah of the Khawarij came upon Ali, among them a man called al-Jad ibn Baja. He said to him: Fear Allah, O Ali, for you shall die. Ali said: Rather killed; a strike upon this dyeing this, meaning his beard from his head; a covenanted covenant, a decreed decree; he who invents has failed. He reproached him about his clothing, saying: What have you to do with my clothing? It is farther from arrogance, more fitting for a Muslim to follow me."
"431","460 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us of it: his father informed them, by reading to him: Abd Allah al-Sarifini informed us, Abd Allah ibn Hababah informed us, Abd Allah al-Baghawi informed us, Ali, that is Ibn al-Jad, narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zura, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: A delegation of the people of Basrah came upon Ali, among them a man of the chiefs of the Khawarij called al-Jad ibn Baja. He preached to people, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O Ali, fear Allah, for you shall die; you know the path of the doer of good and the doer of evil. Then he admonished him and reproached him about his clothing. He said: What have you to do with my clothing? My clothing is farther from arrogance, more fitting for a Muslim to follow me."
"432","Zayd ibn Yuthay al-Hamdani, also said Ibn Uthay, from Ali, upon him be peace - 461 - Al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in Isfahan that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Zayd ibn Uthay, he said: We asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: With what were you sent in the Hajj? He said: I was sent with four: No naked one shall circumambulate the House; whoever had a covenant between him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it stands to its term; whoever has no covenant, his term is four months; none shall enter Paradise but a believing soul; Muslims and polytheists shall not gather after their year. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq."
"433","462 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, by reading to him: Ibrahim Sibtt Bahrawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Uthay: We asked Ali: With what were you sent? He said: I was sent with four: No naked one shall circumambulate the House; no polytheist shall enter the Sanctuary; whoever had a covenant between him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it stands to its term; whoever has no covenant, his term is four months; none shall enter Paradise but a believing soul. Zuhayr said: Thus Sufyan said: Zayd ibn Uthay, but he is Zayd ibn Yuthay. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Umar, Ali ibn Khashram and Nasr ibn Ali, all three from Ibn Uyaynah, saying: A hasan sahih hadith."
"434","Another - 463 - Al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them, by reading to him: Al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah informed us, my father narrated to me, Aswad Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, meaning al-Farra, narrated to me, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, from Ali, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall we appoint after you? He said: If you appoint Abu Bakr, you shall find him trustworthy, ascetic in the world, desirous of the Hereafter. If you appoint Umar, you shall find him strong, trustworthy, fearing no blamer's blame in Allah. If you appoint Ali, and I do not see you doing so, you shall find him guiding, guided, taking you by the straight path. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it, mentioning the disagreement, saying: Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, mursal, mentioning neither Ali nor Hudhayfah. The mursal is more like correct; he had mentioned it from Sulayman and from Hudhayfah."
"435","Another - 464 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, by reading to him while present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Khalid, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Yuthay, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said upon the pulpit: I adjure by Allah a man, and I adjure none but the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Ghadir Khumm. And six stood from this side and six from this side, saying: We bear witness that we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomsoever I am master of, Ali is his master. Said ibn Wahb narrated it. It shall come hereafter."
"436","Sa'ib ibn Malik - and it is said: ibn Yazid - al-Thaqafi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 465 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Ali: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will not give you two and leave the people of al-Suffah with their stomachs folded from hunger. And he said once: I will not give you two servants, while I leave the people of al-Suffah with their stomachs folded."
"437","466 - And with it (the same chain) my father narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Za'idah told us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared Fatimah with a khamil (a woolen cover), a waterskin, and a leather pillow whose stuffing was idhkhir fibre."
"438","467 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi told us, Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Ali: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Fatimah to him, he sent with her a khamilah, a pillow of leather stuffed with fibre, two jars, two millstones and a waterskin. Ali said to Fatimah: By Allah, I have drawn water until my chest ached, and Allah has brought your father captives, so go to him and ask him for a servant. She said: And I, by Allah, have ground until my hands were blistered. So she went to him, but she felt shy to mention that to him, and he said: What has brought you? She said: I came to greet you, O Messenger of Allah. So she returned, and Ali said to her: What did you do? She said: I felt shy to mention anything to him. So they both came to him together and mentioned that. He said: Allah has brought you captives and plenty, so give us servants. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will not give you two servants while I leave the people of al-Suffah folding with hunger, and I find nothing to spend on them; rather I will sell them (the captives) and spend on them. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"439","468 - And Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Umari informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ahmad al-Samarqandi informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal told us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi told us, Muhammad ibn Nuh al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Harun - he is ibn Ishaq - narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father: he said: Ali came to Fatimah - may Allah be pleased with her - and said to her: I complain of my chest from drawing with the water-bucket. She said: And I, by Allah, complain of my hand from grinding with the millstone. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith similarly. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah. And Ibn Majah narrated, from Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, his statement: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Fatimah to him, he sent with her a khamilah and a pillow of leather stuffed with fibre. And likewise al-Nasa'i narrated it also, from Nusayr ibn al-Faraj, from Abu Usamah, from Za'idah. And Ibn Hibban narrated that, from al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim al-Khallal, from Sa'id ibn Ayyub al-Sarifini, from Abu Usamah."
"440","Sa'd, father of al-Hasan, from Ali, peace be upon him: 469 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi told us, al-Qadi Isma'il narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah - and what is correct is Ubaydullah - narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from his father, from Ali: he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I performed ghusl from janabah, then prayed Fajr, then in the morning I saw on my forearm a spot the size of a fingernail that water had not touched. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you had wiped over it with your hand it would have sufficed you. Ibn Majah narrated it, from Suwayd ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah."
"441","Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sufyan, or Amr, from Ali, peace be upon him: 470 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Shadhan told us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab told us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from his father: he said: Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made no covenant to us about leadership in anything; rather it was an opinion we formed. So Abu Bakr was appointed caliph, and he stood upright and acted uprightly. Then Umar was appointed caliph, and he stood upright and acted uprightly. Then religion struck with its grants (became firmly established), and Allah pardons whom He wills and punishes whom He wills."
"442","471 - Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ghassani informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hadid told us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sulami told us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Khara'iti told us, it being read to him: Umar - he is ibn Shabbah - narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Sa'id ibn Amr, from his father: he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made no covenant to us about leadership in anything; rather it was an opinion we formed. So Abu Bakr was appointed caliph, and he stood upright and acted uprightly. And Umar was appointed caliph, and he stood upright and acted uprightly. Then religion struck with its grants, and there are people who sought the world; whomever Allah wills of them to punish, He punishes, and whomever He wills to have mercy on, He has mercy on."
"443","472 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Amr ibn Sufyan: he said: A man addressed on the day of Basra when Ali prevailed, and Ali said: This is the eloquent (shahshah) preacher. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went first, and Abu Bakr prayed (second), and Umar was third. Then a trial struck us after them; Allah does in it what He wills. It was said: al-shahshah means the one penetrating in a matter. Ibn Abi Hatim al-Razi said: Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sufyan narrated from his father Amr ibn Sufyan. Al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated from him in a hadith in which Abu Asim al-Nabil was alone in inserting Sa'id into the chain in what he narrated from al-Thawri, from al-Aswad, and he is not followed in it."
"444","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib ibn Hazn, al-Makhzumi, Abu Muhammad, from Ali, peace be upon him: 473 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi al-Darir informed us in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali: that he prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came, then saw in the house a curtain in which there were images, so he returned. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what made you return, may my father and mother be ransom for you? He said: In the house there is a curtain in which there are images, and the angels do not enter a house in which there are images."
"445","474 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad, may Allah have mercy on him, that Abu Shuja' Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi told us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Ali ibn Abi Talib prepared food and invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he accepted. When he entered the house he saw a picture, so he returned. Ali said to him: What is the matter with you, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture. Ibn Majah narrated it, from Abu Kurayb. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Mas'ud ibn Juwayriyah, from Waki'. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Waki' transmitted it with a connected chain, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali. And the companions of Hisham differed from him, narrating it from Hisham as mursal, and the mursal is more correct."
"446","Another (narration): 475 - Abu Abdillah Mahmud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ullayyah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden through suckling what He has forbidden through lineage. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it, from Ahmad ibn Mani'. And he said: a sound hadith. And Muslim narrated in his Sahih that when Ali said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the daughter of Hamzah: she is not lawful for me, she is the daughter of my brother through suckling. And al-Daraqutni authenticated the narration we mentioned from the narration of Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an."
"447","Another (narration): 476 - Imam Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: he said: Ma'mar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: he said: Ali sought from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is sought from a dead person, but did not find it, so he said: May my father be ransom for you, you were pure alive and you are pure dead. Al-Daraqutni said when asked about it: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad and Safwan ibn Isa said, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id: Ali said. And Ibn al-Mubarak and Abd al-Razzaq transmitted it as mursal, from Ma'mar. And likewise said Salih ibn Kaysan and al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri. And the mursal is more authentic."
"448","Another (narration): 477 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri told us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna told us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Safwan ibn Isa al-Zuhri narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Performing ablution fully in disliked (hard) circumstances, walking with the feet to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer wash away sins thoroughly. And Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad and Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated it, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu al-Abbas, from Sa'id."
"449","478 - Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar al-Bistami informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad al-Khalili told us, Ali al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham al-Shashi told us, Ibn al-Munadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Abu al-Abbas, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Performing ablution fully in disliked (hard) circumstances, walking with the feet, and waiting for prayer after prayer wash away sins thoroughly. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad, from Safwan ibn Isa. And Abu al-Abbas - his name is not known. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"450","Sa'id ibn Wahb al-Hamdani, from Ali, peace be upon him: 479 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq: he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Wahb say: Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - adjured the people, so five or six of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever I am his mawla (guardian/ally), then Ali is his mawla."
"451","480 - And with it (the same chain) Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb and from Zayd ibn Yuthay' - both said: Ali adjured (the people) in al-Rahbah: whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Ghadir Khumm except that he stand. He said: So there stood from the side of Sa'id six, and from the side of Zayd six, and they testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to Ali on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Is not Allah more worthy of the believers? They said: Yes indeed. He said: O Allah, whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"452","481 - Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Salafi informed us, by ijazah - he said: Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Harith al-Mu'allim told us, from what I read to him from the basis of his hearing: Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to you, by dictation: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hassan ibn al-Qasim al-Judayli narrated to us in Baghdad: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Sulayman al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Wahb: he said: Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - said: I adjure by Allah whoever heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Ghadir Khumm: Allah is my Wali, and I am the wali of the believers; whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, oppose whoever opposes him, and help whoever helps him. He said: Sa'id said: So there stood beside me six. He said: And Zayd ibn Yuthay' said: There stood from my side six. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Al-A'mash narrated it, and Shu'bah and Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, from Ali, and he mentioned what is in it of disagreement. He said: And the closest to what is correct is the saying of al-A'mash, Shu'bah, Isra'il and whoever followed them. And the like of this was narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, peace be upon him."
"453","Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali, peace be upon him: 482 - Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Akhdar informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi and Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them, it being read to them both - both said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Naqur told us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah told us, Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali - peace be upon him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are its possessor of two horns (dhu qarnayha); so do not follow one glance with another glance, for the first is for you and the last is not for you."
"454","483 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, it being read to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah told us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani told us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah al-Taymi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Salamah ibn Abi al-Tufayl, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are its possessor of two horns; so do not follow one glance with another glance, for the first is for you and the last is not for you. Al-Tabarani said: Hammad ibn Salamah was alone in it. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Affan, from Hammad. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it, from Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa, from Hudbah. And al-Tabarani narrated it, from Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Hajjaj ibn Minhal, from Hammad similarly. And from Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar, from Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn A'ishah."
"455","Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami al-Shami, Abu al-Salt, from Ali, peace be upon him: 484 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad told us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Shurayh - meaning ibn Ubayd - narrated to me: he said: The people of Sham were mentioned before Ali ibn Abi Talib while he was in Iraq, and they said: Curse them, O Commander of the Believers. He said: No; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Abdal (substitutes) will be in Sham, and they are forty men; whenever a man dies, Allah replaces in his place a man. By them rain is given, by them victory is granted against the enemies, and by them punishment is averted from the people of Sham. Abu al-Mughirah is Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj al-Khawlani, a shaykh of al-Bukhari. And Safwan is ibn Amr ibn Harim al-Saksaki, from the men of the Sahih. And Safwan ibn Abdillah ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf al-Jumahi narrated this hadith from Ali - peace be upon him - as mawquf upon him."
"456","485 - Shaykh Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us of it, with my reading to him in Naysabur - I said to him: Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari told us, Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Hamdun told us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi told us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-San'ani narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdillah ibn Safwan: he said: A man stood on the day of Siffin and said: O Allah, curse the people of Sham. So Ali said: Mah (hush); do not revile the people of Sham in a great multitude, for among them are the Abdal. Shurayh ibn Ubayd is Shami; he heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and others of the people of Sham, and I am not certain whether he heard from Ali - peace be upon him - or not. And Safwan ibn Abdillah ibn Safwan heard Ali and others, so the mawquf seems more worthy. And Allah knows best. And Salih ibn Kaysan followed Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri."
"457","486 - Abu al-Hasan al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muqri al-Tusi informed us, it being read to him while we listened, in Naysabur, that Abu al-Futuh Abd al-Wahhab ibn Shah ibn Ahmad al-Shadhyakhi informed them, it being read to him: Shaykh Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mukram told us, al-Sayyid Abu al-Husayn ibn Dawud told us, Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi told us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, Safwan ibn Abdillah ibn Safwan narrated to me that Ali stood at Siffin while the people of Iraq were reviling the people of Sham. So he said: O people of Iraq, do not revile the people of Sham in a great multitude, for among them are men averse to what you see, and in Sham there will be the Abdal."
"458","Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man al-Hamdani al-Sa'idi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 487 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed you, it being read to him: Abu Ali al-Mudhhib told us, Ahmad al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man - Abu Ishaq said: and he was a truthful man - from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear, and not to sacrifice a one-eyed animal, nor a muqabalah, nor a mudabarah, nor a sharqa, nor a kharqa. Zuhayr said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did he mention an adbاء (mutilated)? He said: No. He said: I said: What is muqabalah? He said: The front of the ear is cut. I said: What is mudabarah? He said: The back of the ear is cut. I said: What is sharqa? He said: The ear is slit. I said: What is kharqa? That the brand pierces its ear."
"459","488 - And with this chain my father narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man al-Hamdani, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to sacrifice a muqabalah, or a mudabarah, or a sharqa, or a kharqa, or a jad'a (mutilated). Shurayh - Abu Ishaq narrated from him. And his saying has preceded: and he was a truthful man. And Sa'id ibn Ashwa' narrated from him, and his son Sa'id ibn Shurayh. And Abu Hatim said: He is not used as proof; and so is the habit of Abu Hatim, saying about more than one of those from whom the authors of the Sahih narrated: he is not used as proof, without clarifying the criticism, so we do not accept except with clarification of the criticism. And Allah knows best. Abu Dawud narrated it, from al-Nufayli, from Zuhayr. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, and from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Ubaydullah ibn Musa, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq. And he said: a hasan sahih hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Adam, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah; and from Abu Dawud, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan, from Zuhayr, all from Abu Ishaq; and from Ahmad ibn Nasih, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; and from Harun ibn Abdillah, from Shuja' ibn al-Walid, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Abu Ishaq, similarly. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Isra'il, Zuhayr, Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, Sharik, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, Ali ibn Salih, Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah and others narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man, from Ali. He said: And Abu Ishaq did not hear this hadith from Shurayh. Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik narrated, from Qays ibn al-Rabi': he said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did you hear it from Shurayh? He said: Ibn Ashwa' narrated it to me from him. And al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Ashwa', from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man, from Ali, marfu'. And al-Thawri narrated it, from Ibn Ashwa', from Shurayh, from Ali, mawquf, and it resembles that the saying is the saying of al-Thawri. And Allah knows best."
"460","Shaqiq ibn Salamah Abu Wa'il al-Asadi al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 489 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il: he said: A man came to Ali and said: O Commander of the Believers, I am unable (to pay) my mukatabah (contract of manumission), so help me. He said: Shall I not teach you words the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me - if there were upon you like the mountain of Sir in dinars, Allah would pay it off for you? Say: O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your unlawful, and enrich me with Your bounty from whoever is besides You."
"461","490 - And Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us, it being read to him while we listened, in Naysabur - it was said to him: Your grandfather Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur informed you, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Khalaf told us: he said: Abdillah Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim ibn Ismah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Abu Wa'il: he said: A man came to Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - and said: Help me in my mukatabah. He said: Shall I not teach you words the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me - if there were upon you like the mountain of Sir in debt, Allah would pay it off for you? Say: O Allah, suffice me with Your lawful against Your unlawful, and enrich me with Your bounty from whoever is besides You. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yahya ibn Hassan, from Abu Mu'awiyah, and said: a hasan hadith. And this is the narration of al-Hakim in the book al-Mustadrak."
"462","Another (narration): 491 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna told us, Ubaydullah - meaning al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us: he said: Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah narrated to me: he said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salamah say: I saw Ali perform ablution three times three times. And he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution. Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit - Abu Zur'ah declared him trustworthy, and Yahya ibn Ma'in said: Salih al-hadith. And Abu Hatim said: There is no harm in him."
"463","492 - Sharif Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Sami' ibn Muhammad al-Abbasi informed us in Baghdad that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzar informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari told us, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah known as al-Askari told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah that he heard one who says - and he is Shaqiq ibn Salamah - say: I saw Ali and Uthman - may Allah have mercy on them both - perform ablution three times three times, and they both say: Thus is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad said: And Asim ibn Ali narrated it to us with its chain, similarly. Ibn Majah narrated it from Mahmud ibn Khalid, from al-Walid, from Ibn Thawban, and with him (it is): I saw Uthman and Ali performing ablution three times three times. Sa'sa'ah ibn Suhan ibn Sakhr al-Abdi, Abu Ikrimah, from Ali, peace be upon him."
"464","493 - Abu Muhammad Abdillah ibn Dahbal ibn Ali ibn Karih al-Harimi informed us, in al-Harim of Baghdad, that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ubaydillah ibn al-Banna informed them, it being read to him: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Jawhari told us, Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Musa Abu al-Husayn al-Hafiz told us, Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Mawdud narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Suhan, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among eloquence is magic, among poetry is wisdom, among seeking knowledge is ignorance, and among speech is (that which brings) dependents (burden). Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrates it, and there is disagreement from him: Shu'bah narrated, from Umarah, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from Sa'sa'ah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). That was said by Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani, from Yahya ibn al-Sakan, from Shu'bah. And Yahya ibn Abi Talib differed from him, narrating it from Yahya ibn al-Sakan, from Abu Juzayy, from Umarah, from Buraydah, from Sa'sa'ah, mursal. And likewise said Mas'ud ibn Juwayriyah, from Isma'il ibn Ziyad, from Abu Juzayy. And Hussam ibn Misakk narrated this hadith, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Sallam Abu al-Mundhir said: from Matar al-Warraq, from Ibn Buraydah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). That was said by Muhammad ibn Umar al-Qasabi from him; and Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Tammar differed from him, saying: from Sallam, from Matar, from Ibn Buraydah, from Ibn Abbas."
"465","Zalim ibn Amr ibn Sufyan, Abu al-Aswad, from Ali, peace be upon him: 494 - Imam Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi, Abu Abdillah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafis informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal told us, Abu Ahmad Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Abu Ya'qub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil told us, Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn Mani' ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dayli narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, and from Ibn Jurayj, and a man, from Zadham, thus both said: While the people were one day with Ali, they found from him a good mood. So they said: Narrate to us about your companions, O Commander of the Believers. He said: About which of my companions? They said: The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: All the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are my companions; which of them do you want? They said: The group whom we saw you honour with your mention and prayer upon them apart from the people. He said: Which of them? They said: Abdillah ibn Mas'ud. He said: He knew the Sunnah, and recited the Qur'an, and sufficient is it as knowledge. Then he concluded with it with him. They did not know what he meant by his saying: sufficient is it as knowledge - whether sufficient is Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, or sufficient is the Qur'an. They said: Then Hudhayfah. He said: He was taught - or knew - the names of the hypocrites, and asked about difficult matters when they were neglected; if you ask him about them you will find him knowledgeable of them. They said: Then Abu Dharr. He said: He retained knowledge, miserly, keen - miserly over his religion, keen upon knowledge - and he used to ask much, so he would be given and withheld; yet there has been filled for him in his vessel until it was full. They said: Then Salman. He said: That is a man from us and to us, Ahl al-Bayt; who has for you the like of Luqman the Wise? He knew the first knowledge, attained the last knowledge, recited the first Book and the last Book, and was a sea that does not dry. They said: Then Ammar ibn Yasir. He said: That is a man whose flesh, blood, bone, hair and skin Allah mixed with faith; he does not part from the truth for an hour; wherever it turns, he turns with it. The Fire should not eat anything of him. They said: Then narrate to us about yourself, O Commander of the Believers. He said: Gently; Allah forbade self-praise. He said: A speaker said: But Allah - Mighty and Majestic - says: And as for the favour of your Lord, proclaim it. He said: So I proclaim the favour of my Lord much: when I ask I am given, and when I am silent I am initiated (given unasked); between my flanks is abundant knowledge. So Abdillah ibn al-Kawwa al-A'war of Banu Bakr ibn Wa'il stood and said: O Commander of the Believers, what is: By the scattering winds? He said: The winds. He said: Then what is: And the load-bearers? He said: The clouds. He said: Then what is: And the smooth runners? He said: The ships. He said: Then what is: And the distributors of command? He said: The angels. And do not return to the like of this, nor ask me about the like of this. He said: Then what is: By the sky full of paths? He said: The abode of good character. He said: Then what is the darkness that is at the edge of the moon? He said: A blind man asks about a blind thing; you did not want knowledge by this. Woe to you, ask to understand, and do not ask obstinately - or he said: foolishly. Ask about what concerns you, and leave what does not concern you. He said: By Allah, this does concern me. He said: Allah says: And We made the night and the day two signs, then We effaced the sign of the night - the darkness that is at the edge of the moon. He said: Then what is al-Majarrah (the Milky Way)? He said: The seam of the sky, and from it the gates of the sky were opened with pouring water at the time of the flood upon the people of Nuh. He said: Then what is the bow of Quzah? He said: Do not say the bow of Quzah, for Quzah is Satan; rather it is the bow, and it is a security against drowning. He said: Then how much is between the sky and the earth? He said: The measure of the supplication of a servant who supplicates Allah; I say nothing other than that. He said: Then how much is between the east and the west? He said: A day's journey of the sun; whoever narrates to you other than that has lied. He said: Then who are those about whom Allah the Exalted says: And lodged their people in the abode of ruin? He said: Leave them, for you have been spared them. He said: Then what is Dhu al-Qarnayn? He said: A man Allah sent to a disbelieving people of the Book; their earliest were upon truth, then they associated with their Lord, innovated in their religion, and brought upon themselves; so today they strive in falsehood thinking they are upon truth, and strive in misguidance thinking they are upon guidance. Their effort went astray in the life of this world while they think they do well. He said: He raised his voice and said: And the people of al-Nahrawan tomorrow are not far from them. He said: So Ibn al-Kawwa said: By Allah, I will not ask other than you, nor follow other than you. He said: So he said: If the matter is to you, then do."
"466","Another (narration): 495 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Ubaydullah - meaning al-Qawariri - narrated to us (Ha). 496 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, it being read to him: Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudi told us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah told us, my grandfather told us, Bundar narrated to us - both said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us: he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the urine of the infant: The urine of the boy is sprinkled, and the urine of the girl is washed. The wording is the hadith of Ibn Khuzaymah. And in the narration of al-Qawariri: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the infant: it is sprinkled. Qatadah said: This is when he has not eaten food; if he has eaten food, both are washed."
"467","497 - And Abdillah ibn Abi al-Majd informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar - they said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The urine of the infant boy is sprinkled, and the urine of the girl is washed. Qatadah said: And this is while they have not eaten; if they have eaten, both are washed. Hisham raised it (as marfu'), from Qatadah, and Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah stopped it (as mawquf). Abu Dawud narrated it, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Mu'adh, and from Musaddad, from Yahya, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, and Musaddad did not raise it. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Bundar, and said: a hasan hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Hawtharah ibn Muhammad al-Minqari and Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, both from Mu'adh. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it, from Ibn Khuzaymah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah raised it, from the narration of his son Mu'adh, and Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith, from Hisham; and others besides them stopped it from Hisham. And likewise Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah and Hammam narrated it from Qatadah as mawquf. And Allah knows best."
"468","Another (narration): 498 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Ishaq - he is ibn Abi Isra'il - narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dayli, from his father, from Ali: he said: Abdillah ibn Salam came to me while I had put my foot in the stirrup. He said: Do not go to Iraq, for I fear the edge of the sword will strike you there. Ali said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had informed me of it. Abu al-Aswad said: I never saw like today a warrior informing of that about himself."
"469","499 - And Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i told us, Ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dayli, he heard him narrate from his father: he said: I heard Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - say: Abdillah ibn Salam came to me while I had put my leg in the stirrup. He said: Where do you want? I said: Iraq. He said: If you come to it, the edge of the sword will strike you there. Then he said: By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it. Abu Harb said: So I heard my father say: I marvelled at him, saying: A warrior narrates the like of this about himself. Ibn Hibban narrated it, from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, from Ibrahim ibn Bashshar, from Sufyan."
"470","Abbad ibn Abdillah, from Ali, peace be upon him: 500 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Abbad ibn Abdillah al-Asadi, from Ali: he said: When this verse was revealed: And warn your closest kin, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered of his household, so thirty gathered, and they ate and drank. He said: So he said to them: Who will guarantee my debt and my promises on my behalf, and be with me in Paradise, and be my successor among my family? A man - whom Sharik did not name - said: O Messenger of Allah, you were a sea; who can undertake this? He said: Then the other said. He said: So he presented that to his household, and Ali said: I. Al-Bukhari said in his Tarikh: Abbad ibn Abdillah al-Asadi heard Ali, and there is consideration (doubt) about him."
"471","Another (narration): 501 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal, from Abbad ibn Abdillah, or Abdillah ibn Abbad, from Ali: that he ascended the pulpit on Friday and addressed, then al-Ash'ath stood to him and said: al-Humayra (A'ishah) has prevailed over you against us. So he said: Who will excuse me from these bulky ones? One of them stays behind tossing on his stuffed mattresses, while these come early to the remembrance of Allah. If I drive them away, then I am of the wrongdoers. But by Allah, I heard him saying: They will surely strike you back upon religion as you struck them upon it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrates it, from al-A'mash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad ibn Abdillah al-Asadi, from Ali, mawquf. And Abu Awanah and Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli raised it, from al-A'mash. And Sharik narrated it from al-A'mash leaning toward raising it, without stating it explicitly; and its raising is correct."
"472","Abbad ibn Abi Yazid - and it is said: ibn Yazid - al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 502 - Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghana'im al-Wa'iz informed us, with my reading to him in the outskirts of Cairo - I said to him: Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad told us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah told us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub told us, Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tirmidhi told us, Ubadah ibn Ya'qub al-Kufi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abbad ibn Abi Yazid, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Makkah, and we went out in one of its outskirts; no mountain nor tree faced him except that it said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. Thus al-Tirmidhi narrated it, and said: a gharib hadith. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Isma'il al-Suddi narrates it, and there is disagreement from him: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr and Anbasah ibn al-Azhar narrated it, from al-Suddi, from Abbad ibn Abi Yazid, from Ali. And Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated it, from al-Suddi, from Abu Yazid al-Khaywani, from Ali."
"473","Asim ibn Damrah al-Saluli al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 503 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali told us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us (Ha). 504 - And Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Ahmad ibn al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah told us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Witr (One) and loves the witr; so perform witr, O people of the Qur'an. Sufyan narrated it."
"474","505 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Abdillah al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri told us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna told us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali: he said: Witr is not obligatory like prayer; rather it is a sunnah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established. Ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Waki'."
"475","506 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, it being read to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Ahmad told us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad ibn Ayyub told us, Abu Ya'qub Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, from Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: Witr is not obligatory like the prescribed prayer; rather it is a sunnah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established."
"476","507 - And Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub told us, my grandfather Ishaq told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said to him: No; witr is not obligatory nor like your prescribed prayer; rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr."
"477","508 - And with it (the same chain) from Asim, from Ali: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people of the Qur'an, perform witr, for Allah is Witr and loves the witr."
"478","509 - And with it (the same chain) Ahmad ibn Mani' told us: he said: Abu Ahmad told us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali: he said: Witr is not obligatory; rather it is a sunnah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established. And Isra'il narrated it."
"479","510 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali informed us that his father informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Zuhayr told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: Witr is a sunnah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established, so perform witr, O people of the Qur'an. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Ibrahim ibn Musa, from Isa ibn Yunus, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Abu Ishaq. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Ishaq, more complete than the hadith of Zakariyya. And he said: a hasan hadith. And from Bundar, from Ibn Mahdi, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq with its meaning, and in it: (It is not obligatory, but it is a sunnah the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established). And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Ali ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, like the hadith of Bundar. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Abu Bakr, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim: (Perform witr, O people of the Qur'an). And from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Waki', and from Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Nu'aym, all from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim: (Witr is not obligatory) to its end. And Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and others, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, similarly."
"480","Another (narration): 511 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have remitted for you (the zakat of) horses and slaves; so pay the sadaqah of silver: from every forty dirhams a dirham. And there is nothing in ninety and a hundred; when it reaches two hundred, in it are five dirhams. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Surayj ibn al-Nu'man, from Abu Awanah. And Sulayman al-A'mash narrated it, from Abu Ishaq."
"481","512 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: I have remitted for you (the zakat of) horses and slaves, and there is no zakat in less than two hundred. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Amr ibn Awn. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib, both from Abu Awanah. And Abu Dawud said: Al-A'mash narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, as Abu Awanah said. And Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah and Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Tirmidhi said: I asked Muhammad about this hadith, and he said: Both are with me sahih from Abu Ishaq; it is possible he narrated from both. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Usamah, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim; and from Husayn ibn Mansur, from Ibn Numayr, from al-A'mash, adding: And there is no zakat in less than two hundred."
"482","Another (narration): 513 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kamil al-Jahdari Fudayl ibn Husayn narrated to us - by dictation from his book: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that he was asked about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the daytime. He said: He used to pray sixteen rak'ahs. He said: He would pray when the sun was here like its state here, like the Asr prayer - two rak'ahs; and he would pray when the sun was here like its state here like the Zuhr prayer - four rak'ahs; and he would pray before Zuhr four rak'ahs and after Zuhr two rak'ahs, and before Asr four rak'ahs."
"483","514 - And Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim: he said: We came to Ali and said: O Commander of the Believers, will you not narrate to us about the daytime voluntary prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Who of you can bear that? We said: We will take from it what we can. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Fajr, then wait until when the sun rose here and ascended, being from the east like its state from the west - meaning at Asr time - he stood and prayed two rak'ahs. Then he waited until when the sun rose here and ascended, being from the east like its state from the west - meaning at Zuhr time - he stood and prayed four, separating between every two rak'ahs with taslim upon the angels brought near, the prophets, and whoever followed them of the believers and Muslims. Then he waited; when the sun declined he stood and prayed four, then prayed after Zuhr two rak'ahs, and prayed before Asr four, separating between every two rak'ahs with taslim upon the angels brought near, the prophets, and whoever followed them of the believers and Muslims. So those are sixteen rak'ahs, and I have not seen anyone pray them after him. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Waki', from Sufyan, Isra'il and his father, from Abu Ishaq. And Abdillah ibn Ahmad said: Waki' narrated to us. He said: And my father said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit said - when he narrated it to him: Your hadith of yours equals the fill of your mosque in gold. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq similarly in full, and from Ibn Muthanna, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah similarly. And he said: a hasan hadith; and Ishaq said: The best thing narrated about the voluntary prayer of the Prophet is this. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi, from Waki', from Sufyan, his father and Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq similarly. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Shu'bah with its chain; and from Ibn al-Muthanna, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ishaq similarly; and the hadith of Shu'bah is more complete."
"484","515 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Shuja' Umar ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi told us, Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Awfi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me while I was uncovering my thigh. He said: O Ali, cover your thigh, for it is of the awrah. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Rawh ibn Ubadah, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Habib, from Asim; and from Rawh, from Ibn Jurayj, from Habib."
"485","516 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yazid Abu Khalid al-Baysari al-Qurashi narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not expose your thigh, nor look at the thigh of a living one nor a dead one. And Abu Dawud narrated it, from Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramli, from Hajjaj, from Ibn Jurayj: he said: I was told from Habib ibn Abi Thabit similarly, and said: This hadith contains nakarah (objectionability). And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Bishr ibn Adam ibn bint Azhar al-Samman, from Rawh ibn Ubadah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Habib."
"486","Another (narration): 517 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eight rak'ahs of voluntary prayer at night and twelve rak'ahs in the daytime."
"487","518 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym Abu Ma'mar al-Hilali narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eight rak'ahs in voluntary prayer, and in the daytime twelve rak'ahs. And in a copy: (twelf)."
"488","Another (narration): 519 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks for something out of sufficiency amasses thereby embers of Hell. They said: What is sufficiency? He said: Supper. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad, from Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith."
"489","Another (narration): 520 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Abu Sa'id Mansur ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani told us, Hafiz Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham told us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray that night, the night of Badr, saying: O Allah, if You destroy this band, You will not be worshipped. And rain befell them that night."
"490","Another (narration): 521 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, it being read to him: Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi told us, Abu Tahir - he is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah - told us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq told us, Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us (Ha). 522 - Abu Bakr said: And Muhammad ibn al-Ala ibn Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us. 523 - Abu Bakr said: And Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after every prescribed prayer two rak'ahs, except Fajr and Asr. This is the wording of the hadith of Waki'. Ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Waki'."
"491","524 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after every prescribed prayer two rak'ahs except Asr and Subh."
"492","525 - And Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Ahmad al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to me, Jarir and Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray a prayer after which prayer is performed except that he prayed after it two rak'ahs."
"493","526 - And with it (the same chain) Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray after every prescribed prayer two rak'ahs, except Fajr and Asr. And Abd al-Rahman said: (At the end of every prayer). Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad, from Abu Nu'aym, from Sufyan, like the narration of Ibn Mahdi. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Jarir. And Abu Dawud narrated it in full, from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Sufyan. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned that Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated it from al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali. And the companions of al-Thawri narrated it from him, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali; and the preserved is the hadith of Asim, from Ali."
"494","Another (narration): 527 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, with my reading to him - I said to him: Abu al-Fath Muflih ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Warraq informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Hafiz told us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Amr told us, Abu Dawud told us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli narrated to us, Zuhayr told us, Abu Ishaq told us, from Asim ibn Damrah and from al-Harith al-A'war, from Ali. Zuhayr said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Give a quarter of the tenths: from every forty dirhams a dirham. And there is nothing upon you until it completes two hundred dirhams; when it is two hundred dirhams, in it are five dirhams, and whatever increases is upon that calculation. And in sheep: in every forty sheep a sheep; if there are only thirty-nine, there is nothing upon you in them. And he drove the sadaqah of sheep like al-Zuhri. He said: And in cattle: in every thirty a tabi', and in forty a musinnah; and there is nothing upon working (animals). And in camels - and he mentioned its sadaqah as al-Zuhri mentioned. He said: And in twenty-five, five of sheep; when it increases by one, in it is a she-camel in its second year (bint makhad); if there is no bint makhad, then a male ibn labun, up to thirty-five; when it increases by one, in it is a bint labun up to forty-five; when it increases by one, in it is a hiqqah fit for the stallion, up to sixty. Then he drove like the hadith of al-Zuhri. He said: When it increases by one - meaning one and ninety - in it are two hiqqahs fit for the stallion, up to a hundred and twenty; if the camels are more than that, then in every fifty a hiqqah. And what is joined is not separated, nor what is separated joined, fearing sadaqah. And no decrepit, nor defective, nor billy-goat is taken in sadaqah, unless the collector wills. And in crops: what the rivers water or the sky waters, the tenth; and what is watered by bucket, in it is half the tenth. And in the hadith of Asim and al-Harith: Sadaqah is every year. Zuhayr said: I think he said once in the hadith of Asim: When there is in the camels neither bint makhad nor ibn labun, then ten dirhams or two sheep. He only said: as al-Zuhri mentioned, for before this hadith with him is the hadith of al-Zuhri which is in the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it the mention of the obligations of sadaqat. Al-Daraqutni was asked and mentioned the disagreement about it: that some of them raised it and some stopped it. He said: And what is correct is mawquf."
"495","528 - And with this chain, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us: he said: Ibn Wahb told us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed me - and he named another - from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah and al-Harith al-A'war, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with part of the beginning of the hadith. He said: When you have two hundred dirhams and a year passes over them, in them are five dirhams. And there is nothing upon you - meaning in gold - until you have twenty dinars; when he has twenty dinars and a year passes over them, in it is half a dinar, and whatever increases is upon that calculation. He said: I do not know whether Ali says: upon that calculation, or he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And there is no zakat in wealth until a year passes over it. Except that Jarir said: Ibn Wahb adds from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no zakat in wealth until a year passes over it. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it, and said: Shu'bah, Sufyan and others narrated it, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali, and they did not raise it."
"496","Another (narration): 529 - Umar informed us, Muflih told us, Ahmad told us, al-Qasim told us, Muhammad told us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray before Asr two rak'ahs. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it."
"497","Another (narration): 530 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr from the first of the night, its end and its middle; then his witr ended at sahar (pre-dawn)."
"498","531 - And with it (the same chain) Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr in the first of the night, its middle and its end; then witr became fixed for him at its end. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"499","532 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us (Ha). 533 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed witr at every part of the night - its first, middle and end - and his witr ended at the end of the night. And Abdillah ibn Ahmad said in his narration: Shu'bah narrated to me."
"500","534 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that his father Abu Mansur ibn Ali informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Zuhayr told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: he said: Witr is not obligatory of prayer; rather it is a sunnah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for Allah - Mighty and Majestic - is Witr and loves the witr. Abu Abdillah ibn Majah narrated it, from Bundar, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, and from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki', both from Shu'bah similarly. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it. He said: And the preserved is the saying of whoever said: Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali."
"501","Another (narration): 535 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdillah al-Adib informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: he said: My father informed me, al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey, every taloned bird, the price of carrion, the price of domestic donkeys, the earnings of the prostitute, and the stud fee of every stallion."
"502","536 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad informed us that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan told us, Ahmad told us, Abdillah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey, every taloned bird, the price of carrion, the flesh of domestic donkeys, the dowry of the prostitute, the stud fee of the stallion, and purple saddle cloths."
"503","Another (narration): 537 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Mu'adh - meaning al-San'ani - narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: Whoever wishes his life extended, his provision expanded, and an evil death averted from him, let him fear Allah and join his kin. Abdillah ibn Mu'adh - Abd al-Razzaq spoke about him, while Yahya ibn Ma'in and Abu Hatim al-Razi declared him trustworthy. And Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated it, from Ma'mar."
"504","538 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed us, in writing: that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Bayan informed them, it being read to him: Talhah ibn Ali ibn al-Saqr ibn al-Mujib told us, Ahmad - he is ibn Uthman ibn Yahya al-Adami - narrated to us, Abbas - he is al-Duri - narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr ibn Bariyy narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes his life extended, his provision expanded, and an evil death averted from him, let him fear Allah and join his kin."
"505","Another (narration): 539 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, it being read to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Ubaydullah - meaning al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Duha."
"506","540 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray of Duha."
"507","Another (narration): 541 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you, it being read to him while you were present: Ahmad ibn Abdillah told us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad told us, Muhammad ibn Asim told us, Abu Yahya - he is al-Himmani, his name Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah: he said: Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - recited this verse: And those who disbelieved will be driven to Hell in groups, then recited: In extended columns, and marvelled at the Fire as much as Allah willed him to marvel. Then he recited: And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups until when they come to it and its gates are opened - a tree will face them, in its trunk two springs; they will perform ablution and wash from one of them - Abu Yahya doubted - so their heads will not be dishevelled, their skins will not be pale, and upon them will run the radiance of bliss. Then they will drink from the other spring, leaving in their bellies no filth, harm or evil: Until when they come to it and its gates are opened and its keepers say to them: Peace be upon you, you were good, so enter it abiding. He said: And the youths will face them like hidden pearls and scattered pearls, calling them by their names, telling them of the honour Allah prepared for them, clinging to them as people cling to a beloved one who was absent and has come. So a boy will go to his wife and give her glad tidings; she will say: Did you see him? He will say: I saw him. She will say: Did you see him? He will say: I saw him - three times. Joy will make her light until she comes to the threshold of her door. Then he will come to a dwelling built for him upon boulders of pearl; he will see lined cushions and spread carpets, and above that a lofty structure green, yellow and red, of every colour. He will raise his head to that structure; were it not that Allah - Mighty and Majestic - made it his abode and dwelling, his sight would flash and be gone. So they will say then: Praise be to Allah who guided us to this, and we would not have been guided had Allah not guided us, and they will be called. Zuhayr narrated it, from Abu Ishaq."
"508","542 - And Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us of it in Baghdad that his father informed him, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi told us, Ali told us, Zuhayr told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim, from Ali: he said: He mentioned the Fire - magnifying its matter - a mention I do not remember. He said: And those who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups, until when they reach a gate of its gates they find by it a tree from beneath whose trunk two springs flow. They will go to one of them as though commanded, drink from it, removing what is in their bellies of filth, harm or ailment. Then they will go to the other and purify from it, and upon them will run the radiance of bliss; their hair will never be dusty after it, nor their heads dishevelled, as though oiled with oil. Then they will reach Paradise and say: Peace be upon you, you were good, so enter it abiding. Then the youths will meet them, circling them as the youths of this world circle a beloved one coming to them from absence, saying to him: Glad tidings of the honour Allah prepared. Then a boy of those youths will go to one of his wives of the houris and say: So-and-so has come, by the name he was called in this world. She will say: Did you see him? He will say: I saw him, and he is behind me. Joy will make one of them light until she stands at the threshold of her door. When he reaches his dwelling he will look at the foundation of its building - boulders of pearl, above it a lofty structure green, red and yellow, of every colour. Then he will raise his head and look at its roof - like lightning; were it not that Allah - Mighty and Majestic - decreed it, it would befall that his sight go. Then he will lower his head, and there are his wives: And cups set, and lined cushions, and spread carpets. Then they will recline and say: Praise be to Allah who guided us to this, and we would not have been guided - the verse. Then a caller will call: You shall live and never die, reside and never depart, be healthy - I think he said - and never fall ill. Abu Ishaq said: Thus he said. Al-Bukhari narrated in his Sahih many a tafsir of Abdillah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both. Hakim Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Bayyi' said - and he narrated in al-Mustadrak in the supplications a hadith in tafsir from Abu Hurayrah not ascribed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): They both agreed - meaning al-Bukhari and Muslim - that the tafsir of a Companion is a musnad hadith."
"509","Asim ibn Amr al-Madani, from Ali, peace be upon him: 543 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi and Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid both informed us in Isfahan that Ali ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri told us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah - and the wording is his - and Muhammad ibn Zayyan ibn Habib both said: Abu Musa Isa ibn Hammad Zughbah narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd told us, from Sa'id - he is al-Maqburi - from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Asim ibn Amr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: that he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we were at al-Harrah at al-Suqya which belonged to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me water for ablution. So he performed ablution, stood, faced the qiblah, said takbir, then said: O Allah, Ibrahim was Your servant and friend who supplicated for the people of Makkah for blessing; and I, Muhammad, Your servant and messenger, supplicate You for the people of Madinah to bless them in their mudd and sa', like what You blessed the people of Makkah, with blessing upon blessing."
"510","544 - And Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us in Baghdad that Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn al-Hasan al-Khallal told us, Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Nafari told us, Muhammad - he is ibn Nuh al-Jundaysaburi - narrated to us, Harun - he is ibn Ishaq - narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sharahbil al-Kindi narrated to us, Layth told us, from al-Maqburi, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Asim ibn Amr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were at al-Harrah at al-Suqya which belonged to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me water for ablution. So he performed ablution, stood, faced the qiblah, then said: O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and friend who supplicated for the people of Makkah for blessing; and I, Your servant, supplicate You for the people of Madinah to bless them in their mudd and sa' like what You blessed the people of Makkah, with blessing upon blessing. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Hajjaj, from Layth. And al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i both narrated it, from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Layth; in al-Tirmidhi's narration: Asim ibn Amr, and in al-Nasa'i's narration: Asim ibn Umar. Al-Tirmidhi said: a sahih hadith. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it, from Ibn Khuzaymah, from al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, from Ibn Wahb, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth, from his father. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it. He said: And the closest to what is correct is the saying of al-Layth and whoever followed him - meaning this narration. And Allah knows best."
"511","Amir ibn Sharahil al-Sha'bi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 545 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna told us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali: he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and Umar came. He said: These two are the masters of the elders of the people of Paradise among the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers."
"512","546 - And with it (the same chain) Ahmad ibn Ali told us, al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, from Waki', from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali: he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and Umar came. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two are the masters of the elders of the people of Paradise among the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers. O Ali, do not inform them. Al-Sha'bi narrated from Ali - peace be upon him - about flogging a woman then stoning her; al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih. And this hadith which we wrote here was narrated by Abdillah ibn Hashim al-Tusi, from Waki' ibn al-Jarrah, from Yunus, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali; so it is as though al-Sha'bi did not hear it from Ali. And Allah knows best."
"513","Another (narration): 547 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, with my reading to him in the western side of Baghdad - I said to him: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib told us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar told us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Abdillah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Jarir, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - that a Jewess used to insult the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and attack him, so a man strangled her until she died; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nullified her blood. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"514","Another (narration): 548 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Tabarzad al-Daraqazzi informed us there that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur informed them, it being read to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib told us, Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Ja'far told us, Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i told us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him: he said: Do not be extravagant in a shroud, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not be extravagant in a shroud, for it will be stripped quickly. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"515","Another (narration): 549 - Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed us, with my reading to her in Naysabur - I said to her: Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you, it being read to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Musa told us, Yahya ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Harb told us, Abu Muhammad Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi told us, Abdillah ibn Hashim ibn Hayyan al-Tusi told us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah - he is ibn Malih al-Ru'asi - narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Amir: he said: I saw Ali white-bearded, filling what is between his shoulders. He said: And Ali said: We did not deem it unlikely that tranquillity spoke on the tongue of Umar. And Sharik narrated it, from Isma'il."
"516","550 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that his father informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Sharik told us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir: he said: Ali said: We did not deem it unlikely that tranquillity spoke upon the tongue of Umar."
"517","Amir Abu Wathilah al-Laythi Abu al-Tufayl - and he is a Companion - from Ali, peace be upon him: 551 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in the western side of Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj and Abu Nu'aym both said: Fitr narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Abu al-Tufayl - Hajjaj said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there did not remain of this world except a day, Allah - Mighty and Majestic - would send a man from us who would fill it with justice as it was filled with injustice. Abu Nu'aym said: A man from me. He said: And I heard him once mention from Habib, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"518","552 - And Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: If there did not remain of time except a single day, Allah would send a man from my household who would fill it with justice as it was filled with wrong and injustice. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abu Nu'aym."
"519","Another (narration): 553 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Muhammad and Abu Nu'aym al-Ma'ni narrated to us, Fitr told us, from Abu al-Tufayl: he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - gathered the people in al-Rahbah, then said: I adjure by Allah every Muslim man who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Ghadir Khumm what he said. So some people stood to him. Abu Nu'aym said: Many people stood and testified when he took his hand and said to the people: Do you know that I am more worthy of the believers than themselves? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whomever I am his mawla, then this is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. He said: So I went out as though in myself something, and met Zayd ibn Arqam. I said to him: I heard Ali say such and such. He said: What do you deny? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that to him. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it, from Abdillah al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Nu'aym and Yahya ibn Adam, from Fitr ibn Khalifah similarly."
"520","Another (narration): 554 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Imam Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar al-Razi al-Muqri told us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas told us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Dayli told us, Abu Ubaydillah Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Husayn, from Abu al-Tufayl: he said: I heard Ibn al-Kawwa ask Ali, while he was on the pulpit, about the saying of Allah, Majestic: Have you not seen those who exchanged the favour of Allah for disbelief and lodged their people in the abode of ruin? He said: Leave them, for you have been spared them; that was the day of Badr. He said: And Ibn Abbas said: They are the disbelievers of Quraysh."
"521","555 - And with it (the same chain) from Abu al-Tufayl: he said: I heard Ibn al-Kawwa ask Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - about Dhu al-Qarnayn. So Ali said: He was neither a prophet nor an angel; he was a righteous servant who loved Allah so Allah loved him, and was sincere to Allah so Allah was sincere to him. He was sent to his people, they struck him on his horn (qarn) and he died, then Allah raised him, so he was called Dhu al-Qarnayn."
"522","556 - And with it (the same chain) from Ibn Abi Husayn: he said: I heard Abu Tufayl say: I heard Ibn al-Kawwa ask Ali ibn Abi Talib - may Allah be pleased with him - about: By the scattering winds. He said: They are the winds. And about: And the load-bearers. He said: The clouds. And about: And the smooth runners. He said: The ships. And about: And the distributors of command. He said: The angels."
"523","557 - And with it (the same chain) he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: I witnessed Ibn al-Kawwa ask Ali ibn Abi Talib about: By the frequented House. He said: It is in the seventh (heaven); seventy thousand angels enter it every day, never returning among them; and it is al-Durah (the much-visited). Ibn Abi Husayn: his name is Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn. Muslim narrated for him in the Sahih from the narration of Sufyan ibn Uyaynah from him, from Abu al-Tufayl."
"524","Those named Abdillah: Abdillah ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib from his uncle Ali ibn Abi Talib, peace be upon him: 558 - Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid informed us in Isfahan that his grandfather Ghanim ibn Khalid informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah told us, Isa ibn Hammad Zughbah narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd told us, from Muhammad ibn al-Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, from Abdillah ibn Ja'far, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me these words, and commanded me if distress or hardships descend upon me to say them: There is no god but Allah, the Noble, the Forbearing; and glory be to Him, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"525","559 - And Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi and Abu Abdillah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, from Abdillah ibn Ja'far, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me these words, and commanded me if distress descends upon me to say them: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Noble; glory be to Him, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Rawh ibn Ubadah."
"526","560 - Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us, it being read to him while we listened, in Damascus - it was said to him: Abu al-Majd Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Tha'labi informed you, it being read to him while you listened - he said: Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini told us: he said: Shaykh Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal told us, it being read to him - he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi told us, it being read to him - he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasa'i told us, Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd told us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: he said: Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, from Abdillah ibn Ja'far, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words to say at distress when it descends upon me; I did not teach them to Hasan nor Husayn - I have singled you out with them: when a matter distresses you, say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Noble; glory be to Him, blessed is Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"527","561 - And with it (the same chain) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i told us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far told us, Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abdillah ibn Hasan, from Abdillah ibn Ja'far: he said about these words: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Noble; glory be to Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; O Allah, have mercy on me; O Allah, overlook me; O Allah, pardon me. Abdillah ibn Ja'far said: My uncle informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him these words. Thus al-Nasa'i narrated it in the book of deeds of day and night. And he narrated it by paths, some raising it, some stopping it. And he narrated it in al-Bu'uth of his book and in deeds of day and night, from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Ajlan. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it, from Isma'il ibn Dawud ibn Wardan al-Bazzar, from Isa ibn Hammad. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ibn Ajlan, Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi and Aban ibn Salih narrated it and agreed on raising it; and Rib'i ibn Hirash differed from them, narrating it from Abdillah ibn Shaddad, from Abdillah ibn Ja'far, from Ali, mawquf. I say: Mis'ar raised it, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abdillah ibn Hasan, from Abdillah ibn Ja'far."
"528","Another (narration): 562 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed me, may Allah have mercy on him, that Abu Zur'ah Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed them, it being read to him, in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Muqawwimi told us, al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib told us, Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah ibn Bahr al-Qattan told us, Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us, Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Zayd ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abdillah ibn Ja'far, from his father, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I die, wash me with seven waterskins from my well, the well of Ghars. Thus Ibn Majah transmitted it."
"529","Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn Abd al-Muttalib, from Ali, peace be upon him: 563 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, it being read to him: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Fath told us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi ibn Mas'ud al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz told us, Abu Muhammad ibn Abi al-Shawk - he is al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Zayyat - narrated to us, Hilal ibn al-Ala Abu Umar narrated to us, my father narrated to me - dictating it to me alone from his memory: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Ali ibn Abi Talib - peace be upon him - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: Allah - Mighty and Majestic - says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it. And the fasting person has two joys: at breaking fast, and when he meets his Lord - Mighty and Majestic. And by Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Hilal ibn al-Ala with its chain. And he narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdillah, mawquf, and said: This is what is correct with us; the hadith of al-Ala is a mistake; and I have seen for al-Ala objectionable hadiths."
"530","Another (narration): 564 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Abu Ya'la told us, Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Ali: he said: The first to be clothed of creation is Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - two linen garments; and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will be clothed a Yemeni cloak, while he is at the right of the Throne. Mawquf. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Aban ibn Taghlib narrates it, from Imran ibn Maytham, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i narrated it, from al-Minhal, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Ali, mawquf; and it is what is correct."
"531","Another (narration): 565 - Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed him, al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, my father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim, freedman of Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from his master Abdillah ibn al-Harith: he said: I performed umrah with Ali ibn Abi Talib in the time of Umar - or the time of Uthman - and he stayed with his sister Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. When he finished his umrah he returned, water for ghusl was poured for him, so he performed ghusl. When he finished his ghusl, a group of the people of Iraq came in to him and said: O Abu Hasan, we came to ask you about a matter we wish you inform us of. He said: I think al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah narrates to you that he was the last of the people to be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Yes; about that we came to ask you. He said: The last of the people to be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Qutham ibn al-Abbas."
"532","Abdillah ibn Habib al-Sulami Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi al-Muqri, from Ali, peace be upon him: 566 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali informed us in Baghdad that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa al-Simmari informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi told us, Ibrahim ibn Khadhm told us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd told us: he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi told us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf prepared food for us, invited us and gave us wine to drink. The wine took hold of us, prayer came, so they put me forward and I recited: Say: O disbelievers; I do not worship what you worship - and we worship what you worship. He said: So Allah Mighty and Majestic revealed: O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say."
"533","567 - And Abu Hafs Umar ibn al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Fadl known as Ibn al-Mu'awwaj informed us, with my reading to him in the western side of Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Hafiz told us, al-Qasim ibn Ja'far al-Hashimi told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar told us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib told us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - that a man of the Ansar invited him and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and gave them to drink before wine was forbidden. So Ali led them in Maghrib and recited: Say: O disbelievers, and mixed in it. So revealed: Do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it. And al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Abd ibn Humayd, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Amr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, similarly."
"534","568 - And Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi informed us in Cairo that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them, it being read to him - he said: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i told us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali: he said: It was he, Abd al-Rahman and another man; Abd al-Rahman prayed with them and recited: Say: O disbelievers, and mixed in it. So revealed: Do not approach prayer while intoxicated. Thus came in this narration that the one praying was Abd al-Rahman."
"535","Another (narration): 569 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: he said: Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: Whoever lies about his two eyes will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection with tying between the two ends of a barley grain. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Hujayn, from Isra'il, from Abd al-A'la, and from Affan, from Abu Awanah."
"536","570 - And with it (the same chain) Abdillah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isma'il narrated to me, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali: he said - I think he raised it - he said: Whoever lies in his dream will be burdened with tying a barley grain on the Day of Resurrection. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri and Abdillah ibn al-Walid, from Sufyan. And Abd ibn Humayd narrated it, from Abu Nu'aym, from Isra'il. And likewise Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from Abu Nu'aym; and with him Sufyan said: I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Qutaybah, from Abu Awanah, and from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, from Sufyan, from Abd al-A'la."
"537","Another (narration): 571 - Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la - he is al-Tha'labi - from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about: And you make your provision that you deny: He said: Your gratitude - you say: We were rained by such-and-such star and by such-and-such star. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Ahmad ibn Mani', and said: a hasan gharib hadith. And Sufyan narrated it, from Abd al-A'la, without raising it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Isra'il and Aban ibn Taghlib narrated it, from Abd al-A'la, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and al-Thawri differed from them, narrating it from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, mawquf; and the disagreement seems to be from Abd al-A'la."
"538","Another (narration): 572 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that his father informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad told us, Abdillah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah told us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him: he said: When you hear a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), think of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is most fitting, most guiding and most godfearing. He said: And he came out to us when the caller called for Subh prayer, and said: Where is the asker about witr prayer? This is a good time for witr. Sulayman al-A'mash narrated it, from Amr ibn Murrah."
"539","573 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami: he said: Ali said: When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), think of him what is most fitting, most guiding and most godfearing. And Mis'ar narrated it, from Amr."
"540","574 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib told us, Abdillah ibn Ja'far told us, from Abdillah ibn Ahmad, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mis'ar, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali: he said: When you are narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), think of him what is most fitting, most guiding and most godfearing. Imam Ahmad narrated it also, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah, and in it the mention of witr; and from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Shu'bah similarly, without mentioning witr. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Bundar, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Shu'bah, without mentioning witr. Abu al-Bakhtari: his name is Sa'id ibn Fayruz. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned that a group narrated it without mentioning Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: And what is correct is whoever mentioned Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"541","Another (narration): 575 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb told us, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan narrated to us, Asbat narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, his saying about: And give them of the wealth of Allah which He gave you. He said: A quarter of the mukatab (contract sum)."
"542","576 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Shukr al-Tamimi informed us in Isfahan that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dhakwani told us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz told us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us: he said: Ibn Jurayj told us: he said: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed me that Abdillah ibn Habib informed him, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said about: And give them of the wealth of Allah which He gave you. He said: A quarter of the kitabah (contract sum)."
"543","577 - And with it (the same chain) Abu Bakr ibn Mardawayh told us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Susi told us, Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, that Abdillah ibn Habib informed him, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about the saying of Allah: And give them of the wealth of Allah which He gave you. He said: A quarter of the kitabah. Ibn Jurayj said: And more than one told me that he used to narrate this hadith without mentioning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Abd al-Razzaq, Hisham ibn Sulayman, Hajjaj and Abu Qatadah raised it, from Ibn Jurayj, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Rawh stopped it from Ibn Jurayj. And likewise Zuhayr, Hushaym, Ibn Ullayyah, Jarir, Asbat ibn Muhammad, al-Muharibi, Hammad ibn Salamah and Bakr ibn Khunays narrated it, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, mawquf. And likewise Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi narrated it, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, mawquf; and it is what is correct. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Abd al-Razzaq, then said: And more than one told me, from Ibn Jurayj, that Ata ibn al-Sa'ib would not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it. And he narrated it from Jarir, from Ata, from Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"544","Another (narration): 578 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib: he said: I prayed Fajr, then came to Abu Abd al-Rahman and found him sitting in his prayer place. I said: If you stood to your bed it would be more comfortable for you. He said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant sits in his prayer place, the angels pray for him; and their prayer for him is: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"545","579 - And with it (the same chain) Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us: he said: I heard Ata ibn al-Sa'ib say: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman say: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant sits waiting for prayer, the angels pray for him; and their prayer for him is: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Yahya ibn Adam and Husayn ibn Muhammad, both from Isra'il. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"546","Another (narration): 580 - Abu al-Qasim Ziki ibn al-Wathiq ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Bayhaqi al-Khayyat informed us in Marw that al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Shahhami informed them, it being read to him: Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Himmi told us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Muzakki told us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muhammadabadi told us, Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali: he said: We were commanded with siwak. And he said: When a servant stands praying, an angel comes to him and stands behind him listening to the Qur'an, drawing near; he keeps listening and drawing near until he places his mouth upon his mouth; he does not recite a verse except that it is in the angel's interior."
"547","581 - Abu al-Faraj Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us that his grandfather Hafiz Isma'il ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: Abu al-Husayn al-Dhakwani told us, Abu [...] al-Istarabadhi al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Saydalani narrated to us, Hamdun al-Jazzar narrated to us, Abbas ibn al-Walid [...] narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - that he used to command siwak, saying: When a man stands in prayer [...] except that it falls in the angel's mouth. He said: I said: Is it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"548","Another (narration): 582 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join fasts to sahar (pre-dawn). Abd ibn Humayd narrated it in his Musnad, from Abu Nu'aym, from Isra'il."
"549","Abdillah ibn Hunayn al-Hashimi, their freedman, from Ali, peace be upon him: 583 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad that Abu Abdillah al-Husayn [...] informed them, it being read to him while he listened: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur told us: he said: [...] al-Qasim ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah dictated, Abu Bakr Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Faqih narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us: he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me, from Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir, from Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right, turning its stone to what faces the inside of his palm. Sharik said: Abu Salamah narrated to me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear the ring on his right."
"550","584 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, as I see that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him while he was present: Abu Bakr ibn Abdillah ibn Shadhan told us - by ijazah: Abu Bakr Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab told us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim told us, Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Sharik ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Namir, from Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ibn Wahb. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the book al-Shama'il, from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it, from Qutaybah, all from Ibn Wahb. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."
"551","Abu al-Khalil, Abdillah ibn al-Khalil - and it is said ibn Abi al-Khalil - from Ali, peace be upon him: 585 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdillah al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, it being read to him: Abu al-Qasim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna told us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali: he said: I saw a man seeking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists. I said: You seek forgiveness for your parents while they are polytheists? He said: Did not Ibrahim seek forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist? He said: So I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and revealed: It is not for the Prophet and those who believed to seek forgiveness for the polytheists - to the end of the two verses. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Yahya ibn Adam, from Sufyan similarly. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Waki', and said: a hasan hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan."
"552","Another (narration): 586 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Khalil, from Ali: he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah had a spear; when we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he would plant it, people would pass by it and carry it off. I said to him: If I come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I shall inform him. He said: If you do, no lost item will be raised. Abu al-Khalil - Salamah ibn Kuhayl and Abu Ishaq narrated from him. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Abu Ahmad. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Samurah, from Waki', from Sufyan."
"553","Another (narration): 587 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad told us, Ali ibn Ahmad told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated to us, al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Isra'il told us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdillah ibn Abi al-Khalil, from Ali: he said: I heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said takbir in prayer say: There is no god but You; glory be to You; I wronged myself, so forgive my sins; none forgives sins but You."
"554","Abdillah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi al-Misri, from Ali, peace be upon him: 588 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan told us, Ahmad told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abdillah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi: he said: I heard Ali say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold in his right and silk in his left, then raised his hands with them and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah. Thus in our hearing; Abu Aflah was not mentioned."
"555","589 - And al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Zuhayr ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq told us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abdillah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah."
"556","590 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid told us, it being read to him: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa told us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri told us, Muhammad ibn Zayyan ibn Habib ibn Zayyan al-Misri told us, Muhammad ibn Rumh told us: he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd told us, from Yazid - he is ibn Abi Habib - from Abu al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah, from Abdillah, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold and placed it in his right, took silk and placed it in his left, then said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah."
"557","591 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb told us, Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abdillah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, I heard him say: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took silk in his left and gold in his right, then raised his hands with them and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah, lawful for its females. Abu Dawud narrated it, and al-Nasa'i, both from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from al-Layth. And al-Nasa'i narrated it also, from Muhammad ibn Hatim, from Hibban, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Layth, from Yazid, from Ibn Abi al-Sa'bah; and from Amr ibn Ali, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abd al-Rahim. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it, from al-Husayn ibn Abi Ma'shar, from Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Humayd ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abdillah ibn Zurayr, without mentioning Abu Aflah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Al-Layth ibn Sa'd, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far and Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Ibn Zurayr, from Ali, and he mentioned in it other than this saying. He said: And what is correct from Ibn Ishaq is the saying of Yazid ibn Harun and Jarir from him, due to the following of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far and al-Layth of them both."
"558","Another (narration): 592 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan told us, Ahmad told us, Abdillah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abdillah al-Yazani, from Abdillah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to ride a donkey named Ufayr. Salamah ibn al-Fadl - some declared him trustworthy, some criticised him; but this hadith has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Amr ibn Maymun, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal: he said: I was behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a donkey called Ufayr."
"559","Another (narration): 593 - Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid informed us in Isfahan that his grandfather Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them, Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abdillah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: A mule was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he rode it. So Ali said: If we bred donkeys upon horses we would have the like of this. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only those who do not know do that. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Hashim, from al-Layth. And Ibn Hibban narrated it, from Abu Khalifah, from Abu al-Walid, from Layth. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib similarly."
"560","Abdillah ibn Sabu', from Ali, peace be upon him: 594 - Abu Muslim Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim told us, Muhammad told us, Ahmad told us, Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abdillah ibn Sabu': he said: It was said to Ali: Will you not appoint a successor? He said: No; rather I leave you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you to."
"561","595 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Abu Ya'la told us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abdillah ibn Sabu': he said: Ali addressed us and said: By Him who split the grain and created the soul, this shall be dyed from this - meaning his beard from the blood of his head. He said: A man said: By Allah, none does that except that we extirpate his kin. He said: I adjure by Allah - or: I beseech by Allah - that none be killed for me except my killer. A man said: Will you not appoint a successor, O Commander of the Believers? He said: No; rather I leave you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you. He said: Then what will you say to Allah - Majestic His mention - when you meet Him? He said: I will say: O Allah, You left me among them as long as it seemed to You, then You took me and left You among them; if You will, You set them right, and if You will, You corrupt them. Thus Abdillah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi and Muhadir narrated it, from al-A'mash, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement in it: that some did not mention Salamah ibn Kuhayl, and that Jarir, Abdillah ibn Dawud and Muhadir mentioned him. He said: And what is correct is the saying of Abdillah and whoever followed him. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Waki' in full, from al-A'mash, from Salim."
"562","Abdillah ibn Salamah al-Muradi al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him: 596 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubaydillah al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that his father Abu Mansur informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah - meaning al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah: he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Salamah say: I entered upon Ali - peace be upon him - and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would relieve himself, eat meat with us, recite the Qur'an; and nothing would veil him - or: bar him - from reciting the Qur'an except janabah."
"563","597 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur told us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri told us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili told us, Ubaydullah - he is ibn Umar - narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah: he said: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, I and two men of Banu Asad - I think - and he sent us forth, saying: You two are stout, so strive for your religion. Then he entered the privy, relieved himself, came out, took a handful of water and wiped with it, then began reciting the Qur'an. He said: It is as though he saw that we disapproved of that, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would relieve himself, come out, recite the Qur'an, eat meat with us; and nothing would veil him from the Qur'an except janabah."
"564","598 - And with it (the same chain) Abu Ya'la told us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far - meaning Ghundar - narrated to us, Shu'bah told us, from Amr ibn Murrah: he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Salamah say: I entered upon Ali, I and two men - a man of us and a man of Banu Asad - and he sent them both forth, saying: You two are stout, so strive for your religion. Then he entered the privy, took a handful of water and wiped with it, then came reciting the Qur'an; he saw that we disapproved of that. Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to the privy and relieve himself, come out, eat bread and meat with us, recite the Qur'an; and nothing would veil him - sometimes he said: bar him - from the Qur'an except janabah - or: janabah."
"565","599 - Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Su'ud al-Busiri informed us in Egypt that Murshid ibn Yahya al-Madini informed them, it being read to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Naysaburi told us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Zakariyya al-Qattan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr told us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim told us, from Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah: he said: I came to Ali, I and two men, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out of the privy, recite the Qur'an, eat meat with us; and nothing would veil him from the Qur'an except janabah."
"566","600 - And with it (the same chain) al-Nasa'i told us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Saydalani informed me, Isa narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali - peace be upon him: he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite the Qur'an in every state except janabah. Thus al-Nasa'i transmitted it in his book. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Waki' and others, from Shu'bah. And Abu Dawud narrated it, from Hafs ibn Umar, from Shu'bah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Uqbah ibn Khalid, from al-A'mash, and Ibn Abi Layla, from Amr ibn Murrah similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Bundar, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah, from Hamid ibn Yahya, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Shu'bah and Mis'ar. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, saying: And the saying is the saying of whoever said: from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali."
"567","Another (narration): 601 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, it being read to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Ali told us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali: he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was ill, saying: O Allah, if my term has come, relieve me; if it is delayed, raise me; if it is a trial, make me patient. So he struck my chest with his hand and said: O Allah, grant him health and heal him; and I never complained of that pain after. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, Affan, Waki' and Ghundar, from Shu'bah. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Shu'bah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Khalid, from Shu'bah. And Ibn Hibban narrated it, from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Bundar, from Yahya and Muhammad, from Shu'bah. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said, after mentioning the disagreement in it: And what is correct is the saying of whoever said: from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali."
"568","Another (narration): 602 - Abu Abdillah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: Shall I not teach you words - when you say them Allah forgives you, though you are already forgiven? There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Noble; there is no god but Allah, the High, the Mighty; glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the noble Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Abu Ahmad."
"569","603 - Qadi Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Samad ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed us, with my reading to him in Damascus - I said to him: Tahir ibn Sahl ibn Bishr al-Isfarayini informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Uthman al-Azdi al-Misri told us, it was said to him: Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Khurshid told you, saying: Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi told us, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Shurayh ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdillah ibn Salamah, from Ali: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, shall I not teach you words - when you say them, though sins as numerous as ants are upon you, you are forgiven - though you are already forgiven? Say: There is no god but Allah, the High, the Mighty; there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Noble; glory be to Allah, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in his book Deeds of Day and Night from Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim in agreement, and from Harun ibn Abdillah, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, from Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Aban, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Ali ibn Salih."
"570","Another (narration): 604 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us that his father Abu Mansur Ali informed them, it being read to him: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah told us, from Amr ibn Murrah: he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Salamah say: A man asked Ali - peace be upon him - about His saying: And complete Hajj and Umrah for Allah. He said: Enter ihram from the environs of your family."
"571","Abdillah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Ali, peace be upon him: 605 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man told us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri told us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' al-Khuza'i told us, Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Salim ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Khaytham told us, from Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Amr al-Qari that he said: Abdillah ibn Shaddad came and entered upon A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, while we were with her sitting, on his return from Iraq on the nights Ali ibn Abi Talib was killed. She said to him: O Abdillah ibn Shaddad, will you tell me truthfully what I ask you of? Tell me about those whom Ali killed. He said: Why should I not tell you truthfully? She said: Then narrate to me their story. He said: When Ali corresponded with Mu'awiyah and the two arbiters arbitrated, eight thousand of the reciters of the people went out against him and settled a land called Harura on the side of Kufah. They blamed him, saying: You stripped off a shirt Allah - Mighty and Majestic - clothed you with, and a name Allah the Exalted named you with; then you arbitrated in the religion of Allah the Exalted - there is no judgment but Allah's. When there reached Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - what they blamed him for and parted from him in, he commanded a caller to call: None shall enter upon the Commander of the Believers except a man who has carried the Qur'an. When the house filled with the reciters of the people, he called for a mushaf - a great imam - placed it before him, began striking it with his hand, saying: O mushaf, speak to the people! The people called to him: O Commander of the Believers, what do you want with the mushaf? It is but ink on paper; we speak of what it narrated and argue by what is in it. What do you want? He said: These people went out against obedience, parted the community, declared their imams disbelievers; is there anyone with them to speak of what Allah sent down for them? So people stood to him and said: We are all knowledgeable of tafsir; argue with us. Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - said: A servant of Allah will meet you - they hoped it a man of the people, for he had not entered with Ibn Abbas - so Ibn Abbas came and entered upon them, saying: Peace be upon you. They said: And upon you peace, O Ibn Abbas; what brought you while you have abandoned us? He said: I came from the Commander of the Believers and a people of the Muhajirun and Ansar, so I may tell you what they say and tell them what you say. They argued with him a while, then said: What do you blame upon the Commander of the Believers? He said: What do you blame upon him? They said: We blame three things upon him. They blamed him that he arbitrated men in the religion of Allah, though Allah says: Judgment is only Allah's; what is this, O Ibn Abbas? He said: By Allah, this is Muhammad - to him was revealed: If you judge between them, judge with justice; and: Allah and His Messenger shall judge. Would you go back from this? They said: Allahumma na'am (O Allah, yes). And they blamed him that he fought yet did not take captives nor spoils; if those he fought were disbelievers, their captives were lawful for us and their spoils lawful; and if they were believers, fighting them was not lawful for us. Would you go back from this? They said: Allahumma na'am. And they blamed him that he erased his name from Commander of the Believers; if he is not Commander of the Believers, he is Commander of the Disbelievers. Would you go back from this, O Ibn Abbas? He said: Do you know that on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, when Suhayl ibn Amr came to us while we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made treaty with Quraysh; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. Suhayl said: Do not write: In the name of Allah, the Merciful, the Compassionate. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then how shall we write? He said: Write: In Your name, O Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. Suhayl said: If I knew you are the Messenger of Allah, I would not oppose you. So he wrote: Muhammad ibn Abdillah. And Allah - Mighty and Majestic - says in His Book: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example. So Ali ibn Abi Talib sent Ibn Abbas to them, and I went out with him; we walked until we were in the midst of their camp. Ibn al-Kawwa stood and addressed the people, saying: O bearers of the Qur'an, this is Abdillah ibn Abbas; whoever did not know him, I shall make him known from the Book of Allah - Mighty and Majestic: this is of what was revealed about him and his people: Nay, they are a contentious people. Return him to his companion, and do not give him the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: Their preachers stood and said: By Allah, we shall surely give him the Book of Allah - Mighty and Majestic: if he comes with a truth we know, we shall follow him; if he comes with falsehood, we shall refute him with his falsehood and return him to his companion. So they gave Abdillah the Book for three days. Four thousand of them returned, all repentant - among them Ibn al-Kawwa - until he brought them in to Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - in Kufah. So Ali sent to the rest, saying: There was of our affair and the people's affair what you have seen; so stand where you wish until the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathers and you enter with them where you wish. Between us and you is that you shed no forbidden blood, cut no road, nor wrong a covenant; if you do that, we have cast to you: Upon equality; Allah does not love the treacherous. A'ishah said: So he killed them. He said: By Allah, he did not kill them until they cut the road, shed blood and violated Kufah. She said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, was it so? He said: By Allah besides whom there is no god, it was so. She said: What is something that reached me the people of Iraq narrate, saying: Dhu al-Thudayyah? He said: I saw him and stood over him with Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - among the slain. He called the people and said: Do you know this? How many came saying: I saw him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so praying, and I saw him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so praying; and they brought about him no established identification except that. She said: Then what was Ali's saying when he stood over him as the people of Iraq claim? He said: I heard him say: Allah and His Messenger spoke truth. She said: Did you hear from him that he said other than that? He said: O Allah, no. She said: Yes; Allah and His Messenger spoke truth. May Allah have mercy on Ali; it was of his speech that he would see nothing pleasing him except that he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke truth. So the people of Iraq go and lie upon him and add upon him in hadith. Imam Ahmad narrated it in full, from Ishaq ibn Isa al-Tabba', from Yahya ibn Sulaym, from Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym."
"572","Another (narration): 606 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, with my reading to him there - I said to him: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed you, it being read to him while you listened: Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Isma'il told us, Qadi Abu Sa'id al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi narrated to us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj told us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdillah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: he said: Stoning is two stonings: stoning by confession, and stoning by evidence. What of it is by confession, the first to stone is the imam, then the people; and what of it is by evidence, the first to stone is the evidence (witnesses), then the imam, then the people. And wind is two winds: mercy and blessing; and wind of punishment and vengeance. And jealousy - two jealousies: a good, beautiful jealousy by which a man sets right his family, and a jealousy that admits him to the Fire, carrying him to killing so he kills."
"573","Abdillah ibn Abbas, from Ali, peace be upon him: 607 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Abdillah al-Sufi informed us, it being read to him while we listened, in Baghdad - it was said to him: Your father Abu Mansur Ali informed you, Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini told us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah told us, Abdillah - he is ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah told us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar - may Allah be pleased with him - was brought an insane woman who had committed zina while pregnant, and he wanted to stone her. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Has it not reached you that the pen has been lifted from three: from the insane until he recovers, from the child until he understands, and from the sleeper until he wakes. Abu Zibyan: his name is Husayn ibn Jundub."
"574","608 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, it being read to him: Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri told us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah told us, my grandfather told us, Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la al-Sadafi and Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us - both said: Ibn Wahb told us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed me, from Sulayman ibn Mihran, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas: he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by an insane woman who had committed zina, while Umar had commanded her stoning. So Ali returned her and said to Umar: O Commander of the Believers, do you stone this? He said: Yes. He said: Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen is lifted from three: from the insane, overpowered in his mind, until he understands; from the sleeper until he wakes; and from the child until he dreams (matures)? He said: You spoke truth. So he left her. Abu Dawud narrated it, and al-Nasa'i, from Abu al-Tahir Yunus ibn Ubayd."
"575","Another (narration): 609 - Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali told us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far told us, Abdillah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Ubaydullah al-Khawlani, from Ibn Abbas: he said: Ali entered my house and called for ablution water, so we brought a cup holding a mudd or near it, until placed before him. He said: O Ibn Abbas, shall I not perform for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes indeed, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: A vessel was placed for him; he washed his hands, rinsed, sniffed and blew, then took with his hands and struck his face with them, placing his thumbs on what faces of his ears. He said: Then he called for the like of that three times. Then he took a handful of water with his right hand and poured it on his forelock, letting it flow upon his face. Then he washed his right hand to the elbow three times, then his other hand likewise. Then he wiped his head and his ears from their backs. Then he took with his palms water and struck his feet with them while sandals were on them, then rubbed them with them, then upon the other leg likewise. He said: I said: And in the sandals? He said: And in the sandals. I said: And in the sandals? He said: And in the sandals. I said: And in the sandals? He said: And in the sandals. Abu Dawud narrated it with its meaning, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad, from Yahya ibn Wadih al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"576","Another (narration): 610 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us, it being read to him in Isfahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdillah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, it being read to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah told us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad told us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas - may Allah be pleased with him - from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him: he said: I married Fatimah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you build (prepare a dwelling for me with her)? He said: Do you have something to give her? I said: No. He said: Where is your Hutamiyyah armour? I said: With me. He said: Give it to her. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr ibn Mansur, from Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik al-Tayalisi."
"577","Another (narration): 611 - Imam Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal told us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq told us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Ahmad ibn Mani' told us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali, about His saying: Be not like those who harmed Musa, so Allah cleared him of what they said. He said: Musa and Harun - peace be upon them both - ascended the mountain; Harun died. So Banu Isra'il said: You killed him; he was more beloved to us than you, and gentler to us than you. So they harmed him with that. Allah commanded the angels, they carried him until they passed over Banu Isra'il; the angels spoke of his death until Banu Isra'il knew he had died. They went with him and buried him; none of Allah's creation saw his grave except the vultures, so Allah made them deaf, dumb."
"578","Another (narration): 612 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there that Fatimah bint Abdillah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, it being read to her: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah told us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - used to say in the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah - Mighty and Majestic - says: If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels? By Allah, we shall not turn back on our heels after Allah guided us. By Allah, if he dies or is killed, I shall surely fight upon what he fought upon until I die. By Allah, I am his brother, his wali, his cousin and his heir; who is more entitled to him than me?"
"579","Abdillah al-Ma'afiri, from Ali, peace be upon him: 613 - Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Asadi informed us in Damascus that his grandfather Abu al-Qasim al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad informed them, it being read to him: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Missisi told us, I said to him: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn al-Qasim ibn Ma'ruf ibn Abi Nasr informed you, it being read to him: Abu al-Hasan Khaythamah ibn Sulayman ibn Haydarah al-Atrabulsi narrated to us, Hilal ibn al-Ala al-Raqqi narrated to us, my father and Abdillah - he is ibn Ja'far - narrated to us - both said: Ubaydullah - he is ibn Amr - narrated to us, from Zayd - he is ibn Abi Unaysah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdillah al-Ma'afiri, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold in one hand and silk in the other, and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah. Abdillah added: Lawful for its females."
"580","Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Hind al-Jamali, from Ali, peace be upon him: 614 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili told us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i told us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb told us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Warraq narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, from Awf, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Hind al-Jamali al-Basri, from Ali: he said: Whenever I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he gave me; and when I was silent he initiated me. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Khallad ibn Aslam, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Awf al-A'rabi, and said: a hasan gharib hadith from this aspect."
"581","Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from Ali, peace be upon him. 615 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Aban ibn Sa'id ibn al-As al-Umawi narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: Ali said to us: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to recite as you were taught."
"582","616 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed you, reading to him while you listened: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Muhammad Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us - he came to us from Kufa - Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh. 617 - Abdullah said: And Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, my father narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh who said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: We disputed about a surah of the Qur'an, saying thirty-five verses, thirty-six verses. He said: So we went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found Ali conversing privately with him. We said: We have differed about the recitation, and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned red. Then Ali said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to recite as you were taught."
"583","Abdullah ibn Nafi' from Ali, peace be upon him. 618 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Nafi' who said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari visited al-Hasan ibn Ali, and Ali said to him: Have you come visiting the sick or as a visitor? Abu Musa said: Rather I have come visiting the sick. Ali said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever visits a sick person in the morning, seventy thousand - meaning angels - accompany him, all of them seeking forgiveness for him until evening, and he shall have a harvest in Paradise; and if he visits him in the evening, seventy thousand angels accompany him, all seeking forgiveness for him until morning, and he shall have a harvest in Paradise. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Shu'bah, and said: Mansur narrated it from al-Hakam as Shu'bah narrated it."
"584","Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), scribe of Ali, from Ali, peace be upon him. 619 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there, that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, from Zayd ibn Ali, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at Arafah and said: This is the standing place, and all of Arafah is a standing place. Then he took Usamah behind him and began to move swiftly on his she-camel, while the people were striking camels right and left, not turning to them, saying: Calmness, O people. He set out when the sun had set, came to Jam' and prayed there the two prayers - meaning Maghrib and Isha - then spent the night there. When morning came he stopped at Quzah and said: This is Quzah, it is the standing place, and all of Jam' is a standing place. He said: Then he went on, and when he came to Muhassir he spurred her, and she trotted until she crossed the valley, then he restrained her, and took al-Fadl behind him, then went on until he came to the Jamarah and stoned it, then came to the slaughter place and said: This is the slaughter place, and all of Mina is a slaughter place. Then a young woman from Khath'am came and said: My father is an old man, enfeebled, and the obligation of Allah in Hajj has reached him; will it suffice if I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes, perform on behalf of your father. He said: And he twisted the neck of al-Fadl. Al-Abbas said to him: O Messenger of Allah, why did you twist the neck of your cousin? He said: I saw a young man and a young woman, and I feared Satan for them. He said: And a man came to him and said: I hastened before shaving. He said: Then shave - or: shorten - and there is no harm. He said: And he came to Zamzam and said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, your watering, were it not that the people would overpower you over it I would have drawn. Abu Dawud narrated from it up to the mention of Quzah, from Ahmad ibn Hanbal. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar, from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, from Sufyan in full, and said: A hasan sahih hadith, we know it from the hadith of Ali only through this channel. Ibn Majah narrated part of it from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Yahya ibn Adam. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned the disagreement in it, and said: The word is the word of al-Thawri and whoever followed him, and Allah knows best, meaning this narration."
"585","Another. 620 - Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us in Baghdad, that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed him, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khuza'i informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb informed us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khalid of the people of Madinah narrated to us - Abdullah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices a group passing by people that one of them greets, and it suffices on behalf of those sitting that one of them replies. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali. Sa'id ibn Khalid was declared weak by Abu Zur'ah and Abu Hatim al-Raziyan. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned it, then said: The hadith is not established; Sa'id ibn Khalid al-Madani is alone in it from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl. And Sa'id ibn Khalid is not strong."
"586","Ubaydullah ibn Khalifah al-Hamdani Abu al-Gharif, and it is said al-Muradi al-Kufi, from Ali, peace be upon him. 621 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, A'idh ibn Habib narrated to us, saying: Amir ibn al-Simt narrated to me, from Abu al-Gharif who said: Ali - may Allah have mercy on him - was brought ablution water, so he rinsed his mouth and nose three times, then washed his face three times, washed his hands and forearms three times, then wiped his head and washed his feet, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution, then recite something of the Qur'an, then say: This is for one who is not junub; as for the junub, then not, not even a verse."
"587","622 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed you: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah informed us, my father narrated to me, A'idh ibn Habib narrated to us, Amir ibn al-Simt narrated to me - and in our hearing it is al-Sibt, and the correct is with mim, and Allah knows best - from Abu al-Gharif who said: Ali was brought ablution water, so he rinsed mouth and nose three times, washed his face three times, washed his hands and forearms three times each, then wiped his head, then washed his feet, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution, then he recited something of the Qur'an, then said: This is for one who is not junub; as for the junub, then not, not even a verse. Abu al-Gharif - Abu Hatim al-Razi said: They spoke about him, and he mentioned nothing besides that."
"588","Abidah ibn Amr al-Salmani from Ali, peace be upon him. 623 - Abu al-Futuh Mas'ud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Ghayth al-Daqqaq informed us in Baghdad, that Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, reading to him: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Naqur informed us, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Harun informed us, Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, Abu Abdah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar al-Hamdani narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Hafari Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Jibril - peace be upon him - descended to him and said: Give them - meaning his Companions - choice regarding the captives of Badr: killing or ransom, on condition that an equal number of them will be killed next year. They said: Ransom, and some of us will be killed. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Ubaydah Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Hamdani and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, and said: A hasan gharib hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Ibn Abi Za'idah. Abu Usamah narrated something like it from Hisham. al-Nasa'i narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan and Muhammad ibn Rafi', from Abu Dawud. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Hajib ibn Musa, from Abu Dawud. I said: Ibn Awn has narrated it from Ibn Sirin."
"589","624 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Mu'addib informed us in Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Marwan al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the captives of Badr: If you wish you kill them, and if you wish you ransom them and benefit from the sacrificial animals, and a number equal to them will be martyred from you. He said: And the last of the seventy was Thabit ibn Qays, killed on the day of Yamamah. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and mentioned these two narrations with its chain, saying: And Ibn Awn narrated it from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah, mursal, and the mursal is more likely correct, and Allah knows best."
"590","Another. 625 - Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abidah, from Ali who said: No man divorces with the Sunnah divorce and ever regrets."
"591","Those named Abd al-Rahman. Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhunan from Ali, peace be upon him. 626 - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Aquli informed us in Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed them, reading to him: Abu Ja'far ibn al-Muslimah informed us, Isa ibn Ali ibn al-Jarrah informed us, Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhunan, from Ali - peace be upon him - that he used to recite: And their plot was not to remove the mountains thereby."
"592","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi from Ali, peace be upon him. 627 - Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan - I said to him: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed you, reading to him while you listened: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Hisham ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Ali: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I cannot enumerate praise upon You, You are as You have praised Yourself."
"593","628 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us with its chain, the like of it exactly."
"594","629 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there, that Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz and Abu Kamil narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us - Bahz said: Hisham ibn Amr al-Fazari narrated to us - from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 630 - Imam Ahmad said: Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at the end of his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I cannot enumerate praise upon You, You are as You have praised Yourself."
"595","631 - And with it he said: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Amr al-Fazari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hisham, from Ali that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it exactly. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musa ibn Isma'il, from Hammad ibn Salamah, and said: Hisham is the oldest shaykh of Hammad. al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani', and said: A hasan gharib hadith, we know it only through this channel from the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah. Hisham was declared trustworthy by Imam Ahmad and Abu Hatim al-Razi. It is narrated from Yahya ibn Ma'in that he said: None narrated from him except Hammad ibn Salamah. al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: He narrated from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Ali, and it is a mistake. And he said: Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hisham ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Ali, and it is the correct. I said: Abdullah ibn Ahmad has narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, from Hammad upon what is correct. Perhaps some narrator from Ibrahim erred in it. And Allah knows best."
"596","Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh al-Azdi from Ali, peace be upon him. 632 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abdullah ibn al-Banna' informed them, reading to him: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Hababah informed us, Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath informed us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Wadin ibn Ata' narrated to us, from Mahfuz ibn Alqamah al-Hadrami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh al-Azdi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The eye is the strap of the anus, so whoever sleeps, let him perform ablution. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ali ibn Bahr, from Baqiyyah. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Baqiyyah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Baqiyyah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ibn Musaffa."
"597","Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Hanafi Abu Salih, from Ali, peace be upon him. 633 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Ubaydullah - he is al-Qawariri - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abi Awn, from Abi Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the day of Badr, and to Abu Bakr: With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il, and Israfil, peace be upon them, a mighty angel, witnessing the fighting, or being in the fighting. Sharik also raised it."
"598","634 - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa' al-Aquli informed us, reading to him while we listened, in Baghdad - it was said to him: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed you: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us, saying: It was read to chief Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn al-Jarrah - while I listened - saying: It was read to Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abi Awn, from Abi Salih, from Ali - peace be upon him - who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the day of Badr: Mika'il is with you, and to Abu Bakr: Jibril is with you. Or he said to me: Jibril is with you, and to Abu Bakr: Mika'il is with you, and Israfil is a mighty angel on the side of the rank, witnessing the fighting."
"599","635 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abi Awn al-Thaqafi, from Abi Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: It was said to Abu Bakr and to me on that day: With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il, and Israfil is a mighty angel, witnessing the fighting, or lining in the rank."
"600","636 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us in Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed them, reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abi Awn, from Abi Salih al-Hanafi, from Ali who said: It was said to Ali and to Abu Bakr on the day of Badr: With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il, and Israfil is a mighty angel witnessing the fighting, or he said: witnessing the rank. Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, like the narration of al-Qawariri. And Abu Awn: his name is Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi."
